Outgoing Lao Ambassador Praises Royal Government of Cambodia's 19 Camidivid Campaign to Reopen
In this afternoon meeting, the Ambassador of Laos informed about the purpose of the mission in Ratanakkiri province is to congratulate and wish Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun on the occasion of his new assignment as Provincial Governor and to say goodbye on the occasion. He will end his term in Cambodia in the near future.
The Lao Ambassador also requested the understanding of the Governor, who took the opportunity to take a break to pay a courtesy call on the occasion. The Laotian ambassador said that in the past, despite the Kovid-19 crisis, relations between Laos and Cambodia, especially the border provinces, have remained cooperative and good relations with each other as neighbors. The good side.
In addition, the Lao Ambassador stated that Ratanakkiri has a close history with Laos, with some former leaders participating in the revolution in Laos in the past, at the same time all diplomatic missions at all levels to Ratanakkiri. Always received a warm welcome from the Ratanakkiri provincial leadership.
At the same time, the Lao Ambassador expressed his appreciation to the Cambodian government for its good management of the Kovid-19 issue and for vaccinating the people in all doses and for re-opening the country in all fields. Share to Laos. The Ambassador of Laos also informed about the purpose of strengthening the Cambodia-Laos Association by bordering provinces as members.
In response, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun expressed his gratitude to the Ambassador of Laos for taking the time to wish and say goodbye on this occasion. He said that the Kovid-19 issue has made relations between the two countries difficult, and this tradition has existed from the beginning between leaders at all levels to promote closer ties with the best of emotions.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun said that although the ambassador had ended his term, traditional relations between Ratanakkiri and the border provinces of Laos continued to function normally. At the same time, he always welcomed the invitation to come to Ratanakkiri after the end of the mandate in any form. In response to the strengthening of the Cambodia-Laos Association, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun expressed his support for this initiative to promote better cooperation and relations.
Once again, the Lao Ambassador expressed his gratitude and expressed confidence that Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun's leadership will change the face of the province during his tenure, depending on the leadership and the natural climate in the northeastern province.
