World Tourism Organization helps to promote the exemption of vaccines for vaccinated travelers to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The World Tourism Organization (UNWTO) has helped publicize the exemption of vaccinations for all vaccinated travelers arriving in Cambodia, while the Ministry of Tourism has also expressed confidence that international tourists will visit. Cambodia is growing through the help of the World Tourism Organization.
According to the World Tourism Organization, from November 15, 2021, all fully vaccinated passengers arriving in Cambodia through all international ports (land, air, and waterways) will no longer be required to travel. .
To receive this exemption, these vaccinated passengers must provide:
1: Complete vaccination certificate.
2: Certificate or certificate of negative PCR test result for 72 hours.
The above certificate or certificate must be issued and recognized by the competent authority of the country of origin. Upon arrival at the international port, passengers must take a quick test and wait for the results for 15 to 20 minutes. If the result is negative, passengers can travel all over Cambodia.
Passengers who have not been vaccinated should be screened for 14 days after a quick test at an international port. At the same time, those who are currently doing cataracts in Cambodia are allowed to complete cataracts from November 15, 2021 onwards, if they are not tested positive for Kovid 19.
