Angkor Wat Hall Bridge is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2021
(Siem Reap): The team of the Department of Preservation of Temples in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology is completing the remaining work on the site of repairing the bridge over the Angkor Wat temple and the plan is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2021.
On Sopheap, an archaeologist and chairman of the Angkor Wat Bridge Bridge Repair Team, said that by mid-November, the Angkor Wat Bridge Bridge repair project was almost 100 percent complete. He added that work on the upper part of the bridge floor is 99 percent complete, while the lower part of the laterite wall is about 80 percent completed and may be completed by the end of 2021.
Rehabilitation work on the northern port will continue, with the project likely to take another year to complete.
It should be noted that the project to repair the Angkor Wat north bridge, the second phase, with a total length of 94 meters, started in 2016, which is a cooperation project between APSARA Authority and Sofia University, Japan.
