International Analysis: Misconceptions Behind Biden and Xi Jinping Summit
China, US join hands to resolve domestic issues
Beijing and Washington have been prioritizing tackling domestic issues, especially the COVID-19 outbreak, which could be one of the reasons for the face-to-face meeting between Biden and Xi Jinping. Delay in the past.
* Success under the heat of stress
The most important outcome of the summit between Biden and Xi Jinping was the success in easing tensions between the two countries. Both Biden and Xi Jinping stressed the importance of maintaining good relations, responsibility to the world, open and honest dialogue.
Such a White House statement could be interpreted by China as a US opposition to Taiwan's claim to independence. According to Xinhua, Biden also assured Xi Jinping that the United States will not try to change China's political system and will not seek to strengthen anti-China alliances, nor will it seek to provoke a conflict with China. No, China.
Biden's assurances appear to have eased Chinese concerns after former US officials under Donald Trump's administration spoke openly about the destruction of China's political system and the Chinese Communist Party. This can be said to be a new strategy that the United States does not want to change China, but wants to control relations and consider its core interests or values.
The video summit between Biden and Xi Jinping may pave the way for diplomatic work to address some of the concerns of both sides, but not all. Here, an important question is how the United States and China can steer their relationship, as the two powers have different economic systems and different perspectives on the international order.
