In order to reflect the changes in the use and improvement of methods for measuring poverty, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided:
* (1): Edit the questionnaire for the Cambodia Socio-Economic Survey 2019-2020 to get better information on consumption, using a detailed list and recording the consumption and price of each item.
* (2): Make adjustments as an approach in line with international practice. This revised approach focuses on two main points: (a) creating a new total utility cost that incorporates the estimated cost of use of durable materials, the estimated cost of rent, and (b) the implementation of the cost method. On basic needs and common baskets to define poverty lines.
