Tourism practitioners hope to be able to revive their businesses after allowing tourists to enter Cambodia without a license (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Experts and business people in the tourism sector hope that The decision to waive travel licenses for travelers to Cambodia will encourage more tourists to visit, which will help restore their business, which has suffered for nearly two years, to a successful operation.
The president of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents, Chhay Sivlin, told Fresh News that not requiring tourists to visit Cambodia was a positive sign for a speedy recovery of tourism as planned. Tourists ahead of other countries in the region, which is a beacon for tourism businesses to quickly recover their business.
She explained, "If we decide to end the stalemate, then the guests know, but the Cambodian option as the first choice in the tour, we can recover soon. In general, we can grab the guests first, because this kind of satire does not like any guests.
However, she is concerned about the shortage of flights due to the immediate announcement that some airlines have not yet launched and do not yet have a wide range of flights for guests.
At the same time, Mr. Huot Kheang, Deputy General Director of Aldream Cambodia Tourism Company, said that the decision of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia is a good decision that will help the economic recovery, especially the tourism sector that suffered greatly. He said that this decision gives those in the field the strength to stand up again.
He expects that after Cambodia opens the country and does not require visitors to do Chatalisak, there will be more tourists, which makes his company's business recovery plan can be reduced from two years to six months. Currently, there are also bookings for tours from some guests.
He emphasized that his company was ready to receive tourists again, "If there is a direct flight to our country, we can allow guests to stay between one week to 11 days due to the potential of tourism in our country everywhere. "Everything is already developed, we are diverse in both nature and culture."
Ms. Khay Chenda, Vice President of the Hotel Association, said that the hotel sector needs some more time to prepare for the reception, but some hotels are also ready to receive tourists. She claims that the number of hotels already prepared will be able to meet the number of visitors to Cambodia now and in the future.
(Central): A youth rehabilitation center built to transfer offenders under the age of 18 from prison to receive education and training at this center has been completed.
Illegal minors will be transferred from prison to the Youth Rehabilitation Center in early December.
This was stated by Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Fitness on the occasion of his visit, the Governor of Kandal Province, and other relevant officials to inspect the Youth Rehabilitation Center to prepare for the inauguration ceremony at the end of 2021. The Youth Rehabilitation Center is located in Bakou Commune, Kandal Steung District, Kandal Province.
Phea Vannak, director of the Youth Rehabilitation Center, said that in the first phase of the trial, about 50 offenders under the age of 18 would be transferred from Kandal Provincial Prison to this location.
He said that for the whole district can accommodate up to more than 1,000 people, the center will start accepting offenders aged 14 to under 18 years in other prisons in the next phase.
The director of the center added that the transfer to the center will provide some vocational education and training for them to have the right life skills after completing their sentences.
For the stay at the location of the Youth Rehabilitation Center, there is a definite period of limitation, with the juvenile violating the law to stay only 24 years. If the person is over 24 years old and the sentence is upheld, the person will be sent back to prison. Polish authorities use water cannons and tear gas to block refugees at Belarus border
Warsaw: Polish police fired water cannons and tear gas at a group of refugees trying to cross the border into Belarus, sparking a dispute between the two European countries. Even more stressful. This is according to the release by CGTN on Wednesday, November 17, 2021.
Meanwhile, about 4,000 refugees are gathering on the Belarusian border. According to the Polish Ministry of Defense, the refugees threw stones and tried to break down the barrier to cross into Polish territory, forcing the Polish authorities to spray water and tear gas to suppress it.
Up to 15,000 Polish troops have been deployed along the border with Belarus. In response to the Polish action, the Belarusian Foreign Ministry issued a statement condemning it as a direct provocation and an inhumane act against the refugees.
