(Battambang): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, assigned a representative to distribute humanitarian aid to 642 flood-affected and most vulnerable families from 73 villages in 13 communes in Koas Kralor and Maung Russey districts, Battambang province.
The handover ceremony was held on November 17, 2021 in the presence of Mrs. Hourn Chanbora, Director of the Department of Communications of the Cambodian Red Cross, Mr. Sok Lou, Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and members of the Committee. Branches, Sub-branches and Executives of the Cambodian Red Cross Volunteer Youth Branch.
For these 642 families, in Koas Kralor district, there are 312 families from 20 villages in 5 communes and 330 families in Moung Russey village, 73 villages in Leuk commune, 8 communes of Battambang province.
Mrs. Hourn Chanbora and Mr. Sok Lou brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all the people in Battambang with nostalgic, compassionate, loving and sharing. Difficult and deeply saddened with the people affected by the floods, which are natural disasters caused by climate change.
Mrs. Hourn Chanbora brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all of you:
First, please consider and take care of good health and hygiene, because health is the main factor for all of us, so every family should drink boiled water to prevent diarrhea or other diseases. Which wastes time and money on treatment.
Second, when the water recedes before returning to your home, clean the house or the environment around the house clean and hygienic and try to continue to produce to restore the family economy.
Thirdly, please cooperate with the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health in accordance with the slogan "Together, take responsibility to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19 virus" by following the measures "3 prevent and 3 do not" and 2 Participate with vigilance and live by New trajectory.
"We can all forget Kovid 19, but Kovid 19 never forgets us. As long as we forget ourselves or are a little careless, we can lose our lives because it is an inanimate enemy," she added. "All citizens participate in implementing the measures of the government and the Ministry of Health by wearing the correct mask, washing their hands often and keeping a distance of at least 1.5 meters."
