The body of Venerable Srey Ly, the chief abbot of Wat Po in Battambang city, has been cremated in his hometown, Kampong Chhnang province, while the items are to be kept for 7 nights and 7 days at Wat Po in
(Battambang): After passing away due to a disease at 3:52 pm on November 16, 2021 at the Russian Hospital, the body of Preah Akka Chou To Srey Ly, Preah Vinay Thor, Battambang Municipality and Chief Inspector of Wat Po in Battambang city was cremated by his family and relatives in his hometown in Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province on the night of November 16, 2021.
After the cremation, the relics of Akka Chhator Srey Ly were taken to the next ceremony in Wat Po in Battambang city, Battambang province for 7 nights and 7 days to pay homage and to pay homage to Grandpa. For the last time from the Buddhist family who always respect and love Grandpa Srey Ly.
The 7-night, 7-day festival is organized by the leadership of the Department of Cult and Religion of Battambang Province, Anukun, Battambang City and the monks of Wat Po Knong Committee. In particular, if nothing changes, there will be a procession of the relics of Atto To Srey Ly in Battambang.
Preah Akka Chota Srey Ly is respected by many people, both at home and abroad, and is considered a patriarch, a pious monk for his children and devotees, especially he has raised intellectuals, monks and students. There are so many, countless, and the people living under the shadow of the old man are all cold, so they are very sad, but can not forbid death.
7 things to know that make you know Akka Chota Srey Ly:
* First: End the Pali language at an old age * Second: Love the monks who study and practice good discipline Take care of the environment in the pagoda, keep the pagoda clean * 5th: Manage the monks in the pagoda by Brahma Vihear * There is a high or low rain as a monk or a monk.
