Cambodia Continues to Send 73 Blue Hat Troops to UN Humanitarian Mission in South Sudan
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of November 16, 2021, Cambodia continued to send the Royal Thai Armed Forces Squadron No. 739, the 10th Brigade with a total force of 73 (34 women) to carry out humanitarian missions under the United Nations umbrella. A total of 73 troops from the Republic of South Sudan, who replaced the 186th Squadron of the Royal Gendarmerie, returned home to Cambodia on November 16.
The farewell ceremony for the 739th Royal Gendarmerie Squadron was presided over by General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Center for Peacekeeping Forces Management, Mine and War Remnants, as well as some Blue Hat Army leaders at the VIP Airport.
On that occasion, General Sem Sovanny conveyed greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. And Chairman of the National Committee for a Safe Return with Success in Assignment.
From 2006 to the present, the Kingdom of Cambodia has sent 7,899 Blue Hat troops to the United Nations peacekeeping mission, including 528 women. Currently, the Blue Hat Force is carrying out 787 UN missions, including 111 women.
