Cambodia needs an additional $ 225 million to achieve its goal of mine-free by 2025 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, stated that in order for Cambodia to achieve its goal Without a landmine in 2025, Cambodia needs an additional $ 225 million and urges development partners as well as member states to be able to assist Cambodia to continue its journey together to achieve its 2025 vision.
The meeting will last for four days from November 15 to 19, 2021, with the participation of 164 member states, states and organizations around the world.
In that statement, Senior Minister Ly Thuch spoke about the joint efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the humanitarian support from friendly countries, donors, development partners, mine operators and other stakeholders, including:
"Achieving nearly 30 years since the humanitarian demining work began in Cambodia in 1992, Cambodia has cleared 2,287 square kilometers of landmines and unexploded ordnance. For agricultural production, housing construction, physical infrastructure development and saving lives.
Cambodia has more than 774 square kilometers of minefields and is stepping up efforts to reduce minefields through non-technical research and land use assessments, which is an important approach to demining. Demining mines and revising resource mobilization strategies in line with donor perspectives.
