As of November 14, Cambodia has vaccinated more than 14 million Cambodians and foreigners living and working in Cambodia from the age of five, equivalent to nearly 88% of the total population of 16 million.
The presence of the 19 smallpox vaccine has become an important element in helping Cambodia achieve vaccination for its people faster than planned. Achieving this rapid Kovid 19 vaccination plan has enabled Cambodia to overcome the Kovid 19 pandemic and to re-establish social and economic activities in all areas as it is today.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always reminded the Chinese government and people of their contribution to the supply of the vaccine. For Samdech Techo, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the provision of vaccines by the Chinese government and people is a great advantage for saving the lives of people from the plague of Kovid 19.
