Spokesperson: Prison is a place where people are imprisoned to carry out their sentences and to educate and transform prisoners into good citizens, not a comfortable place with delicious food like outside.
(Phnom Penh): Spokesman of the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Nuth Savana, said on November 16, 2021 that prisons are places for detaining people to carry out sentences and educate prisoners to become good citizens, not Comfortable place with delicious food like outside.
The statement from the spokesman of the General Department of Prisons was made in a statement that completely denied and dismissed the distortions of former detainees as political activists, human rights activists, social and environmental activists who had just been released by the court. Prison.
A spokesman for the General Department of Prisons stated: "The minimum basic rights of all inmates are respected and guaranteed. However, the prison authorities also recognize that prisons are places of detention to carry out criminal offenses and a place to educate inmates to transform themselves into good citizens, not a place to live comfortably, have good food and have access to food. "The provision of health services is better than in the community."
