Senior Minister Meas Sophea: All religions in Cambodia came into being after the liberation on January 7, 1979
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Meas Sophea, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Preah Vihear Province, stated that all religions in Cambodia came into being after the liberation on January 7, 1979 under Lead the liberation of the Cambodian People's Party.
He said this during a ceremony to give alms at Wat Preah Puth Meanchey, also known as Pal Hal Pagoda, in Pal Hal Village, Pal Hal Sangkat, Preah Vihear City, Preah Vihear Province, on the morning of November 16, 2021.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea said that during the three years, eight months and 20 days of the Khmer Rouge's rule, they shut down all freedoms, including money, no markets, no schools, and pagodas. As a general repository, there is nothing. But after the day of liberation on January 7, when the Cambodian People's Party led the liberation of the country, everything was revived as the second birthday of the Cambodian people, including the resurrection of religion.
The Senior Minister said that under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, the Cambodian society has achieved complete peace, economic growth and development in all areas, including Buddhism. And Buddhism and the realm today go hand in hand.
The senior minister said that the alms-giving ceremony held today was in the context of Kovid-19 disease, which made it impossible for the Buddhists to celebrate as before, as if the original ceremony was not completed in full, only the devotional offerings were completed. On the other hand, the level of participation has also decreased.
