Court charges two Canadians with smuggling more than 167 kilograms of drugs into Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A Canadian man who smuggled more than 167 kilograms of drugs into Cambodia with a firearm was charged with two offenses: illegal possession and transportation of drugs and possession of drugs. Weapons without permission under Article 40 of the Law on Drug Control and Article 490 of the Penal Code. This is according to Mr. Plang Sophal, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The Canadian named FU YONG QING, male, was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of November 16, 2021. He was arrested by the Anti-Drug Crimes Department on November 15, 2021, after conducting a crackdown and search operation from October 27 to November 10, 2021.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) . The opening of the meeting was videotaped with keynote speeches by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Mrs. Heidi Ottala, Vice President of the European Parliament, and Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
In a keynote address at today's important meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the global challenges posed by the Kovid 19 epidemic crisis and the threat to world security and peace due to unilateral politics. Popularity and geopolitical competition from the superpowers, as well as speeches at previous international meetings.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia told the leaders of the Asia-Europe Parliament that global peace and security are under pressure and more difficult to predict due to the rise of geopolitical competition. Samdech Techo continued that geopolitical lines are already being drawn and put pressure on small states to choose a political agenda that does not reflect the will and interests of their nation.
Responding to this concern, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that only a trustworthy partnership can lead the world to maintain a multilateral mechanism that ensures peace, stability, progress and prosperity. The world.
"In this context of tense geopolitical competition, only a trusting partnership can enable us to maintain a multilateral mechanism that will ensure peace," he said. "Stability, progress and prosperity of the world."
"In this spirit, we all need to continue to maintain the values of peace and to continue to explore the necessary mechanisms to achieve this lofty goal."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also saw that multilateral mechanisms remain key to addressing global challenges as well as concerns over the destruction of world peace and security.
In today's keynote address, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed Cambodia's commitment to respond to these global issues as well. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is committed to adhering to the principles of mutual respect, mutual learning, mutual understanding, trust and mutual benefit to build a necessary foundation for implementation. Multilateral foreign policy.
It should be noted that in recent years, the rivalry between the powers of the superpowers, especially between China and the United States, as well as the allies, has created many problems, such as trade wars and the escalation of arms and armaments activities. To go to war and so on.
This has caused great concern for the region and the world from the outbreak of crises as well as the possibility of flames of war.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always sent a message expressing concern over the escalation of the crisis, a negative response for this world, and always called on all countries in the world to work together to solve the problem to bring about a better state of partnership. And world cooperation.
The Reception Ceremony for the 186th Royal Gendarmerie Squadron was held in the presence of General Sem Sovanny, Deputy Chairman of the National Committee and Director General of the National Center for the Management of Peacekeeping Forces, Demining and Remnants of War, as well as some Blue Hat Army leaders at VIP Airport.
The General also wished all the Cambodian Blue Hat troops who completed their mission abroad who were doing the Talat Sak good luck forever.
In this meeting, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum said that we, as representatives of the electorate and 60% of the world's population, have an obligation to jointly consider and make recommendations based on the principle of open cooperation. Openly respect each other for the common benefit of Asia-Europe and the world.
In this context, Samdech would like to share some views as follows:
First, with regard to resolving confrontations and tensions of trade, geography, politics and armed conflict, I urge all parties to promote peaceful dialogue based on respect for international law, sovereignty and independence. And non-interference in internal affairs to find a win-win solution, national unity and global unity (Global Unity)
"Indeed, peace in a country, a region, as well as the world as a whole is the most necessary prerequisite for development. A peaceful area is a place of development. "Peace must go hand in hand with development." This is an additional confirmation from the President of the National Assembly.
Therefore, the parliament must continue to promote a culture of dialogue and the value of peace to address these issues. "Parliamentary diplomacy" includes conflict prevention diplomacy as a key mechanism for resolving these issues. In addition, in order for peace to be lasting, we need to promote common prosperity, social justice, good governance, human rights and the values of democracy.
Dispute closes road in Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham provincial governor resolves the dispute and reopens the road
(Kampong Cham): The long-running dispute over the closure of a public road in Prek Changran village, Lve commune, Koh Sotin district has been successfully resolved under the intervention of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of the Dispute Resolution Commission. Provincial land.
This work took place on the afternoon of November 15, 2021, after this problem happened a long time ago.
The provincial governor requested that both parties reach an understanding to reach a complete end to the dispute, and the provincial authorities will work together to open this road for the benefit of both parties, as well as the entire village can travel through the transport of agricultural products. Connect to some other road to their plantation.
At the same time, the parties to the dispute also agreed to mediate with the provincial governor, and the provincial governor also assigned local authorities and experts to visit the site to actually inspect and make an agreement on November 16. To open a road at least 3 meters wide for a public road for all people to use.
At the same time, the provincial governor instructed the parties to the conflict, who are related to each other, to know how to love each other and live in the same village and fence together forever. Svay Rieng Governor Encourages Private Sector to Invest More in Their Province
(Svay Rieng): After the Royal Government announced the reopening of the country, the Governor of Svay Rieng Province, Mr. Men Vibol, announced his support for the private sector, both inside and outside the province, to invest more in Svay Rieng Province, while the provincial administration has encouraged High for investors, especially in the real estate sector.
This announcement was made on the occasion of Mr. Men Vibol inaugurating the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Sovanmacha Business House in Thmor Sor Village, Svay Chrum Commune, Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province on November 15, 2021.
"While the country is peaceful and developed in all areas, it is an opportunity for all investors to invest in Svay Rieng, and Svay Rieng also has many favorable land locations for investors," he said. .
Governor Men Vibol has always encouraged and cooperated in providing confidence in development, and he was optimistic that all private sector investment would really contribute to the government's poverty reduction policy to some extent, such as providing affordable housing. Decent land, decent housing, especially provided employment to the people.
Svay Rieng provincial officials confirmed that through the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Ministry of Economy and Finance are working together to develop policies to encourage the private sector to invest in low-cost and medium-cost housing. Great consideration for the lives of the people by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Royal Government has allowed the establishment of a series of special economic zones, which is why the economy in Svay Rieng province is growing rapidly, resulting in rapid population growth, both new income and migration. The rate decreases significantly.
