The road was demolished by a sand and rock transport company, despite some landslides and rubble. Villagers reported that a company representative, in order to transport land to fill a pond in a nearby area, wrote a letter to the village chief, promising that if the sand transport on the road was damaged, they would be rehabilitated, but the company did not do much. As promised, despite the pouring of sand and some rubble on the road.
