Aung San Suu Kyi accused by Myanmar military of rigging 2020 elections
Rangoon: The Myanmar military has just indicted former Myanmar leader Aung San Suu Kyi on charges of rigging the 2020 election. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, November 16, 2021.
Since being overthrown by a military coup in February 2021, Suu Kyi, who remains in custody, has been charged with a number of charges, including illegal possession of a radio communication device and incitement to commit a crime. Rebellion, corruption, and if convicted, she could face up to decades in prison.
Suu Kyi's NLD party saw a sharp increase in support in the 2020 election compared to the 2015 election. However, the Myanmar military claimed that the election results were rigged and decided to stage a coup to seize power from Suu Kyi's government. Myanmar's military chief Min Aung Leng has promised new elections in the coming years.
