In terms of Chinese society, democracy is not entirely foreign. Originally, China's long history and culture also trained and nurtured simple democratic ideas. Since its inception, the Chinese Communist Party has consistently embraced the outstanding achievements of its country and world political civilization, and has adhered to making the people its hosts.
Is a country democratic or not? The people of their country have the most freedom of expression. According to the latest referendum results released by the US Census Bureau, the Chinese people's preference for the ruling party and government of China is 95 percent and 98 percent, respectively. Each. This is the Chinese people's best answer to their democratic rights.
