Village Road No. 1A, Sangkat Svay Rolum is a road used by hundreds of local people and has never been badly damaged, although the road has been occasionally flooded by rain.
Local people gather to pour soil and gravel as much as possible to make the road used to serve the people's livelihood every day without clogging time. But Road No. 1, about 1,000 meters long, after the land grab by the HSK sand truck business, crossed the road several weeks ago, the livelihood and travel of civil servants living in the streets. That road was very difficult.
The road was demolished by a sand and rock transport company, despite some landslides and rubble. Villagers reported that a company representative to transport land to fill a pond in a nearby area had written a letter to the village chief, promising that if the sand transport on the road was damaged, they would be rehabilitated, but the company did little to comply. That promise, despite the pouring of sand and some rubble on the road.
Villagers who gathered on Sunday, November 14, 2021, could not stand the irresponsible act, told Fresh News that they had contacted the local administration several times to help resolve the issue. People lose their jobs, cannot go to work on time, or lose money every day to repair vehicles due to the company's lack of responsibility.
Dozens of villagers told the Fresh News Agency in Kandal province, citing the hardships of travel as the road was almost completely destroyed this rainy month, causing damage to the road. Debris can not travel easily.
Residents have urged authorities to ban the sand transport company from suspending operations while the road was smashed by giant sand trucks. The company will continue to do its business.
Residents have asked the company not to use heavy trucks to haul heavy sand and rocks on the road without a solid foundation, otherwise the road will only be used for the benefit of the company. Only one side.
Meanwhile, Mr. Moeng Youleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province, told Fresh News Agency on November 15, 2021 that he would look into this case and ask people to submit a letter of intervention. Come to the department so that he will summon the car team and other stakeholders for questioning and to order the road to be rebuilt for the people. However, the sand company has not been able to contact yet.
