On November 17, another 2 million doses of Chinese aid vaccine will arrive in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will receive in person
An additional 2 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine, funded by the Chinese government and people, will arrive in Cambodia on November 17, 2021.
According to a senior official of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, will personally receive the vaccine with the assistance of the Chinese government and people at the Phnom Penh International Airport.
China has become the leading supplier of 19 Kovid vaccines to Cambodia. China was also the first country to provide vaccine assistance to Cambodia. China has also become a country that Cambodia has chosen as a strategic reference for the supply of 19 Kovid vaccines.
As of October 14, 2021, the vaccines that Cambodia received from China, both aid and orders, totaled 32.8 million doses. The vaccines that the Chinese government provided to Cambodia totaled 6,800,000 doses. At the same time, Chinese company Sinowak provided 500,000 doses.
