Details of the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, on Monday afternoon, November 15, 2021, had a special video conference.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, emphasized that at the beginning of the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure to meet with Chinese Prime Minister Li Keqiang and send greetings to Mr. Xi. Chinese President Jin Ping also.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked his Chinese friends for their warm hospitality to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni and His Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk during their visit to China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen celebrates the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China in July 2021. Samdech Techo praised the Chinese government and people for completely eradicating poverty in Chinese society. He also hailed China's 9.8 percent economic growth in the first nine months of 2021 and believed that under Xi Jinping's leadership and the participation of Chinese leaders, China would grow stronger.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth also said that in this special meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ly Ker Chheang discussed bilateral relations and cooperation between the two countries and also discussed regional and international cooperation. .
For the bilateral framework, Samdech Techo and the Prime Minister focused on the economy, trade, agriculture and people-to-people relations. In connection with these issues, Samdech Techo and Mr. Li Keqiang agreed to boost trade between the two countries to 10 billion dollars per year and also agreed to enter into force a free trade agreement between Both countries in January 2022.
In the field of agriculture, Li Keqiang urged the two sides to work together to discuss rice and agricultural import quotas directly to China through the establishment of a joint mechanism to review the products to be exported from China. Cambodia to China should take place directly between the two countries.
In this meeting, Mr. Li Keqiang promised to continue to help Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19 by providing vaccines to help prevent Kovid 19. In the future, the government and the people will continue to provide vaccines to 19 Kovid doctors and other medical equipment to Cambodia, Li Keqiang said.
Li Keqiang also confirmed that China will continue to provide scholarships to 500 Cambodian students for the 2022-2023 academic year for an additional five years. The government is also looking to allow Cambodian students to return to China to study directly in the near future.
For regional and international cooperation, the Chinese Prime Minister confirmed that China will attend the Asia-Europe Meeting hosted by Cambodia and China will also provide assistance to Cambodia during its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022. Banteay Meanchey provincial health director tells Cambodian workers returning from Thailand who have been fully vaccinated against Kovid 19 do not need to be vaccinated, but need to be tested quickly
