The Ministry of Labor announces the procedure for Cambodian trainees to work in Japan in accordance with the new border measures of the Japanese government
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notification on the procedure for Cambodian trainees to work in Japan in accordance with the new border measures of the Japanese government. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received on the night of November 15, 2021.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has confirmed that the public, private recruitment agencies and interns - skilled workers who are preparing to go on internship and work in Japan all know that the Government of Japan has decided to allow foreigners, including interns. Cambodian skilled workers will re-enter Japan from November 8, 2021, following the following procedures:
First, cooperate with the receiving company or association in Japan to apply for a permit for interns - skilled workers entering Japan issued by the Ministry or competent agency of Japan. Second, you need to attach a permit for the interns to enter Japan when applying for a visa for the interns at the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia.
