MANILA (Reuters) - Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte on Monday nominated a candidate for the Senate election in the May 2022 general election. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday, November 15, 2021.
Duterte, now 76, will run for senator under the PDDS, another political party, not his ruling PDP-Laban party. Rodrigo Duterte was elected President of the Philippines in 2016, and his term ends on June 30, 2022, in accordance with the Philippine Constitution, which stipulates that a president can serve only one term, but for six years. .
Last October, Duterte announced that he would retire from politics after his term expired and would not run for office next year. His daughter, Rosa Duterte, has just run for vice president.
