It is the first time India has allowed foreign tourists to enter the country on general commercial flights since March 2020, when the South Asian country implemented one of its strictest sanctions. Try to control the epidemic of COVID-19. Last month, India began accepting vaccinated foreign tourists on special flights.
According to the Indian Ministry of Health, foreign tourists entering India must be fully vaccinated with COVID-19 (2 doses) and adhere to preventive measures and be tested negative for the disease within 72 hours. Flight.
They will also be tested at the airport upon arrival in India, except for those from countries that have vaccination agreements with India, such as the United States, the United Kingdom and many other European countries. They can leave the airport without being tested.
