Administrative Regulation Explains the Examination and Investigation of Crimes in the Civil Service Sector
(Phnom Penh): In order to share knowledge to the public, the Public Administration Regulator has prepared an article explaining the examination and investigation of crimes in the public sector.
Within the framework of operations related to the examination and investigation of offenses under the Law on Public Administration, the Inspector General of Public Administration has the authority to search, seize evidence, summon relevant persons, and perform other procedures in accordance with Provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
In cases where it is necessary to detain a suspect, the Inspector General of Public Administration must obtain the prior permission of the prosecutor, albeit orally.
All operations of the Inspector General of Public Administration in the examination, investigation of crimes and the arrest of suspects must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
The Inspector General of Public Administration has the right to request assistance from the sub-national administration and the armed units or other relevant competent authorities to participate in the suppression of the offenses set forth in the Law on Public Administration.
