BEIJING, Nov. 11 (Xinhua) - The Declaration of the Sixth Plenary Session of the 19th CPC Central Committee, released on November 11, uses the words "Adherence to the 10 Sectors" to address the issue. Which foreign dignitaries have always studied, studied and been interested in.
What is the successful password of the Chinese Communist Party? Among these passwords, "adherence to the focus on the whole of humanity" is not only an important experience of the Chinese Communist Party, but also reflects the worldview of the Chinese Communist Party.
Since its inception, the Chinese Communist Party has also had a long-term aspiration, which is not to dominate the world, but to contribute to the world. From the five principles of peaceful coexistence that adhere to the inclusion of the path of peaceful development in the Constitution and the Party's statutes, to the establishment of a common community for the common destiny of mankind. Etc.
Over the past 100 years, the struggle of the Communist Party of China has proved that "the Communist Party of China is a party seeking happiness for the people, a party striving for the cause of human progress." Since the founding of the People's Republic of China, China has never initiated all wars and conflicts, and has never invaded other countries' territories.
China has so far sent more than 50,000 peacekeepers to nearly 30 UN peacekeeping missions, the largest member of the UN Security Council. Also. In the field of promoting common development, the Chinese Communist Party has also demonstrated the responsibility of the world's largest ruling party.
The Communist Party of China (CPC) has led the Chinese people in building a prosperous society in all aspects and has historically eradicated extreme poverty. China's contribution to global poverty reduction has exceeded 70%. And China's contribution to global economic growth has been the highest in the world for 15 consecutive years.
Going through a hundred years of development and anticipating the future, all the work that can benefit the whole of humanity, the Chinese Communist Party will consider it as its inevitable duty and will do better! General knowledge: Which ocean is the hottest and which is the coldest?
The second coldest ocean on earth is the South Ocean, which surrounds the Antarctic ice sheet of the South Pole. The ocean has an average temperature between 2 degrees Celsius and 10 degrees Celsius. Some geologists have suggested that the Southern Ocean does not deserve the status of another ocean, but some international scientific organizations and countries, including the United States, have recognized the ocean.
The Atlantic Ocean covers nearly 20 percent of the earth's surface. The ocean has some very cool climates, such as near the poles, while near the equator it has a tropical climate. The average temperature of the Atlantic Ocean is between 2 ° C and 30 ° C. 4: Pacific Ocean
Because much of it is tropical, the Indian Ocean is the hottest ocean on earth. The ocean has an average temperature of 20 to 30 degrees Celsius, and it is not as cold as the Pacific Ocean and the Atlantic Ocean.
