Rainy season rice harvest in Ratanakkiri reached more than 70% as market prices were higher than last year
(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Soy Sona, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Ratanakkiri Province, said that the price of rice is higher than last year, while the rainy season rice harvest has reached more than 70%.
Mr. Soy Sona said this during the visit to understand the rainy season rice harvest of farmers in Moy village, Nhang commune, Andong Meas district on November 15, 2021.
Mr. Soy Sona said that throughout Ratanakkiri province, in the rainy season of 2021, the cultivation of rice and paddy fields of more than 30,000 hectares, of which more than 10,000 hectares of rice to date, more than 70% harvested. And the average yield is more than 2 tons per hectare.
According to the director of the Department of Agriculture, this year's rice yield is about 60,000 tons, which can supply enough markets in the province and reach exports. The price of rice is 1,100 to 1,200 riel per kilogram, compared to last year, the price has increased slightly.
Chan Jiayuan, a rice grower who cultivates 257 hectares of rice, described this year's rice harvest as a result of sufficient rainfall.
