In addition, the provincial administration has introduced the following two stages:
* Must thoroughly monitor and evaluate the readiness, fitness and performance of the business before deciding to allow any business to operate (by notifying the operator in advance for the operator to apply for a karaoke business (KTV). ) Entertainment Club, Bar - Disco Teak).
* Must thoroughly train business owners and employees on tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SOPs) in the new normal course for the karaoke (KTV) business, entertainment club, bar-disco.
* Second: Phase 2 (after the decision to reopen)
* Municipal and district administrations must set up mechanisms to continue to regularly and thoroughly monitor the implementation of tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SCP) along the new normal trajectory for karaoke (KTV) businesses, clubs, bars and discos. After deciding to re-enable
* In case the business owner does not properly follow the tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SOP) in the new normal course for karaoke business (KTV), entertainment club, bar-district, the city-district administration shall take additional measures as required. To close the business and be responsible before the law in force.
