Hundreds of Takeo Market Vendors Protest at Provincial Hall Against Takeo Market Construction Project
(Takeo): Hundreds of Takeo market traders on Monday morning, November 15, 2021, protested in front of Takeo Provincial Hall, asking Takeo Governor Ouch Phea to intervene to cancel the market investment project.
Takeo traders have asked the provincial governor to cancel the investment project to build a market, as this project will affect their business operations, and once it is built, vendors will be evacuated and their stalls may be lost.
According to Takeo market traders, they support the project to renovate the market to make it more beautiful and to restore the drainage system so that the market does not flood, but strongly oppose the construction of the market.
During the protest rally, Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, came out to meet the traders and listened to their requests. In the morning of the same day, the governor also issued an official letter confirming the decision to suspend the construction and repair of Takeo market.
In a letter from the provincial governor, Fresh News stated, "Based on the request of the vendors in Takeo market who have protested against the construction of additional stalls in Takeo market. The provincial administration will make a request to the Ministry of Economy and Finance to suspend the construction and renovation of Takeo market at the request of Takeo market traders.
The provincial governor confirmed that the provincial administration will report to the Ministry of Economy and Finance for the principle of canceling the construction of the market.
