BREAKING: The Ministry of Health issues an official press release confirming that there is no requirement for anyone who enters Cambodia at the time of full vaccination.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on November 14, 2021 issued an official press release confirming that there is no requirement for anyone (including foreigners) to enter Cambodia. This is not only for those who have already been fully vaccinated.
In a statement obtained by Fresh News, the Ministry of Health added that although there is no requirement for a vaccinator to be vaccinated, another obligation is to take a sample using a rapid test kit.
For those who have not been vaccinated, 14 days of immunization and PCR sampling are required, with no special conditions for those who have already been vaccinated.
The Ministry of Health issued the above press release following the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen via voice message, which was allowed to be released to the public on the evening of November 14, 2021.
The Ministry of Health added that passengers who have been fully vaccinated with Kovid-19 and are being vaccinated at Chatsali centers, hotels and homes across the country and who are not positive for Kovid-19 will be allowed to leave the country from the 15th. November 2021 onwards.
