The cost of pig production in Cambodia is discussed by ministries and institutions to understand in depth to enhance competitiveness
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has organized discussions with the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Ministry of Agriculture and independent analysts to analyze the cost of pig production in Cambodia, in order to gain an in-depth understanding of pig production and prices in Cambodia, especially the key factors. Affect costs and challenges aimed at enhancing Cambodia's competitiveness in pig production, farmers' living standards and economic excellence.
Secretary of State Sok Sopheak highlighted the general situation related to pig production in Cambodia compared to pig production in neighboring countries and the need for cooperation between relevant ministries, institutions and the private sector to propose measures to increase the competitiveness of pig production. In Cambodia.
The meeting also discussed the preliminary study of experts, emphasizing key factors such as analysis of production costs, raising costs of raising pigs, piglets, feed costs, transportation costs, as well as recommendations and policies to Solve challenges and to increase productivity in pig production.
He said that as a result, the meeting agreed to edit the study report by examining the possibility of adding additional information as well as recommendations and policies that are specific and appropriate for implementation before submitting to the Economic and Financial Policy Committee for review and decision in the future. Face. Interior Ministry spokesman: 55 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on 13 November
