The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the National Election Committee have previously set up a joint commission to provide visas to journalists as well as foreign media outlets to cover the North African election.
Libya is scheduled to hold general elections on December 24 as part of a roadmap approved by the United Nations-sponsored Forum on Libyan Political Dialogue (LPDF). The election was given internationally in the hope that it would help rebuild peace and unity in Libya after the fall of Muammar Gaddafi in 2011.
Twenty people were seriously injured when a truck carrying workers collided with a concrete truck in Bavet City
(Svay Rieng): At least 20 workers were seriously injured in a traffic accident between a Hyundai brand concrete mixer truck and a Sanyong truck carrying workers in the same direction. This incident happened on the evening of November 12, 2021 on National Road No. 1 between Lomet 153 in Prey Top village, Sangkat Prey Angkunh, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province.
According to Bavet City Police, one of the 20 injured workers, Khuon Nam, 32, lives in Lle Village, Kork Pring Commune, Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province.
The driver of the provocative concrete truck was not identified as he escaped, leaving only a white Hyundai concrete truck with license plate number 5A-0035 in Svay Rieng. The driver of the car carrying the workers was not identified because he fled immediately after the incident.
The police confirmed that the reason for the accident was due to the Hyundai brand concrete mixer truck driving at high speed and lack of caution. As for the exhibits of the two vehicles, the authorities measured and dragged them to be temporarily stored at the Bavet City Police Inspectorate to be sent to the provincial specialized office for legal action.
