ASEAN Transport Minister issues Joint Statement on the Outcome of the 27th Meeting
* Promoting digital change or revolution in ASEAN
* Strengthening ASEAN Single Aviation Market
The Meeting finalized the Protocol to Implement the Twelfth Package of Commitments on Air Transport Services under the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Services (AFAS), which will be signed by country to facilitate its implementation in Further liberalize aid services for air transport in ASEAN.
The Meeting noted the steady progress of the implementation of the ASEAN Air Traffic Control Master Plan, which aims to achieve the objectives of smooth air traffic management in the areas of safety, interoperability, harmonization, environment, capacity and efficiency, as well as promoting openness. Smooth open skies that will support the creation of a single ASEAN aviation market.
* Improving the land transport network and facilitating the transit of goods across ASEAN borders
The Meeting welcomed the full ratification and entry into force of the Second Protocol (Boundary Demarcation) of the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Transit Goods (AFAFGIT) from all ASEAN Member States and look forward to Full ratification of Protocol 6 (Border Stations and Rail Exchanges) to complete the ratification of all implementation protocols under the AFAFGIT Framework Agreement.
The meeting was pleased to note the implementation of the ASEAN Transit Customs System (ACTS), despite restrictions on cross-border transport due to Kovid-19, and called for greater coordination between transport officials and officials. Customs to work together in efforts to increase the use of the ASEAN ACTS transit system by the private sector. * Integration of sustainable transport plans and land use
The Meeting issued the Phnom Penh Declaration on Sustainable Urban Traffic, which aims to promote the establishment and implementation of SUMP and MTE models in ASEAN member countries to promote integrated transport integration. And land use plans in the ASEAN region.
Towards greater connectivity and integration of maritime transport
The meeting commended the completion of initiatives to review existing statistics, policies and programs related to maritime safety at the regional and national levels. The meeting recognized the importance of the presence of a strong maritime safety management system and emergency plans to reduce unforeseen maritime incidents.
* Transport cooperation with dialogue partners
Regarding the negotiation of an aviation service agreement (ASA) ongoing with dialogue partners (DPs) such as New Zealand, Japan and Korea, the meeting urged the relevant working groups to continue working towards a successful conclusion and obtaining a service agreement. An aviation (ASA) that provides mutual benefits and greater freedom in one aspect to strengthen air connectivity between ASEAN and dialogue partners.
With China, the Meeting welcomed the approval of the draft Action Plan 2021-2025 of the Update Strategic Plan for ASEAN-China Transport Cooperation and assigned the Senior Minister to strengthen coordination with China to implement the cooperation project. Set to be effective.
With Korea, the Meeting was pleased to note the progress of project implementation and activities under the ASEAN-Korea Transport Cooperation Roadmap 2021-2025, especially the implementation of some projects under the Human Resource Development Program. Technology and management in 2021.
* 28th ASEAN Transport Ministers' Meeting
The meeting agreed to hold the 28th ASEAN Transport Ministers' Meeting in Indonesia in 2022.
The meeting recognized the importance of the ASEAN-Korea Aviation Services Agreement (AK-ASA) and encouraged the senior officials and relevant working groups to continue working closely to complete the AK-ASA as soon as possible, including the exchange of traffic rights. Liberalize and have more mutual benefits to promote air connectivity between and outside ASEAN and Korea.
The meeting was pleased to note the progress of the project and maritime transport activities, including the following activities implemented in 2021:
The meeting looked forward to the implementation of maritime transport activities to be held in 2022, including a workshop on service and management of smart ships, the organization of the 2nd ASEAN Regional Forum (ARF) Training on Safety Capacity Building. Ferry copy and cooperation on e-ship certification.
