Minister of Water Resources inspects Trapeang Beong Reservoir dam in Chhouk district, Kampot province, which has a storage capacity of about 6 million cubic meters and can irrigate about 2,000 hectares of wet rice, dry rice and mixed crops.
(Kampot): On Saturday, November 13, 2021, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by Mr. Chan Vanna, Director of Kampot Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, inspected some pool conditions in Kampot Province. In fact, this morning, the Minister and his team inspected the Trapeang Boeung Reservoir Dam in Sat Pong Commune, Chhuk District, Kampot Province.
It should be noted that the Trapeang Beong Reservoir Irrigation System was rehabilitated by the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology in 2017 and continuously improved until now, with a storage capacity of about 6 million cubic meters, irrigated on rainfed rice. Dry and mixed crops about 2,000 hectares as well as water used in the daily life of the people in this area.
The location of Trapeang Beong Reservoir is geographically favorable, which helps to save water for use in Chhouk district, which is a water-scarce area, and now after the implementation of the project to dig the foot of the Crow Crow by labor from 2020 and in 2021 has been modernized. Which allows this irrigation system to be able to irrigate by turning the water into the field.
During the inspection, the Minister proposed to the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampot Province to study the construction of additional dams in the lowlands in order to maintain the amount of water in the basin to serve more. Cultivation of farmers and multi-purpose to facilitate the livelihood of the people in the area.
