During the visit to strengthen health capacity at Kampong Thom Provincial Referral Hospital, Ms. O Vandin expressed her deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for taking into account the well-being of the people and better management. There was a new marriage of the 19th Kovid era.
While the Royal Government of Cambodia has authorized this re-enactment, it has issued guidelines and standards (SOPs) to prevent and prevent the transmission of Kovid 19. After getting permission, it was observed that the people also started to organize weddings for their children gradually.
Seeing this, as a health officer, Ms. O Vandin repeatedly instructed and conveyed the message to the people who planned or organized this traditional ceremony to be organized in a new way of the 19th Kovid era, with Maintain security gaps and reduce at large gatherings at each event.
Ms. O Vandin cited practical examples such as setting the table for guests to eat, etc. In the past, there was one table for 10 or more guests, but now the number has been reduced to 5-6 or so. According to the actual situation, the food must be prepared according to the number of guests.
However, Ms. O Vandin also warned of the risks that may occur in case of individuals not cooperating or not following the guidelines issued by the Ministry of Health or the capital-provincial administration at the local level.
