During the meeting, the Secretary of State expressed a warm welcome to the presence of the Ambassador of Japan and representatives of Japanese companies who came to the Ministry of Economy and Finance to find out the policy to encourage investment in vehicle assembly projects.
The Secretary of State said that Cambodia and Japan have good relations on diplomacy, economy, trade, society and culture, which Cambodia has always considered Japan as an important development partner, and with this, the number of Japanese investors to Cambodia has increased steadily since. Small to large enterprises, with the establishment of many factories ranging from the food sector to vehicles.
