(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on the occasion of chairing the ASEAN Transport Ministers' Meeting, received attention from CNBC, a well-known American television station. The reporters of this TV station asked many questions related to the construction of infrastructure as well as the source of funds for the construction of infrastructure in Cambodia.
In an interview held on November 12, 2021, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted the introduction of electric vehicles (EVs), which are in the early stages of development in Cambodia. The senior minister emphasized that Cambodia has drafted a road transport policy to encourage Cambodians to use EVs.
The US Secretary of State also highlighted the joint venture between the Royal Government and the private sector on the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) principle to ensure adequate and secure charging station installation. That the disposal of the old battery was done correctly. The ministry is currently working with the Ministry of Economy and Finance to reduce the tax rate for electric vehicles by 50%.
In the interview, the Senior Minister also focused on discussions on foreign direct investment (FDI) and the growth of Cambodia's development, noting that the average FDI is generally around $ 3 billion a year in various projects.
The senior minister urged companies in the United States to consider participating in the bidding process to build infrastructure in Cambodia. The Minister noted that the bidding process complies with the procedures of the World Bank and JICA in accordance with international standards. The Senior Minister encouraged the private sector to participate in building quality infrastructure in Cambodia based on the principles of PPP and BOT.
Regarding investment policy, the Senior Minister reiterated that Cambodia is a small country with an open economy with a free investment regime in Asia. The Royal Government acts as a facilitator for the private sector, not a private sector manager. The success of the private sector is the success of the country.
