Japanese investment is considered a potential investment for Cambodia. In fact, as of the end of October 2021, Cambodia has welcomed and registered 146 qualified Japanese investment projects with a total investment capital of approximately 2,853 million US dollars.
To attract more Japanese investors, Cambodia has been promulgating a new investment law recently signed by the King of Cambodia.
Mr. Masahiro Mikami, Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, said that the new investment law will be an effective and timely strategy to restore the socio-economic situation after the Kovid-19 crisis and make Cambodia An attractive and highly competitive destination in the region for investment.
Mr. Masahiro Mikami also expressed his cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting and attracting direct investment from Japan to Cambodia towards the progress and economic prosperity of both countries.
In 2020, Cambodia exported more than 1 billion dollars to Japan, while imports from Japan to Cambodia amounted to more than 637 million dollars.
