(Kampot): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the ceremony to recognize the Honorary President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, Mao Thunin was replaced by Mr. Chiao Tai and transferred to Pursat province.
The recognition ceremony was held on the morning of November 12, 2021 at the Kampot Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Phuong Siphan, Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense. Leaders of the three armed forces, local authorities and more than 200 veterans.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim sent a message of greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all veterans, both of them. Forget or abandon the veterans, and Samdech always remembers the past when they were armed together, because Samdech is also a disabled person due to a war.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that in response to the invaluable merits of veterans in the cause of seeking peace for the motherland, Senior Minister Kun Kim instructed and requested the relevant authorities to increase Take care of the well-being and difficulties in the lives of the relatives of the veterans.
In particular, the Chief of Administration, Commune / Sangkat Chief, must assign one of his officials to hold the job of veterans and to clearly grasp the living conditions of the veterans to ensure that our brothers and sisters receive the attention and warmth of the Chief of Staff. Government. Because the sacrifice of fresh flesh and blood of veterans is invaluable to the Cambodian people in the cause of seeking peace for the motherland.
Meanwhile, Mr. Mao Thunin, Provincial Governor and Honorary President of Kampot Provincial Veterans Association, and Mr. Oknha Vinh Hour also donated 50,000 Riels to each of the 100 veterans on that occasion. .
