Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: ASEAN-Japan relations reach maturity in transportation
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia and Chairman of the ASEAN Transport Ministers' Meeting, said that in the field of transportation, ASEAN-Japan relations have reached a new level of maturity and understanding due to Mutual communication has improved significantly.
He added that stronger and broader relations between ASEAN and Japan are being established through institutional integration, which demonstrates progress on key transport cooperation initiatives.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also highlighted Japan's active role in efforts to build the ASEAN Community, an important trade and investment partner for ASEAN and a leading partner in promoting regional connectivity and providing rich resources. Much to support the implementation of the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025.
The senior minister added that over the years, various activities, programs and projects have been successfully implemented under the framework of the ASEAN-Japan Transport Partnership (AJTP), focusing on four key pillars: Transportation, transport infrastructure, sustainable and quality transportation and human resource development.
Taking this opportunity, the Senior Minister also thanked Japan for its generous support in the rehabilitation and construction of two bridges across the Mekong River, the expansion of National Road 5 from two lanes to four lanes and the construction Improving National Road No. 1 from Phnom Penh to Vietnam, the No. 1 ASEAN Highway from Thailand to Vietnam.
