(Phnom Penh): A road nearly 7 kilometers long and 12 meters wide, passing through three districts in Phnom Penh, which is the hand of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to the people on the outskirts of the city, was opened and repaired by the Phnom Penh Capital Administration To be bigger after this section of road was damaged by rain in the past.
The groundbreaking ceremony was held this morning, November 12, 2021, under the chairmanship of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh in Sre Reach village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that after the outbreak of Kovid 19, some construction sites were suspended, but after Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to reopen the country, today is the first construction site that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has opened. A road nearly 7 kilometers long is being rebuilt.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that this section of road is the bond of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the people in Phnom Penh, especially the people living in 3 communes and Khans such as Khan Por Senchey, Khan Kampol and Khan Prek Pnov.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that Samdech Techo not only liberated the country from zero and developed the country for prosperity, he also considered the well-being of the people. In fact, at this stage of the epidemic of Kovid 19, the prince tried his best to find a vaccine to prevent Kovid 19 to be given to all people throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In connection with this vaccination, the Governor of Phnom Penh also called on the people who have not been vaccinated in the first dose, the second dose, the third dose or the boost dose to go to the vaccination center. Health in their districts and the 14 district authorities must facilitate the people to get this vaccine for everyone.
On that occasion, Mr. Hem Darith, Governor of Por Senchey District, said that the section of road that was opened for the above repair work is 6,490 meters in the inter-Khan geographical area: Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Sangkat Sngor, Khan Kampoul and Sangkat Ponsaing, Khan Prek Pnov. From Victory Blvd., Sre Reach Village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey, to Street 42, Village, Sangkat Ponsaing, Khan Prek Pnov, is a dirt road (formerly in Por Sen Chey District).
The district governor said that in 2019 and 2020, due to the flood, the road was severely damaged. Seeing the plight of the people, Mr. Khuong Sreng also proposed plans to repair this road in the Phnom Penh Development Plan for 2020, but due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease, most projects were suspended, diverting funds to fight And Kovid-19 disease.
For this year 2021, Mr. Khuong Sreng also decided in principle to open the construction site to repair and expand the above road to the people who have a 12-meter-wide road and install a drainage system on both sides of the road.
