(Stung Treng): Another prisoner was arrested by the police this morning, November 12, 2021, while three other prisoners who escaped from Stung Treng Provincial Prison are still being hunted carefully. .
Stung Treng provincial authorities confirmed that the arrested prisoner, Chak Ly Chettali, was sentenced to life in prison for drug trafficking. He was arrested at around 8 am on the 12th of this month. This November in Thala Parivat district, Stung Treng province.
Authorities claimed that the prisoner was the mastermind behind the escape from prison, and before arresting him, police had to monitor his hunger, thirst and even in the forest.
Please be informed that 7 inmates in Stung Treng Provincial Prison escaped from the prison at more than 3 am on November 8, 2021. As of the afternoon of November 10, 2021, four prisoners have been arrested by the authorities, while the other three are still at large, but the authorities continue to search carefully.
According to Fresh News, in the early hours of the morning, as prison guards realized the inmates had broken through the wall, they used four firearms to threaten to stop the escape, but could not stop it.
After inspecting the actual location, the police found a number of handicraft tools and hard objects, such as tools to break the stone fence, such as drills, horseshoes, pieces of wood, blankets, blankets to block the sound.
7 Cambodian workers die and more than 10 are being rescued after mixing alcohol with drinking water caused poisoning
(Banteay Meanchey): Seven Cambodian workers died and more than 10 others were being treated at the hospital after they mixed alcohol with drinking water on November 11, 2021 at the Sak Kob Thom Center. Banteay Meanchey Province.
The provincial governor said that after the incident, the victims were immediately sent to Poipet City Referral Hospital, Mongkul Borei District Referral Hospital and some were sent to a hospital in Siem Reap.
If the provincial governor, due to the authorities restrict the import of alcohol into the center, the victim (three women) mixed alcohol with drinking water, causing poisoning.
