Colonel Heang Tharet confirmed that after receiving the victim's complaint, the district police and the police immediately launched a search until they cracked down and arrested two of the five drug suspects. (Two women) without confiscating the exhibits at the point of the former railway, Bak Touk village, Sangkat Tuol Sangke 1 on the evening of November 10, that is, after the suspect escaped for two days.
Colonel Heang Tharet confirmed that the arrested suspects were Chan Touch, a 19-year-old male, and Uy Thira, a 36-year-old male. The two suspects were addicted to drugs and had a negative Kovid 19 disease.
However, the two suspects who cracked down and arrested the case (aggravated theft) beating a motorbike from the victim were remanded in custody by the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate to build a case for legal action. How to continue to search for and arrest three other suspects who are fleeing.
