The reopening of the Bar-Disco-Tek Club business will contribute to providing employment opportunities for employees and contributing to the support of tourism and the national economy during the Kovid-19 learning phase in a new way.
In this regard, the Ministry of Tourism has instructed all business owners of clubs, bars and discos to pay attention to the strict implementation of the contents of Prakas No. 113 Prak, dated 11 November 2021 on the implementation of tourism safety rules. For the following bars-discotheque business:
1. To prepare a plan to adjust its business fitness in accordance with the requirements and guidelines as set out in the content of Prakas No. 113, dated November 11, 2021. The bar-disco-tek business must consider these terms as the main guidelines for implementation at this stage and must be implemented thoroughly and responsibly.
2. The business of club, bar and disco must have a clear action plan to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 for its business operations and must be vigilant to consider the safety of guests, staff safety and social security as a priority. Going forward, developing and managing the bar-disco-teak club business in the context (new normal trajectory).
3. The bar-disco-tek business's business is to organize regular staff training on the contents of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease and training on good hospitality, quality improvement, services, and services for adult entertainment centers.
4: The business of clubs, bars and discos must strictly and strictly implement the measures set by the Ministry of Health and the Tourism Safety Rules of the Ministry of Tourism to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease and to organize training on the rules. Travel safety for businesses, clubs, bars - discos on a regular basis.
5: The club business - Disco Tek must cooperate with the Royal Government to implement policies to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, especially to support the Royal Government's vaccination policy through the implementation of strategies and practical activities. Encourage all staff, including their families, to receive the Kovid-19 vaccine in full and in full doses as prescribed by the Ministry of Health.
