The National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia Hosts the 42nd Board Meeting of the ASEAN Law Association
(Phnom Penh): The National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia, with the approval of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on November 11, 2021, hosted the 42nd Board Meeting of the ASEAN Law Association. According to ZOOM.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Ly Chantola, Chairman of the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia, accompanied by the Permanent Vice President and members of the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia, the Chairman of the Permanent Secretariat and all members of the Permanent Secretariat.
The meeting went smoothly according to the planned agenda and the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia received a lot of congratulations and appreciation from the President of the ASEAN Law Association, President of the ASEAN Law Association of ASEAN. All nine and almost 200 participants for the well-organized and smiling hospitality of the meeting.
Mr. Ly Chantola, Chairman of the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Society of Cambodia, said that due to the global epidemic of Kovid-19, Cambodia has become the first country in the history of the ASEAN Law Association to hold a board meeting. Of the ASEAN Legal Association under the ZOOM program, which in the past was always held in turn by each country directly.
The 42nd Board of Directors of the ASEAN Law Association reviewed and decided on the internal affairs of some associations related to the activities of the Association in 2020 and 2021, as well as the direction of further work for implementation in 2022, including The readiness of the ASEAN Law Association to participate in the mechanisms of the ASEAN Meeting as an independent association.
He informed the ceremony about Cambodia's readiness to chair ASEAN 2022 and host the ASEAN Tourism Forum from 16 to 22 January 2022. Announcement invites all leaders and members of the ASEAN Law Association to join and visit Cambodia as the Grand Family of the ASEAN Law Association.
