(Phnom Penh): A video workshop on the new investment law of the Kingdom of Cambodia has been organized by the Council for the Development of Cambodia in collaboration with the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) and Mizuho Bank for Japanese investors and businesses. On the morning of Thursday, November 7, 2021, the 7th day of the lunar month of Chhlov Trisak 2565.
The Cambodian Ambassador also highlighted the importance of the new Investment Law, which will serve as a compass and a strong legal basis for investors to contribute to socio-economic development and as Cambodia recovers. After the outbreak of Kovid-19.
The Ambassador also expressed his full support for disseminating and raising awareness of the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the business community, which is in line with the implementation of the Cambodia Economic Diplomacy Strategy 2021-2023. .
Mr. Masahiro Mikami expressed his appreciation for the efforts of the Council for the Development of Cambodia in drafting a new law on investment over the years and received comments and suggestions from representatives of the private sector and the Japanese business community. In Cambodia, to collect all the inputs to be included in the new investment law.
The Ambassador also expressed strong belief that the promulgation of this law will be an effective and timely strategy to restore the socio-economic situation after the Kovid-19 crisis and make Cambodia Become an attractive and highly competitive destination in the region for quality and sustainable investment.
He emphasized the cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting and attracting direct investment from Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia towards the economic progress and prosperity of both countries.
In his keynote address, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea thanked the active participation of the Japanese business community in Cambodia through the Japan External Trade Organization and the Mizuho Bank, and other stakeholders for their attention. Submit to this law and help promote the dissemination of this law widely.
He also praised the regular cooperation between the Japan External Trade Organization and Mizuho Bank, which has always played an important role in promoting the investment opportunities and investment environment in Cambodia to Japanese investors.
On the other hand, the drafting of the new investment law is in line with the guidelines of the IDP policy and has undergone several studies and consultations, including consultations with the private sector.
The new investment law is designed based on the concrete structure of the Cambodian economy as well as the actual needs of investors in response to geopolitical and economic changes caused by trade tensions between economic powers, the industrial revolution. Fourth, the digital revolution, and the disruption of the global value chain caused by the Kovid-19 epidemic.
In this regard, he is optimistic that through today's seminar, the Japanese business community and Japanese investors in Cambodia have a clearer and deeper understanding of this law and will help promote Japanese investors from abroad to invest in Cambodia more.
It should be noted that as of the end of October 2021, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has welcomed and registered 146 qualified Japanese investment projects with a total investment of 2.853 million US dollars, including 66 investment projects. Located in a special economic zone with a total investment of about 340 million US dollars.
Ministry of Tourism Informs Capital-Provincial Governors to Prepare to Reopen Karaoke Club After November 30, 2021
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism on November 11, 2021 informed all capital-provincial governors about the re-opening of karaoke clubs after November 30, 2021.
According to a letter from the Ministry of Tourism, received by Fresh News, the Ministry of Tourism has also issued a Prakas on the Implementation of Tourism Safety Rules and Minimum Standards (SOP) Procedures for Karaoke Businesses, Clubs, Disco Takes to Prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and to prepare for the reopening of the business when the Royal Government allows after November 30, 2021.
In this prakas, the Ministry of Tourism has set out some guidelines as follows:
* Phase 1: Preparations before re-launch
1: To thoroughly examine and evaluate the readiness, fitness and performance of the business before deciding to allow any business to operate by notifying the operator in advance for the operator to apply for the operation of the Karaoke KTV Club. Entertainment Disco Bar.
2: To thoroughly train business owners and employees on tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SOP) in the new normal course for business, karaoke (KTV), entertainment clubs, bars, discos.
* Phase 2: After the decision to allow the reopening
1. Capital and provincial administrations shall establish mechanisms to continue regular and thorough inspections on the implementation of tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SOPs) along the new normal trajectory for the karaoke (KTV) business, entertainment clubs, bars, discos and teak. Once decided, allow re-launch.
2: In case the business owner does not properly follow the tourism safety rules and minimum standard operating procedures (SOP) in the new normal course for karaoke business (KTV), entertainment club, bar, disco, tek, the Capital-Provincial Administration shall take additional measures as required. To close the business and be responsible before the law in force.
