Southeast Asia's online economy projected to reach $ 1 trillion by 2030
SINGAPORE: Southeast Asia's online economy is projected to reach $ 1 trillion by 2030 as more people shop online and opt for shipping, an industry report shows. Food online. According to Reuters.
The 11-nation region is one of the fastest growing Internet markets due to the young population, the rapid growth of smartphone use and urbanization, as well as the growing middle class.
The online industry for Southeast Asia is expected to grow from about $ 174 billion in gross domestic product (GMV) by the end of 2021 to $ 360 billion by 2025, according to Reuters. Trillion dollars by 2030. This growth is mainly driven by the growth of e-commerce and food delivery as consumers get stuck at home and turn to the internet.
The report, which covers Indonesia, Thailand, Vietnam, Singapore, Malaysia and the Philippines, found that gross domestic product (GMV) through e-commerce is expected to double to $ 120 billion by the end of this year to 234 billion. Million dollars in 2025.
Xi Jinping Delivers Keynote Video at Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Business and Industry Leaders Meeting
BEIJING, Nov. 11 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping delivered a keynote speech on November 11 at the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Summit. Lead the industry and trade sector of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation in Beijing.
He said that currently 19 Kovid disease is still spreading around the world, the Asia-Pacific region should bravely carry the age to play a guiding role and move towards the common goal of building a common destiny of the Asia-Pacific region. Getting rid of Kovid 19 achieving economic recovery is one of the most important tasks facing the Asia-Pacific region.
Faced with problems related to the future of humankind, economic entities in the Asia-Pacific region and dignitaries of all walks of life must adhere to the priority of putting people and life first, promoting the spirit of scientific solidarity, helping each other to win the battle. Against Kovid 19.
The parties should be open-minded and grasp the general trend. The ideological and geopolitical divisions have no future.
Eco-friendly environment is the most basic public product and most conducive to people's happiness. The Asia-Pacific region needs to revitalize its economy in a green way, striving to be a leader in responding to climate change scientifically.
We need to properly understand the concept of sustainable development, adhere to putting people first, facilitate economic development, ensure livelihoods, save energy and reduce carbon emissions to accelerate the transition to green development and achieve development. More through the transition to a green development formula.
We should increase technological innovation and increase technology innovation regimes of Asia-Pacific member states to create an open, fair, truthful and non-discriminatory environment for technological development.
China's carbon offsets are a profound economic and social change. Although this task is very difficult, we will continue to move forward to contribute to the transition to a global green development.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Duke Kith Meng's participation in a video workshop on the dissemination of the new investment law to about 400 leaders and members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce on November 10, 2021.
This workshop was organized by the Council for the Development of Cambodia in collaboration with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce under the chairmanship of Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
A press release from the Council for the Development of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News, in which Duke Kith Meng said that the adoption of the new investment law is important and timely as Cambodia needs to recover its economy. From the epidemic of Kovid-19 disease.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng added that the new investment law will contribute to making Cambodia get the most out of the free trade agreements that the Royal Government has recently reached.
At the same time, Duke Kith Meng also thanked the Council for the Development of Cambodia for providing the opportunity for the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to participate in the consultation process in the drafting process and accepted the request of the private sector to include in the law. This new investment.
He emphasized that the private sector had welcomed the implementation of the law and expressed strong belief that its effective implementation of the law would create an open, transparent and predictable legal framework. Acceptable and favorable for investment.
In addition, Duke Kith Meng expressed his full support for disseminating and raising awareness of the Kingdom of Cambodia's investment law to the private sector.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, said that the new investment law was designed to respond to the geopolitical and economic changes caused by trade tensions between economic powers. , The Fourth Industrial Revolution, the Digital Revolution, and the Disruption of the Global Value Chain Caused by the Kovid-19 Outbreak.
The new investment law also takes into account the promotion of small and medium enterprises by providing incentives to small and medium enterprises in priority areas and promoting connectivity with large enterprises.
He also said that the partnership between the government and the private sector is an indispensable factor that must complement each other to help the economy grow and not just direct investment. From abroad is important, but investment by local investors is also involved and will contribute to the national economic growth.
The new investment law was promulgated by His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, on October 15, 2021. 19 Kovid Hospital fire kills 2 in Romania
