Minister of Environment: As a low emitter country, but Cambodia has shown great commitment to tackling climate change (Video inside) (English): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the National Council for Sustainable Development and Chairman The Cambodian delegation emphasized that as a low emitter of greenhouse gases, Cambodia has shown a strong commitment to tackling climate change.
In a statement issued at the 26th Summit of the Parties to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (COP26) in Chicago, United Kingdom on the morning of 10 November 2021, Minister Say Sam Al stated that Contribute to reducing greenhouse gas emissions Cambodia has put forward four plans, including:
* First: Launched more than 400 megawatts of solar energy, which represents 15% of our energy source * Second: Do not build new coal-fired power plants * Third: Do not build dams in Along the Mekong River * 4: Reduce deforestation by half by 2030 and no greenhouse gas emissions by 2040.
On that occasion, Mr. Say Sam Al said that this is our unprecedented gathering because of the Kovid 19 pandemic and because of climate change is no longer a rumor. Climate change, as well as global pandemics, does not stop at our borders, and our presence here is a sign that ensures that as world leaders we do not relinquish our shared responsibility for climate action. .
He stressed that international climate finance is still insufficient to meet demand, especially for the adaptation sector, which we find still difficult to obtain for the most climate-sensitive countries.
"I call on all developed countries to increase their contribution to the financial mechanisms under the Convention and to further facilitate access to these funds directly," said Minister Say Sam Al.
Please note that Cambodia has submitted the Updated NDC report with the goal of reducing emissions by 42% by 2030. In addition, Cambodia is developing a long-term, carbon-neutral development strategy to promote low-carbon activities, climate resilience and environmental development.
