(Phnom Penh): In addition to preparing to receive vaccinated international tourists, the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Tourism, has been promoting the promotion of safe tourists from many major tourism markets, including looking at tourism destinations in Japan also to develop a strategy to attract more tourists from this country.
Minister Thong Khon further discussed with Mikami Masahiro that he would promote the opening of more direct flights between Cambodia and Japan, including special arrangements for the travel of Japanese tourists to the above three destinations in The context of Kovid 19. In case of travel to Siem Reap and can continue to travel extensively to other designated tourist destinations.
The minister also urged that Cambodian tour operators be allowed to re-enter Japan, as Cambodians are fully vaccinated and can travel abroad safely.
The Minister of Tourism of Cambodia and the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia also agreed to expand cooperation in the field of tourism and set out a plan to welcome Japanese tourists within the framework of Cambodia's vaccine tourism strategy, such as:
First, to support the online workshop on the connection between the private sector, tourism business, Cambodia-Japan.
Second, support the organization of tours and tours of tour companies and the media from Japan.
Third, Cambodia has invited Japanese tour companies and media to participate in the ASEAN Tourism Forum from 16-22 January 2022 in Sihanoukville.
Fourth, support Cambodia in the development of tourism products such as community tourism, ecotourism, agro-tourism, health tourism and comfort tourism, second home tourism, which Japan is famous for in these areas.
Fifth, continue to support the training of human resources by creating and upgrading the skills of Cambodian tourism professionals.
Seventh: Examine the signing of a memorandum of understanding on tourism cooperation or the framework for cooperation on tourism between Cambodia and Japan in the future. This memorandum will further promote tourism cooperation in all fields.
Eighth: Establish a working group between the Ministry of Tourism and the Japanese side to promote cooperation and initiatives going forward.
