Kampong Speu Provincial Governor: Although the price of rice has fallen slightly, farmers have received high yields
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, said that he was proud that farmers received more rice yields than last year, but also regretted the lower prices than in previous years.
This statement was made while the provincial governor led the relevant professional officers to inspect the harvest situation of farmers in O commune, Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province on November 10, 2021.
Mr. Vy Samnang said that for Kampong Speu, this year, more than 120,000 hectares of rice were planted beyond the plan, up from 110,000 hectares last year. While the cultivation exceeds this plan, what farmers and authorities are proud of is that the yield has exceeded expectations, with more than 3 tons of rice per hectare.
Along with this pride, the provincial governor also expressed regret for the yield that farmers received this year, the price is lower than previous years, this year farmers sell only 1050 riels per kilogram of rice. Compared to last year, farmers sold from 1,100 riel to 1,300 riel.
He said that although the price has been reduced to 1,050 riel per kilogram, farmers still make some profit, but that this profit is not in line with their expectations.
