Cambodia announces the implementation of "Digital Literacy Training Program in Tourism" in line with the Industrial Revolution 4.0
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and the Cambodian Center 4.0 this morning, November 10, 2021, organized the launching ceremony of the "Digital Literacy Training Program in Cambodia's Tourism Sector" to jointly develop the capacity of drivers. Tourism business and tourism operators in line with the context of the evolution of digital technology, or "Industrial Revolution 4.0".
The digital literacy training program in Cambodia's tourism sector is designed to meet the needs of using technology in the current context, as well as to contribute to the recovery of tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis. This training will contribute to the development of digital knowledge and skills for private employees, business owners in the tourism sector, as well as for tourism officials at both national and sub-national levels.
In order to promote the digital literacy campaign in Cambodia's tourism sector to be successful, efficient and effective, Minister Thong Khon made three recommendations, including:
First, continue to organize digital literacy training in Cambodia's tourism sector, focusing on basic literacy and literacy skills to meet current and future needs in line with the new normalization path and the Industrial Revolution 4.0.
Second, promote the adoption and widespread use of technology in all value chains of Cambodia's tourism sector, both in demand and supply.
Third, promote the modernization of tourism information resources for both international and domestic tourism markets using digital nurseries.
In addition, Mr. HUN Many shared four ideas to promote digital literacy in Cambodia, including:
First, continue to strengthen science and technology training from the basic education at the upper secondary level.
Second, continue to promote absorption and adaptation by inspiring all citizens who are socio-economic cells and indispensable actors to absorb and adapt to new technologies by attending training courses. Literacy and access to additional resources available on the Internet
Third, continue to strengthen cooperation between government institutions with the private sector and educational institutions, including general education schools, vocational schools and universities, to integrate technology and science education in training, orientation and capacity building.
Fourth, continue to develop support infrastructure, especially information technology and telecommunications networks, to support innovation and the strengthening of digital knowledge and skills in Cambodia.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: Cambodia wants more ASEAN defense institutions to work together to prevent cross-border epidemics, especially Kovid 19
In Cambodia, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has played a key role in preventing the spread of the disease through a massive vaccination campaign for the Cambodian people and has taken the lead in controlling the population movement, the Minister of Defense said. Citizens across the country will implement the government's 19 measures against Kovid, especially in border areas.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh emphasized: "Seeing the importance of cross-border cooperation to prevent global epidemics, Cambodia believes that practical cooperation among ASEAN defense institutions in preventing cross-border epidemics should be "Further strengthened."
He stressed that strengthening cross-border cooperation will benefit our military in jointly addressing other common security challenges in the future, such as cross-border crime, humanitarian assistance and disaster relief (HADR). ) And so on.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh added: "The Kovid 19 pandemic is truly the most disturbing event in our modern history. The fight against Kovid 19 has become our common battle. "With the 19 outbreak of Kovid, we have seen the dominant role of the armed forces in the fight against global pandemics."
More importantly, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said that the ASEAN military has also provided humanitarian assistance during cross-border disasters to other countries in the region. As natural disasters are likely to increase in the future, practical cooperation among ASEAN militaries must be strengthened, especially through the full and effective implementation of the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting's three-year work program. .
