France to build more nuclear reactors (Video inside) (Paris): French President Emmanuel Macron announced on Tuesday that France will resume construction of nuclear reactors to ensure independence. Its energy part. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday, November 10, 2021.
"For the first time in many years, we will resume construction of nuclear reactors in our country and will continue to develop renewable energy," McConnell said in a message to the nation. "Back." It is in response to the rising prices of fuel and gas, as well as electricity, that the French people have faced in recent weeks.
The French president explained that the decision was made to ensure France's energy independence and to ensure the country's electricity supply, as well as to achieve its goal of achieving carbon neutrality by 2050. .
Makrong did not elaborate, but his government is expected to announce plans for six new nuclear reactors in the coming weeks. In 2020, France announced that it would not finalize the construction of a new nuclear reactor until the long-delayed Flamanville 3 nuclear reactor was completed and operational.
