On the occasion of assuming the chairmanship of the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, pledged to urge the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting to focus on joint efforts to achieve important tasks. Achieving these tasks will help the region achieve a harmonious security and be able to maintain post-Kovid 19 rehabilitation through the strong unity of all of us.
In this spirit, as the rotating chair of Samdech Po Pichey Sena Tea Banh, said that Cambodia has chosen the theme "Solidarity for Security and Harmony" for chairing the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting next year.
According to the above theme, Cambodia will work towards the following priorities:
First, strengthen efforts and commitment to maintain peace, stability and prosperity in the region by adhering to the principles of win-win solutions to all problems.
Second, increase the role of women in ASEAN and their participation in UN peacekeeping operations.
Third, to promote border cooperation between the forces of ASEAN countries in response to the global epidemic.
Fourth, increase efforts to fully implement the three-year action plan of the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting.
Fifth, to promote trust-building and transparency, and in this regard, Cambodia will launch the third Cambodia National Defense Policy Document through the official release of the 2021 National Defense White Paper to express its efforts in Building trust and transparency in national defense in the region.
In line with the above priority points, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh emphasized that Cambodia will also focus on strengthening the core role of ASEAN and ASEAN solidarity for regional communication mechanisms and with external partners. This focus will be on the ASEAN path and principles set out in the ASEAN Charter, the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia and the ASEAN Vision on the Indo-Pacific.
At the same time, the Cambodian Defense Minister said that ASEAN must unite to maintain its resilience and resilience in the face of pressures and influences arising from rising geopolitical competition, transnational crime, terrorism and change. Climate and infectious diseases. This will ensure that ASEAN continues to move towards peace, security and sustainable prosperity.
"We believe that the priorities set for the 2022 ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting will continue to strengthen ASEAN unity and strengthen ASEAN's core role and leading role in "Regional and on the international stage." UN Under-Secretary-General commends Cambodia's Kovid 19 vaccination campaign
The compliment was made on the occasion of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon allowing the UN official to pay a courtesy call and discuss work at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
