(Kandal): On November 10, 2021, the Kandal Provincial Authority led by Mr. Nop Dara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, led a team to close a excavation site owned by Ta Mab and fined according to the law. Seeing that the excavation site is not yet licensed and even causing many other anarchies.
Mr. Nop Dara closed the site after he led several experts to inspect the excavation sites in Kandal Stung district, Kandal province and found that the excavation site is not yet licensed.
Mr. Nop Dara stated that the force was sent to inspect and search for any excavation site that does not have a permit and does not comply with the principles of mining law, traffic law, etc. to study and check the payment of royalties. State and so on.
He said that if it is found that any excavation site is illegal, he will suspend the business temporarily, fine according to the transitional law and request to apply for the law properly.
The action of closing the excavation site of the owner named Tam Mab, located in Traos village, Trea commune, Kandal Stung district, the working group decided to stop the business owner completely, waiting for some problems and the law to come first. He was also fined according to Article 35 of the law.
Mr. Nop Dara warned all mining business owners throughout Kandal province to strictly abide by the law, otherwise the authorities will use hot water regardless of which side.
At the same time, he also suspended two other businesses in Thmey Village and Kraing Tey Village, Thmey Commune, which dug beyond the license limit and did not pay bribes and acted illegally.
He advised and encouraged business owners to do business properly, have permits and comply with technical standards. For these three businesses, the commission will follow the procedure by imposing fines and re-paying royalties to the state.
