Council for the Development of Cambodia Disseminates New Investment Law to Leaders and Members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce
(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia, in collaboration with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, on November 10, organized a video workshop to disseminate the new Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the leaders and members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce. 400 people chaired by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
In his welcoming speech, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, thanked the Council for the Development of Cambodia for providing the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce with the opportunity to participate in the consultation process in the design process and for accepting the request of the section. Private is included in this new investment law.
He added that the adoption of the investment law was important and timely, as Cambodia needed to recover economically after the Kovid-19 outbreak, and that it would contribute to Cambodia has made the most of the free trade agreements that the Royal Government has recently reached.
In this regard, the private sector applauded the implementation of this law and expressed strong belief that the effective implementation of this law will definitely create an open, transparent and predictable legal framework. Has been favorable for investment.
Neak Oknha also expressed his full support for disseminating and raising awareness of the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the private sector.
Mr. Sok Chendasophea thanked the leadership and members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, as well as members in the provinces, for their emphasis on the importance and attention of the private sector to the law. For this meeting is being conducted on video.
He informed the workshop about the background of the drafting of investment law, which started in 2015 in accordance with the indications of the Cambodia Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 and went through many studies and consultations, including Consultations with the private sector as well.
In this regard, he thanked the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce for providing good input in the process of drafting this law, as well as in the mission to promote and attract investment in the past.
He said the new investment law was designed to respond to geopolitical and economic changes caused by trade tensions between economic powers, the Fourth Industrial Revolution, the digital revolution, and the disruption of the line. Global value chain caused by the Kovid-19 pandemic.
He also said that the partnership between the government and the private sector is an indispensable factor that must complement each other to help the economy grow, and not just direct investment. From abroad is important, but investment by local investors is also involved and will contribute to the national economic growth.
In this regard, he believes that through today's seminar, the leaders and members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce have a better and deeper understanding of this law and will increase their investment to another level, as well as help promote Domestic and foreign investors as well.
