Ministry of Women's Affairs and National Authority for Combating Drugs Organize Regional Training of Trainers on Promoting Maternal Involvement to Prevent Drug Use and Distribution
(Koh Kong): Under the cooperation between the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and the Koh Kong Provincial Drug Control Committee, on November 10, 2021, organized a training course for regional trainers on the promotion of Involve mothers to prevent drug use and distribution.
The ceremony was presided over by Ms. Long Sophally, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, and Mr. Tou Savuth, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Provincial Drug Control Commission. The Capital-Provincial Department of Women's Affairs is located in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville, Kep, Kampot, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Kandal, Siem Reap and 42 related institutions.
The purpose is to develop the knowledge of the Women's Affairs Officer so that these operators can use it as a basis to mobilize the participation of women, grandmothers, mothers, aunts, sisters to prevent the use, storage and distribution of illegal drugs from the community. We.
