Speaking on behalf of Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Ms. Long Sophally said that in 2019, the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the National Council for Women of Cambodia inspected the situation of women in 28 prisons across 25 capitals and provinces. It found that most women in prison committed crimes related to drug trafficking, distribution and storage, affecting their families and society as a whole.
On that occasion, Ms. Long Sophally added that drugs are also a contributing factor in encouraging users to commit domestic violence, violence against women, human trafficking and other crimes, according to data collected through Live interviews with target women at the sub-national level in seven provinces (including Siem Reap, Kampong Speu, Kampong Cham, Battambang, Svay Rieng, Koh Kong and Ratanakkiri).
