The Ministry of Culture will hold a major art event later this month to celebrate the three-year anniversary of the inclusion of Cambodian puppetry in the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will organize a big art event called "Memory Night 2021" on November 28, 2021 to celebrate the tangible and intangible cultural heritage that has been inscribed on the Heritage List. The World and the Intangible Heritage of Humanity, in particular, celebrate the 3rd anniversary of the inclusion of the Cambodian Puppet Theater as an Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity Online.
He added that this important event will be broadcast live on the official page of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and on a number of TV-news-social media stations that will jointly broadcast more widely for the world to see. From the value of Cambodian puppetry, which is the value of humanity, and this is the goal that we all want.
He also called on the Cambodian people, especially the youth, to continue their supportive activities to preserve the rich cultural heritage that the Cambodian ancestors left for a long time to come.
Separately, Mr. Tith Thavrith, Undersecretary of State and Deputy Chairman of the Permanent Working Group in charge of event management and Chairman of the Technical Working Group for Event and Performing Arts, further confirmed that this is the second time that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has organized this event. Up after organizing the first memorial night event in the territory of Angkor, Siem Reap province, which was attended by more than 20,000 people.
However, in 2021, due to the global problem of Kovid-19, the 2021 Memorial Night event will not be held directly in a public place or in any tourist area, which means that the aesthetic and technical aspects of the performance are revealed. Two new flavors in a new context of technology (online).
