(Phnom Penh): The vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense has vaccinated more than 610,000 people in Phnom Penh in the past 29 days.
The Ministry of National Defense's Kovid 19 vaccination team launched a booster vaccination campaign (third dose) for people in Phnom Penh on October 11. Vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense is responsible for vaccination in 6 districts, including: Meanchey, Dangkor, Kambol, Por Senchey, Russey Keo, Toul Kork and Khan Sen Sok.
According to the report, as of November 9, the Ministry of National Defense has vaccinated 613,211 people, including 354,924 women.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Joint Chiefs of Staff and Chief Executive Officer of the Ministry of National Defense, told Fresh News that the booster vaccination process went well as planned and did not face many obstacles. He also noted that people have been actively involved in the booster dose.
However, General Ith Sarath continues to call on the people, no matter how busy, to take a dose to encourage everyone to get better health protection from the 19 Kovid virus. General Ith Sarath also called on companies to provide opportunities for workers working in their companies, as well as workers at construction sites to go to the dose to encourage everyone.
It should be noted that for the army-administered doses, the army only vaccinated citizens who had received the first and second doses with the army and had a gap of at least four months from the second dose.
The required document for attachment to the first dose is the immunization card, if not already attached to the immunization form in the first and second doses.
In that case, if people lose their ID card or lost their vaccination form, they can report it to the team there and the team will verify the information with the system. If information is found in the system, the team will give a third dose and re-arrange the card.
