Private sector expects trade between Cambodia and Australia to increase next year
(Phnom Penh): The private sector has expressed optimism that trade between Cambodia and Australia will improve further in the future, especially after the entry into force of the RCEP next year, which will boost exports from Cambodia. Australia is growing.
The optimism comes after Australian Foreign Minister and Minister for Women's Affairs Mary Pence paid a two-day official visit to Cambodia.
Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News on November 9 that trade between Cambodia and Australia has a long history of good relations with both the public and private sectors to contribute to development. At the same time, the RCEP agreement, of which Cambodia and Australia are members, entered into force in January 2022, will further facilitate trade between the two countries.
He expects that in addition to the RCEP, Cambodia may also have a bilateral free trade agreement in the near future to facilitate trade and investment with Australia.
He added that in the past, the export of products from Cambodia to Australia has been good, with the country importing products such as bicycles, clothing and agricultural products. In addition to exports, Australian investors' investments in Cambodia are also plentiful.
"The important thing is that we want him to bring in more of our agricultural products. Not only that, recently the Australian Ambassador has studied the main crops and strategies for bringing them to the Australian market and Europe as well to promote and promote our agro-industrial crops, which are also the main products exported to Australia, which is the best point for Cambodia-Australia.
Please be informed that the Agricultural Value Chain-Australia (CAVAC) program, sponsored by the Australian Government, recently conducted a study on the potential of Cambodian products, showing that nine Cambodian agricultural products include mango, lentils, cashews, peppers, sweet potatoes, sesame. Palm sugar and dried bananas are expensive and in high demand in Australia, New Zealand, Europe, China, ASEAN.
At the inauguration ceremony of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction on November 8, 2021, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia and Australia have good trade relations and the two sides will enhance relations. Better trade.
He said that Cambodia and Australia still have a lot of cooperation to do together to increase trade volume, especially after the RCEP came into force in January next year.
