A new security partnership called AUKUS was recently formed by the United States, Britain and Australia, in which the United States and Britain will help Australia build nuclear-powered submarines. As a result of the alliance, Australia decided to cancel its agreement with France, which it signed in 2016 to buy 12 conventional submarines, leading to a series of verbal and diplomatic attacks.
