(Kampot): Brigadier General Thi Visal, Deputy Director of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police, stated that although National Road 3 is equipped with speed cameras, there are still mobile speed monitors. Which is operated by the land traffic police agency in an unpredictable manner.
This morning, November 9, 2021, on the occasion of accompanying Mr. Khan Maner, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of all projects to improve National Road No. 3, to use electricity. Two traffic lights and check the arrangement of 10 speed camera poles on National Road 3.
Brigadier General Thi Visal said, "For the cameras that we see in practice, see here permanently. At the same time, we also have another mobile speed control device operated by the Road Traffic Police. The piercing is not to know in advance.
Brigadier General Thi Visal said that the mobile speed limit camera has a special function to detect the speed of the car, which can be caught at a distance of about 50 meters, and for the fine, depending on the type of offense. Speed and type of vehicle, and the fine is 120,000 riel, the largest is 62,000 riel.
The general added that the overall purpose of the camera, both fixed and mobile, is to contribute to the prevention and reduction of road accidents caused by speeding, which is the first factor that causes accidents on Roads account for between 30 and 40% of traffic accidents.
Brigadier General Thi Visal, on behalf of the National Police, also called on all road users to respect all traffic laws to reduce road deaths, especially to drive at the speed limit set by law to contribute. Do not endanger yourself and others and contribute to the loss of the national budget caused by traffic accidents.
Please be informed that the Sub-Decree on Transitional Fines 2020 stipulates that drivers of motorcycles or trailers, trailers or tricycles or four-wheeled motorbikes for speeding from 1 to 19 kilometers per hour will be fined 60,000 Riels and 10 Ten thousand riels for speeding from 30 to 39 kilometers per hour.
In particular, if you drive faster than the speed limit of 30 to 39 kilometers per hour, you will be fined 180,000 riels for light vehicles and 375,000 riels for heavy vehicles. Another 466 vehicles were inspected and fined on November 9, 2021
