The following is the decision of Kampong Cham Provincial Administration: A Cambodian project to be selected with the support of Kovid 19 Special Fund for quality distance learning and student employment
The initiative seeks to conduct research on the impact of Kovid on students in higher education: an analysis of the economic, social, cultural and psychological impacts to prevent the psychological or socio-economic consequences of a health crisis. And the development of the necessary tools for the treatment, prevention or prevention of health risks.
A project led by the National University of Battambang in collaboration with the Royal University of Phnom Penh and the Royal University of Fine Arts, this project requires a study of the impact of Kovid 19 on students in higher education: an analysis of the economic, social and cultural impacts. And Psychology within the framework of the International Appel COVID19.2 Outreach Project by the French Agency for Higher Education (AUF).
The object of the project is to take the results of the research and make recommendations to ministries, institutions and universities in order to ensure the sustainability of students' studies during the health crisis and to strengthen employment access through the flexibility of higher education institutions and Produce the necessary equipment for the treatment, prevention or prevention of health risks.
The Will of the Higher Education Initiative of Cambodia and the commitment of the National University of Battambang to promote scientific research at universities present some examples of this project: Cooperation in science and psychology, research development The University focuses on psychological analysis methods related to public health and mental health issues encountered during the 19 crisis.
This project is provided in response to the AUF International Outreach, which was conducted for the second time in 2000 to support universities' initiatives to lead and build health-promoting activities. Public for innovation, pedagogy and strengthening university governance during times of crisis.
Starting from this promotion, 56 projects led by 52 institutions of higher education in 37 countries will receive financial support for 12 months, and some institutions can start implementation from December 2021. Go.
All documents are evaluated by a panel of experts from the 10 AUF regional leaders representing the five continents.
AUF strives to ensure its vital role for universities in the overall development of society and to continue its activities with widespread recognition in French higher education and training at the tertiary level. Includes responses to global challenges.
Founded in 1961, the French Higher Education Agency (AUF) is the world's first network of universities, with more than 1,000 member institutions, present in 120 countries, and a direct operator of international organizations of French-speaking countries. Higher education and research.
Through its network on five continents, AUF is close to the education ecosystem and universities have become one of many operators located directly across the country. The AUF makes a difference through agreements in its field through conferences of heads of state and government of French-speaking countries.
