(Phnom Penh): A total of 11 opposition activists have been released by a court, including seven released last week and four others will be released on November 10 and 12. This is according to Mr. Plang Sophal, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, confirmed to Fresh News on November 9, 2021.
According to Mr. Plang Sophal, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court held a series of hearings and announced a verdict on October 26, 2021 to try criminal cases involving a number of accused youth activists. Known as the Khmer Thavarak Youth Group and announced the verdict on November 1, 2021 in the criminal case involving the accused Kak Sovanchhay.
According to the court's decision, the defendants were sentenced to prison for the crimes they were charged with, but the sentence was to be served in prison and the rest of the sentence was suspended. Hong Lim, also known as a Cambodian-Australian expatriate, was acquitted.
It should be noted that the decision of the above court came after the Ministry of Justice issued guidelines on October 25, 2021, encouraging the court to decide on bail and the use of probation in the trial. Contribute to resolving prison overcrowding.
A spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court added that four other convicts who had completed their prison sentences had not yet been released due to their detention. He was remanded in custody and convicted in other cases, including: Kong Sam An (opposition activist), Long Kunthea, Phuon Keo Raksmey, and Thon Ratha. Mother Nature Movement activists).
Spokesman Plang Sophal added that the series of releases also contributed to resolving prison overcrowding and complying with the Ministry of Justice's guidelines.
This was confirmed by Mr. Khan Maner, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of all projects to improve National Road 3 this morning, November 9, 2021, on the occasion of leading the working group with participation. From Brigadier General Thi Visal, Deputy Director of the Traffic Police and Public Safety Department, opened two traffic lights and inspected the installation of 10 speed camera poles on National Road 3.
Please note that the construction and improvement of National Road No. 3 is divided into two stages, the first phase from Choam Chao, Phnom Penh to Bek Kus, Takeo province, 70 km long, widening the road to 24.5 meters as a concrete road. Rubber (AC) 9 cm thick, divided into 4 lanes (2 lanes to 2 lanes). The second phase from Bek Kus to Kampot city, 64.8 km long, 7 cm thick AC road, extending the width of the road up to 12 m, divided into 2 lanes.
The project has a total budget of 219,911,000 US dollars, a concessional financing from the People's Republic of China with the contribution of the Royal Government of Cambodia, built by the China Bridge and Road Corporation, technical supervision by Guangzhou Construction Technical Consulting Co., Ltd. It takes 48 months to build.
