China's foreign trade maintains strong growth in first 10 months
BEIJING: China's foreign trade maintained growth momentum in the first 10 months of 2021 as the superpower's economy continued to grow steadily. According to the Xinhua news agency.
Both exports and imports continued to maintain double-digit growth in the first 10 months of this year, with exports up 22.5 percent and exports up 21.8 percent year-on-year. Each other last year.
In October alone, China's exports and imports rose 17.8 percent year on year to 3.34 trillion yuan, down 5.6 percent from September.
Over the past 10 months, China's trade with its three major trading partners, ASEAN, the European Union and the United States - has maintained strong growth.
During this period, China's trade value growth with the three trading partners was 20.4 percent with ASEAN, 20.4 percent with the European Union and 23.4 percent with the United States.
China's trade with countries along roads, belts and roads increased by 23 percent from the same period last year, according to the customs data.
