Australian Foreign Minister mentions AUKUS alliance to Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Phnom Penh): As expected by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Australian Foreign Minister Mary Phen raised the issue of the Australian-British-US Trilateral Alliance (AUKUS) in a face-to-face meeting. This Monday afternoon, November 8, 2021.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, at the inauguration of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, just minutes before meeting with Ms. Mariss Phen, predicted that during her visit to Cambodia, the Foreign Minister would inform Samdech about the tripartite alliance. AUKUS.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, confirmed to the media that Ms. Mariss Phen had indeed raised this issue with Samdech Techo, and Samdech Techo Prime Minister also thanked her for this information.
However, Mr. Eang Sophalleth did not break down the details of the discussion between Samdech Techo and Ms. Mariss Phen.
In addition to the above issues, in this meeting, Ms. Mariss Phen also expressed the progress and development in Cambodia. She noted that Cambodia is now much more developed than it was in 2002 and 2005 when she visited.
The Australian Foreign Minister also praised measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia through vaccination, leading to the reopening of schools and the opening of new economic activities.
She also expressed appreciation for the cooperation between Australia and Cambodia in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks. For the bilateral framework, she expressed satisfaction with the fruits of cooperation in agriculture, military, education and the fight against Kovid 19.
She informed Samdech Techo that the Royal Government of Australia has decided to provide Cambodia with 3.25 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine. Of that, 1 million doses will be handed over to Cambodia before the end of 2021.
For the multilateral framework, she congratulated Cambodia for hosting the ASEAN Summit. She expressed her satisfaction and pleasure at the cooperation between ASEAN and Australia, and she informed Samdech Techo that she would help Cambodia succeed as chair of ASEAN.
Within the ASEAN framework, Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes that Australia will join ASEAN member countries in the fight against Kovid 19 to move towards ASEAN reunification after being cut off by Kovid 19.
