Japan to change criteria for assessing 19 Kovid status in the country based on hospital capacity
TOKYO (Reuters) - Japan will shift its COVID-19 status assessment policy from a focus on the number of daily infections to a focus on hospital capacity, Japanese media reported on Monday. This is according to the release by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday, November 8, 2021.
(Phnom Penh): The Australian Minister for Foreign Affairs and Minister for Women's Affairs, Mary Pann, has congratulated Cambodia for hosting the ASEAN Summit next year. At the same time, she asserted that Australia would help Cambodia succeed as chair of ASEAN.
Ms. Mariss Phen made the remarks during a courtesy call on Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the morning of November 8, 2021 at the Peace Palace during her two-day official visit.
After the meeting, Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, confirmed to the media that in the multilateral framework, she congratulated Cambodia for hosting the ASEAN Summit. She expressed her satisfaction and pleasure at the cooperation between ASEAN and Australia, and she informed Samdech Techo that she would help Cambodia succeed as chair of ASEAN.
She also expressed satisfaction with the cooperation between Australia and Cambodia in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks. For the bilateral framework, she expressed satisfaction with the fruits of cooperation in agriculture, military, education and the fight against Kovid 19.
In response, Samdech Techo agreed with her assessment of the good relations between Cambodia and Australia in both the bilateral and multilateral frameworks. Within the ASEAN framework, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Australia will join ASEAN member countries in the fight against Kovid 19 to move towards ASEAN reconnection after being cut off by Kovid 19.
At the inaugural ASEAN-Australia Summit on 27 October, ASEAN leaders agreed to establish a Comprehensive Strategic Partnership between ASEAN and Australia and reaffirmed their commitment. To work with Australia to make that comprehensive strategic partnership effective.
As Cambodia becomes the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced his support for the promotion of ASEAN-Australia relations to become a comprehensive strategic partner.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has released a video on Minimum Standards (SOP) procedures in the new normal course for the Beer Garden business to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and to improve tourism safety in Cambodia as well as sustain the business. Well.
