In this case, Fresh News Agency in Mondulkiri asked for comment on the case because it is his jurisdiction, but the district governor did not comment on this. China ready to cut tariffs under RCEP
The Ministry of Commerce said that the Asia-Pacific Free Trade Agreement will boost confidence in the economic growth among its members after the Kovid-19 era.
China is ready to implement all 701 obligations, including tariff reductions and changes in rules on the origin of goods, the Commerce Ministry said. China will also release guidelines for local governments and industries after conducting more than 600 training courses for 166,000 Chinese businessmen, trade officials and customs officials.
Signed by 15 countries in November 2020, the RCEP is the largest regional trade agreement in the world and is expected to link people and trade output by 30% of people and trade output. The world.
The agreement also aims to eliminate 91 percent tariffs on goods and standardize investment rules, intellectual property and e-commerce among the laws. The agreement is expected to eliminate import duties within 10 years.
