Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara vows to continue 100% land registration by 2023 as the Ministry issues 6.3 million land titles
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, has expressed his commitment to continue to work hard to register 100% of the land for the people by 2023, while the Ministry of Land Management has issued 6 titles. 3 million plots so far.
Speaking at the "Inauguration of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction" this morning, November 8, 2021, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara stated that the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has issued six titles. 3 million plots equal to 90.03% of the estimated total number of 7 million plots.
"Continue to strive for 100% land registration by 2023 to ensure the security of land tenure, which is provided by the Royal Government to people to live, cultivate and invest to create jobs, increase income, contribute to socio-economic development." This is the additional confirmation of the Deputy Prime Minister.
