(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on the afternoon of November 08, 2021 issued an official decision to allow weddings and other traditional ceremonies in Phnom Penh, with a maximum of 200 participants per ceremony. . This is according to the decision received by Fresh News.
Article 1 of this decision states that "weddings and other traditional ceremonies are allowed in Phnom Penh, with a maximum of 200 participants per ceremony from November 8. This year 2021 onwards.
According to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, the maximum number of participants per 200 people is limited to the families of the hosts, relatives and invited guests. Chefs, bands and waitresses are not included.
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has advised the host to have a suitable private venue for organizing weddings or other traditional ceremonies and to submit the application to the district administration of the venue first for review and decision.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, November 08, 2021, on the occasion of the inauguration of the new building of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, announced the permission to organize this wedding ceremony. However, it is limited to 200 guests.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision to reschedule the wedding after months of delays due to the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia, but now that the situation is under control and has improved The prince allowed the ceremony to be rescheduled.
