Speaking at the inauguration ceremony of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction on the morning of November 8, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: You sent me enough, and at least that Hun Sen did not dare? "Hun Sen dared to handcuff a politician at 12 o'clock at night, why not just handcuff him to come and explain in court."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's warning came after Srun Srun, who some media outlets called an activist of the Paris Peace Agreement, criticized that the change from two-thirds to 50 percent plus one was against the principle of duty. The 1991 Paris Agreement, established by the four armed conflict groups.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that this statement was seriously illegal and that legal action should be taken. "Where do you have the legal basis to accuse us of changing this parliament from two-thirds to 50 plus one, in violation of the Paris Agreement?" He asked. "The Paris Agreement stipulates that in the Cambodian Constitution, two-thirds must be in the parliament."
The amendment of the Constitution to use the formula 50 plus 1 or 50% + 1 was approved by the National Assembly by 101 votes out of 123 members of the National Assembly on March 2, 2006 at the 4th session of the 3rd National Assembly. The adoption of this formula came through a secret meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Sam Rainsy.
At least 50% of the vote plus one National Assembly and the Senate can:
* To elect the President, the Vice-President of the National Assembly and the members of the various committees of the National Assembly; In the National Assembly and the Senate.
