Royal Government Establishes Steering Committee for Implementation of Mondulkiri Tourism Master Plan 2021-2035
The establishment of this committee is the result of the approval of the implementation of the Master Plan for Tourism Development of Mondulkiri Province (2021-2035) on August 12, 2021 under the guidance of Minister Thong Khon and technical guidance by Mr. Thong. Rathasak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, is the Chairman of the Secretariat.
This committee will act as a strong and permanent institutional mechanism to lead the implementation of the master plan, along with the approval of investment projects and tourism development and relevant inter-sectoral support in Mondulkiri, as indicated in the action plan of the master plan.
This is the second sub-decree to establish the National Committee after the Royal Government issued Sub-Decree No. 125 on July 30, 2021 to establish the National Committee for Management and Development of Community-Based Tourism and Ecotourism, which is chaired by the Minister of Tourism. The Chief Minister of the Ministry of Environment and the Minister of Agriculture are the Vice-Chairmen.
