Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that this law is a great legacy for the nation for hundreds of years to avoid foreign interference.
Please be informed that the Law on the Determination of One Khmer Nationality for the President of the Constitutional Council, the President of the Senate, the President of the National Assembly and the Prime Minister was officially signed into law by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni Lay, on Third, November 2021.
Constitutional Law on the Amendment of Article 19 (new), Article 82 (new), Article 106 (new), Article 119 (new), Article 119 (new) and Article 137 (new) of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 3 and Article 4 of the Additional Constitution Proposed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on October 6, 2021.
This law is claimed to be made to ensure both legal and political privileges for the position and unwavering commitment to the nation and the people of Cambodia in all circumstances and to ensure the protection of national interests and Cambodians from foreign interference.
Legislation to determine the "single Khmer nationality" for the leaders of the top institutions of the four nations is another new historical event in the history of Cambodia that has not been mentioned since the inception of the Constitution. However, the establishment of this law has received enthusiastic support and support from people of all walks of life and hierarchy, including the institution of monks, which is the national religion.
