7 prisoners in Stung Treng province escaped from prison, police are searching for them
(Stung Treng): Seven inmates in Stung Treng Provincial Prison escaped from the prison at around 3 am on November 8, 2021.
Stung Treng provincial police chief Lt. Gen. Ot Sivutha told Fresh News that his police force was now cooperating with the prison and other border authorities to search for the detainees.
The commissioner confirmed that the prisoners broke through the prison walls and escaped, and that most of them were convicted of drug offenses.
Based on the location, the police found a number of handicraft tools and hard objects that were used to break the stone fence, such as drills, horseshoes, sticks, blankets to block the sound.
Chhun Dara, director of Stung Treng Provincial Prison, said that of the seven inmates, one was sentenced to life in prison for drug trafficking and six others were given minor sentences.
He said that of the seven escaped prisoners, six were in drug trafficking cases and one was convicted of aggravated theft.
