Cambodia identifies 10 potential agricultural products to boost production and exports to make the most of free trade agreements
(Phnom Penh): Based on a study by the working group of the Ministry of Commerce, Cambodia has identified 10 potential commodities to boost production and export in the Free Trade Agreement.
This is according to the results of discussions with the private sector on the strategic document to maximize the implementation of the free trade agreement led by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce on November 5, 2021 via video.
During the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia has continuously integrated its economy into the region and the world.
He said that with the past efforts, Cambodia has successfully completed the negotiation of the first bilateral free trade agreement, the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement on October 12, 2020.
Recently, on October 26, 2021, Cambodia signed the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement. This is the additional emphasis of Minister Pan Sosak.
Minister Pan Sosak emphasized that Cambodia intends to continue to negotiate the establishment of bilateral free trade agreements with other countries such as the European Economic Union, Asia, the Russian Federation, the United Kingdom, the United States, Japan, Mongolia and India.
As for the 10 items, the private sector, which is exporting in the agricultural sector, has expressed its applause and support to take advantage of the free trade agreement. There will be free trade agreements between China, Korea and ASEAN, which will enter into force soon.
However, Duke Song Saran also asked for consideration in adding items as well as secondary fruits such as durian and dragon fruit, which are potential fruits for Cambodia.
Duke Song Saran emphasized, "These 10 items are goods that Cambodia has been making and will be able to enter the market when the FTA enters into force." However, he said that Cambodia also needs a place to process and store properly in accordance with the standards of importing countries.
Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, considers the identification of 10 potential commodities in preparation for the arrival of the FTA and that if Cambodia can successfully export these 10 commodities, other Others, such as fish, meat, poultry (chicken) are all strategic goods that Cambodia can export.
According to the tycoon, what needs to be considered further is how to make Cambodia's agricultural land compatible with irrigation systems, while road and electricity prices are also needed to attract investment.
