The Ministry of Land Management, a sacred new achievement of Cambodian architecture, will be inaugurated tomorrow under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, a sacred new achievement of Cambodian architecture. More than 28 million US dollars will be officially inaugurated on Monday, November 8, 2021 tomorrow. The ceremony will be presided over by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The building of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction is an achievement that demonstrates the values of the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting the value of architecture that is the work of the Khmer children and also shows the ability of the Royal Government to manage and use The national budget to create achievements is a source of pride for the nation as well.
The construction site of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, located in Anlong Kgan Village, Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, northwest of Phnom Penh, was inaugurated on January 28, 2020. The building was completed on March 17, 2021, taking 1 year, 1 month and 20 days.
The building of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction covers an area of 4.5 hectares, with a body size of 132.7 meters long and 94.7 meters wide, with 8 floors, the total height from the sand to the top of the hive 88 .5 meters. The height of the hive is 33.28 meters. There are about 450 parking lots and many motorcycle parking lots.
Office layout works based on functions and usage roles. On the ground floor, there are hospitality halls, restaurants, warehouses, libraries, training centers, OWSOs and Rumduol flower gardens.
The 5th floor has an inter-ministerial meeting hall and the 5th floor, right and left wing, the 6th floor and the 7th floor are offices for rent to the private sector.
As for the roof fittings, there is a 33.28-meter-high Mandap Bosbok representing Mount Sumeru, which has seven floors, representing Phnom Sattariphon, the seven mountains around Phnom Sumeru, Phnom Yukunthor, Phnom Isinthor, Phnom Karvik, Phnom Sots. Phnom Nemin, Phnom Vintak and Phnom Asakna.
The bells on the left and right sides are decorated by Sahasanet or Indra Kong Damrey Ayvorn on the foot of the lion, which is one of the pillars of the East, decorated with elaborate ornaments decorated with ornaments with the face of a dragon. The ornament also represents the harmony between human and natural beliefs that creates happiness and prosperity.
The rectangular building has a shape equal to one-half of the body of Angkor Wat temple, the front and back are divided into 3 Sangkats, the left and right sides are divided into 2 Sangkats and the roof is shaped like letters The "U" extends over the building in all three directions.
On the ground floor, there is a large gate adorned with a statue of Preah Pisnouka or Vishnu, the son of God. The back of the door is decorated with Tep Pranom lanterns adorned with gold leaf on the walls of the reception hall, decorated with carvings of Angkor Wat temples made of copper, size 5 meters by 9 meters.
The building was inscribed with the date of the official inauguration on November 8, 2021 under the high presidency of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
