General Knowledge: Who explored Australia before the Europeans?
There are three main types of people who first explored Australia:
After General Zheng He, there was another Dutch explorer, William Demper, who arrived in Australia in 1697 and recorded the kangaroo for publicity in Europe. At that time, he called this kangaroo animal "a big animal that can jump."
William Dimpier traveled around the world three times, working as a navigator, navigator, sea and air mapmaker, scientific observer, and pirate.
On his way to the South Pacific Ocean from 1768-1771, James Cook encountered a new continent that had never been seen before, and he climbed the continent during the 1770s. . It was then that his fleet met the locals and even fought them fiercely.
After escaping to the United Kingdom, James Cook spread the word about the discovery to the people of Europe, and from then on, the Europeans gradually moved to the new continent and lived for generations. To this day.
