Toxic fumes from burning fabrics emit from the company "Khu Khu" and are affecting the health and living environment of young and old men and women in Lim Chheang Hak Borey, Kantouk Cheung village.
Mr. Nuth Sophea and Ms. Nol Ratha, a representative of about 20 affected families, confirmed on November 5, 2021 that their home is right next to the factory fence, so it is safe to live outside and face the risk of disease. Others, especially young children, because they smell bad almost every day. Speaking of cooking, scraps of cloth from the factory flew through the air into the soup pots.
The representative of the above group added that even the clothes smelled bad, so most of them stayed in the house and did not dare to go out unless necessary. When it comes to cleaning the house, it does not win.
Mr. Nuon Komsan, Deputy Director of O'Dim Primary School, also said that when the "Khu Khu" factory burns the fabric, the children in the class complain that they have difficulty breathing, headache and dizziness due to the toxic smoke.
In the past, school representatives and residents have repeatedly asked for intervention from commune chiefs, district governors, as well as specialized offices, but very few solutions have been accepted.
Therefore, once again, they insist on asking Mr. Khim Sunsoda, Governor of Kampol District, Mr. Keat Rainsy, Director of the Phnom Penh Department of Environment, especially Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, to help the affected people to stop burning the fabric. Because they can not sustain the absorption of toxic odors that emit almost every day.
Authorities split murder case, kill a man and drop him at the mouth of the canal on suspicion of witchcraft, arrest one of the three murderers
(Stung Treng): After a careful investigation, the Stung Treng provincial police force dismantled a case of premeditated murder by killing a man and dumping his body at the mouth of the canal. Police have arrested one of the three killers, who is a brother-in-law, for accusing the victim of witchcraft and killing his father.
A report from the provincial police said that one of the three killers was arrested on November 5, 2021 at Phnom Kambor, Choam Thom village, Koh Sneng commune, Borey O'Svay Sen Chey district.
According to the report, the victim was beaten to death by the three suspects on October 31, 2021 at Phnom Romiet, Koh Ker, Koh Kei village, Koh Sneng commune, Borey Osvay district, Stung Treng province. A case of motorcycle robbery.
Mr. Duong Sivutha, Director of the Office of Serious Crimes of Stung Treng Provincial Police, said on November 6, 2021 that the arrest of the perpetrators was made at Phnom Kambor in Choam Thom village, Koh Sneng commune, district. Borey O'Svay Sen Chey at 15:30 on November 5, 2021.
