Government sets out four priorities to achieve 2030 food system vision
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has demonstrated its commitment and launched a roadmap for a sustainable food system in Cambodia 2030 based on the results of dialogue and analysis on the food system. Link to existing policy frameworks and strategies.
According to the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the 8th National Nutrition Day, which is held annually on November 6, 2021, under the theme "Strengthening the food system for sustainable development."
In a message received by Fresh News on November 6, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to achieve the vision of the food system 2030, which provides food security and nutrition for all people to consider sustainability. Economy, Social Sustainability and Environmental Sustainability The Royal Government has set the following four priorities:
First, the promotion of a healthy diet for all to break the intergenerational cycle of nutrition issues, the Royal Government will continue to work hard to develop in all areas to ensure a healthy diet and safe food available to respond to all nutrition problems. Form.
Third, strengthening resilience of livelihoods and food systems in response to crises and problems that may occur in the future, the Royal Government will continue to work to address vulnerabilities and reduce poverty, strengthen resilience of Stakeholders strengthen employment networks and infrastructure to support livelihoods and food systems.
The Royal Government will continue to support indigenous communities, youth, women, small farmers and small and medium enterprises in the areas of production and food processing to strengthen the livelihoods of rural people to increase resilience. In addition, two-quarters of the Royal Government will continue to use the Cambodian food reserve system, social assistance programs, and implement One-Health to respond to crises.
At the same time, relevant ministries and institutions must continue to strengthen the implementation of existing legal documents and standards related to food safety and quality management and promote the adoption of food safety laws to enhance governance in the food system.
