Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum Sends Condolences on the Death of His Excellency Dr. Nguon Nhel
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, all members of the Senate, and all civil servants of the Senate are deeply saddened and extend their deepest condolences on the death of His Excellency Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly. Died on Friday, November 5, 2021 at 10:36 AM at the age of 79 due to illness.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum emphasized in the condolence message that we all share our condolences with His Excellency and his family for the loss of His Excellency Dr. Nguon Nhel, a pious and pious father. And noble generosity.
The loss of His Excellency Dr. Nguon Nhel is the loss of an outstanding Cambodian political figure with the highest level of competence and experience in building and defending the nation. In particular, His Excellency Dr. Nguon Nhel made a great sacrifice to contribute to the liberation of the motherland and the people of Cambodia from the genocidal regime and rebuild the nation until the development progress in all fields to this day.
Accompanying Samdech Techo to pay their respects to this sad death include Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior, Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Defense, and other senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In a message of condolence sent to the family of the deceased yesterday, Samdech Techo stated that Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen were extremely emotional after receiving the news of Nguon Nhel's death.
Samdech Techo emphasized that the death of Dr. Nguon Nhel was the loss of his father and grandfather, who were social, Brahminical, and inexhaustible. In particular, the death of Mr. Nguon Nhel is also a great loss of a great Cambodian political figure who is full of conscientious will to serve the cause of the nation, nation, religion, the King in all circumstances and has actively contributed to the promotion of the values of The rule of law has many ideals.
