(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, this morning, November 5, 2021, presented the results of the work that the Cambodian Red Cross has achieved for the past two years in contributing to the prevention of the spread of Kovid 19. Through discussions under the theme "The Cambodian Red Cross is responsible for preventing the transmission of Kovid-19 virus."
She added that, of course, as of November 3, 2021, Cambodia had found a total of 118,787 Kovid-19 infected, a total of 115,111 cured and 2,807 dead. According to Samdech Techo, the death rate in Cambodia is higher than in some other countries, so we must continue to strengthen our capacity to treat it.
At the same time, as of October 30, 2021, Cambodia has vaccinated nearly 14 million people aged 6 years and older, equivalent to nearly 86% of the total population of 16 million people, of which vaccinated More than 13 million doses were given in two doses, and nearly 2 million third doses were in the process of vaccinating 5-year-olds.
Key messages were delivered directly to 1,636,772 people (884,083 females) in 12,769 houses / places, in addition to means of outreach through peer educators, mobile friends. In the community, social media, radio and television stations, etc.
According to Ms. Pum Chantyny, the Cambodian Red Cross can achieve the above achievements due to the following key factors:
* First, the Cambodian Red Cross has strong mechanisms and networks, leadership and a high sense of responsibility at all levels - from the middle to the community.
* Second, measures and measures were put in place in a timely manner, along with strengthening the capacity of operators at both the national and sub-national levels, as well as regular monitoring meetings, experience-oriented work.
* Third: There are enough educational materials to disseminate to the community and to educational institutions and towns, as well as to provide alcohol masks, gels, and hand sanitizers. In addition to the community, the Cambodian Red Cross provided educational equipment to prevent Kovid-19 virus, as well as personal protective equipment, sleeping equipment, food, etc. to hospitals, orphanages, associations, and some closed areas.
* Fourth, we also build the capacity of CRC youth volunteer officers through a total of 5 training courses, equal to more than 1,400 people: mental health and social psychology support 3 times and road health courses Psychological and social psychosocial support along with community responsibility twice.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun Appointed Chairman of the Ratanakkiri Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross
(Rattanakiri): On the afternoon of November 5, 2021, the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Ratanakkiri Province held a ceremony to recognize the composition of the Provincial Branch Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, with Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun as the Chairman of the Branch Committee in the fifth mandate.
The meeting was held on the ZOOM system, chaired by Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, with the participation of the two Deputy Secretaries of the Cambodian Red Cross, Branch Committees, Sub-Branch Officers, Head Office, Branch Executives, Red Cross Youth Representatives, a total of 53 people.
As a start, the branch welcomed the activity report and financial report for the first 10 months in 2021. As a follow-up, the First Deputy Secretary General read out the decision on the recognition and revision of the duties and responsibilities of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross. Fifth.
Speaking on this occasion, Ms. Pum Chantyny sent a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the whole ceremony and praised the humanitarian activities of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Ratanakkiri. Respond to vulnerable and vulnerable people in a timely manner.
She instructed the Ratanakkiri Provincial Branch Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, headed by Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, to work hard to help the branch strengthen its ownership in all areas of work and continue to cooperate well with authorities at all levels, departments, national organizations. International in the humanitarian cause to consider the vulnerable and vulnerable people better and better to continue to lead the Red Cross branch in Ratanakkiri in the fifth mandate.
