(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 5, 2021, the Cambodian Red Cross organized a discussion on "Red Cross participates in preventing the transmission of Kovid 19 virus". The discussion was chaired by Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, said that for the past two years, the Cambodian Red Cross, as an assistant to the public authorities, has done a lot of work, especially in the community. For today's discussion, it is like summarizing the work results that the Cambodian Red Cross has achieved.
According to Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, the Cambodian Red Cross has sub-branches in all 25 capitals-provinces to villages and communes, so this discussion can summarize the results of nearly 2 years that they have worked hard. Every day to show the public to participate in the prevention of Kovid 19.
She added that during the discussion, four speakers were selected to give presentations and debates, but that does not mean that only four of them acted.
The first recruitment is from Sihanoukville, the site of the first 19 cases of Kovid, the second is the Cambodian Red Cross Youth in Phnom Penh, and the third is the volunteers in Phnom Penh who have gone through a phase of closure and The center is Cambodia and the fourth is from Koh Thom district, Kandal province, which borders Vietnam.
At the same time, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also mentioned some of the challenges that the Cambodian Red Cross faces when working in the community because Kovid 19 is a deadly infectious disease, but these are not obstacles and Do not hinder the humanitarian activities of the Cambodian Red Cross.
(Phnom Penh): On November 5, 2021, the Press and Quick Reaction Unit of the Office of the Council of Ministers released a new video entitled "Success in the Vaccine Battle is a pillar for the reopening of the country."
Cambodia's most important factor in better control of the disease is the success of the vaccination campaign, which by the end of October 2021, 85.68% of the population of 16 had been vaccinated. And that builds strong community resilience across the country.
Cambodia is one of the largest countries in the world to vaccinate its population against the Covid-19 virus thanks to assistance from friendly and development partners, especially China. Cambodia has made an unexpected difference as Cambodia has higher vaccination rates than some of the richer countries, including the United States and the United Kingdom.
Due to this special point, the social and economic activities of Cambodia can be resumed in a new form of normal life in the context of Kovid-19 disease. Cambodia is commended for its quick, targeted and highly effective response in the fight against the shadowless enemies of the 21st century.
On the other hand, the vaccine is very effective in preventing you from falling seriously ill and dying. In fact, according to the Ministry of Health's daily report on the condition of Kovid-19 in Cambodia, the majority of Kovid-19 deaths are unvaccinated.
The efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia have been helping Cambodia in the past, on the other hand, the vaccine is very effective in preventing people from falling seriously ill and reopening society and the economy, especially in the process of opening up the country. In all areas, faster, safer, stronger and more reliable than many other countries, namely, Cambodia has been leaving the epidemic with confidence and strength.
The Cambodian people are very proud to see their country stand at the top of the list of countries that have succeeded in protecting the lives of their citizens from the devastating epidemic of the century. This is a great honor for the whole Khmer nation. The reopening of the country is a strong hope that the society and economy of Cambodia, as well as the lives of the general Cambodian people will recover quickly under the shadow of peace.
