(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, has ordered the Thmar Puok District Authority to investigate the perpetrators of the land dispute by raising funds from the people to meet with the Cabinet of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Banteay Meanchey Province. Cambodia to resolve the conflict as the Commune / Sangkat Council election season approaches.
The order from Thmar Puok district authorities to open an investigation into the perpetrators by the Banteay Meanchey provincial governor came after information was leaked that a group of criminals had acted to incite 170 families involved in land disputes in Svay village, Thmor Puok commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province, with 14 other families.
They gave two people, Phal Chuot, female, and Sam Vutha, male, to raise more than 10 million riels from 170 families, claiming to meet with Samdech's cabinet. Techo Hun Sen to be released on November 4, 2021 yesterday.
In relation to this issue, Ms. Phal Chuot confirmed to reporters, "Since she and other people do not have any representatives, but the fundraiser is to meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen's cabinet in Phnom Penh, one by one. Some $ 20, some $ 50 because the long journey costs a lot.
He confirmed that 14 families have one order of the Royal Government, which has already been decided and can not be dissolved.
Regarding the above-mentioned chronic land dispute, Mr. Meas Men represented 14 families who came to ask for intervention at Thmar Puok District Hall as they were very unfair because 170 families did not have any documents. Instead, seize their land, even though they already have a legal title.
He revealed that the reason why 170 families always cause rainstorms is because there are brokers behind them. Finally, they requested the district authorities as well as Banteay Meanchey province, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen to intervene. Justice for them, because now the season for farming has arrived. Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany sends a message of deep sadness and condolences on the death of Dr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly
