(Oddar Meanchey): A poor family with a disability living in Trapeang Ampil village, Kork Mon commune, Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province received a house from the Disability Foundation on the afternoon of November 4, 2021.
The disabled man, 46-year-old Wang Sokhoeun, was given a new 4x6-meter house made of galvanized iron by the Disability Foundation to provide him with a decent place to live.
Mr. Sim Sothoun, Director of the Disability Foundation, said that this is the second home for the Disabled People's Fund in Oddar Meanchey province, which the Disabled People's Fund has built for the poor. He said that the budget for the construction of a house came from the donation box of the Disability Fund placed in public places.
The construction of this house is to provide only poor people with disabilities who have an equity or social work card or poverty certificate from the local authority and meet the criteria in accordance with the principle of providing housing for the poor with disabilities in the community of the Disability Fund. He also instructed the families of people with disabilities to take care of this new house for a long time and to take care of their health and avoid any infectious diseases.
The representative of the Kork Mon commune administration thanked the disability fund for building a house for the poor in Kouk Mon commune, which really helped to reduce the poverty and misery of his family.
During the event, the Disability Foundation also donated 100,000 Riels to the families who received a new house, 25 kg of rice under 2 sticks, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish sauce. 2 packets of salt and 1 box of noodles.
