Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the results of a seminar on disseminating the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Council for the Development of Cambodia have organized a video workshop to disseminate the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Cambodian government officials and diplomats at Cambodian embassies abroad. All.
The workshop was held on November 3, 2021 under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, with the participation of Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council. Development of Cambodia.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon praised the leadership and working group of the Council for the Development of Cambodia for its six years of study, research and drafting of the Investment Law. Recently appeared.
The Deputy Prime Minister also highlighted the negative consequences of the Kovid-19 crisis and the trade war, which significantly reduced the global economy and foreign direct investment flows around the world. Powers that alter international order have also put pressure on the Asia-Pacific region and undermined ASEAN's centrality and solidarity and the region's relations with external partners.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that the new investment law will play an important role in implementing the economic diplomacy strategy 2021-2023 more effectively and successfully through all Cambodian embassies abroad, which are the staff of the Ministry. CPR in recruiting new potential investment partners to come to Cambodia.
