One of Cambodia's leading pharmaceutical companies can export medicines to 15 countries and improve the well-being of local people
(Phnom Penh): PPM Pharmaceuticals, the first pharmaceutical enterprise in Cambodia, is capable of producing and exporting millions of dollars worth of medicines to foreign markets each year and supplying the domestic market. This one brings welfare independence for Cambodia.
Dr. Hay Li Eang, founder of PPM Pharmaceuticals, said that almost half of the pharmaceutical products were exported to 15 countries, including neighboring countries and countries in Africa, especially countries. Developing.
He said that for 25 years, this Cambodian enterprise has been able to stand and have a good reputation in the country, the region and the world, and through the export of this medicine, PPM has also contributed to the independence of medicine. Cambodia as well.
"Not only can we provide medicine for our country or food for our country, we can export to other neighboring countries, so we can leave the state of starvation without food, come to prosperity and compete," he said. "With other countries abroad in all areas, we are strengthening our independence."
Despite the fact that Cambodia is facing an epidemic of Kovid 19, PPM continues to supply medicines for Cambodians as well as at fixed prices, as medicines are essential for the health of all Cambodians. That Cambodia is independent in terms of well-being. To date, PPM Pharmaceuticals has about 200 products, while there are 50 products for export.
PPM Pharmaceutical Enterprise was established in 1996 as a symbol of the revival of the national pharmaceutical industry, which was devastated after the civil war and the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Prior to the presence of PPM in the Cambodian market, only imported drugs were often overpriced for the majority of Cambodians, or otherwise, only counterfeit drugs were harmful to public health. Therefore, Cambodia must seek independence in public health in order to make medicines manufactured in accordance with international standards affordable.
