(Phnom Penh): The 9th and 5th Committees of the National Assembly on the morning of November 4, 2021, held a discussion on the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN Protocol on Strengthening Dispute Resolution Mechanisms. The discussion was chaired by Ms. Nin Saphon, Chair of the Ninth Commission, and was attended by members of the National Assembly from both specialized committees.
During the discussion, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led a delegation from the Ministry of Commerce to defend the draft law.
Ms. Nin Saphon welcomed and thanked the representatives of the Royal Government led by Mr. Pan Sosak and informed the meeting about the report of the results of the expert committee on this draft law and fully agreed on the draft law on the approval of the protocol. ASEAN on Strengthening Dispute Resolution Mechanisms.
In addition, as chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia demonstrates Cambodia's commitment and significant contribution to strengthening the dispute resolution mechanism within the ASEAN framework, using the ASEAN Coverage Agreements ratified by the institutions. The legislature is already the basis.
(Beijing): "Supporting the multilateral consensus", "Focus on practical implementation", "Accelerate the transformation of the green formula" are three points on the issue of climate change, said Chinese President Xi Jinping. In a written address at the 26th Summit of the Leaders of the Signatories to the "United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change" on 1 November 2021.
As the summit opens on the same day, the World Meteorological Organization released a report stating that the last seven years of 2021 will be the hottest seven years. Since there is a record. The data show that greenhouse gas concentrations will reach a record high in 2020, but will continue to rise in 2021.
Will the response to climate change affect economic development? Xi Jinping called for "accelerating the transformation of green magic" to promote green economic and social development through innovation. The proposal embraces the general trends of current scientific and technological development and is a summary of China's experience of successfully implementing the concept of "green mountains, clean water, mountains of gold, mountains of silver."
In the past 10 years, China has eliminated 120 million kilowatts of coal-fired power plants. China has recently launched a number of projects and measures to establish a policy system for carbon offsets and "1 plus N" carbon neutrality. China has also promised not to build coal-fired power plants abroad.
Responding to climate change as a global challenge requires the whole world to operate together. Do not talk and plan but do not practice, there is a better action than planning but not implementing. In response to climate change, it is important to take practical action.
