Legislation to determine the "single Khmer nationality" for the leaders of the top institutions of the four nations is another new historical event in the history of Cambodia that has not been mentioned since the inception of the Constitution. However, the establishment of this law has received enthusiastic support and support from people from all walks of life and hierarchy, including the institution of monks, which is the national religion.
The Cambodian people applauded seeing that such a determination was a guarantee of the highest protection of the interests of the nation and the people of Cambodia through the leaders of these four top national institutions. Meanchey National University Research Report: Increasing Tariffs on Tobacco Products in Cambodia Reduces Smoking
(Phnom Penh): Meanchey National University has released a research report stating that the increase in tariffs on tobacco products in Cambodia is part of encouraging smokers to change their decision to quit or reduce smoking. Smoking.
Today's information systems are more diverse, so access to information and knowledge is wider. According to the survey, almost 99% of the population is aware of the dangers and effects of smoking on both health and society. For the people who support the tax increase, they want to increase the tax to 62% of the retail price, more than double the current tax rate.
Raising cigarette prices is part of encouraging smokers to change their decision to quit or reduce smoking. Surveys show that more than half of smokers will decide to quit in the event that the price of cigarettes increases up to four times compared to the last purchase price of 3,000 riel / pack.
