Residents of Bak Kheng Leu village said that the slaughterhouse (Cattle slaughterhouse) at Spean Leang 6, Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, was causing serious damage to the surrounding environment, and residents were thumbprinted to insist that Sangkat authorities intervened, while the Chroy Changvar district administration had instructed the owners to find a suitable new location without renewing the permit.
According to residents and traders, the slaughterhouse is located at the mouth of the canal north of the sixth bridge in Bak Kheng Leu village, where the owner, Sen Kriya, a Cambodian Muslim, slaughtered hundreds of cattle a day. The head then drains the flesh-like waste into the ditch. Apart from that, all around the village, there are cattle breeding ponds, the whole village stinks and flows into the canals, causing the water to stink and become unusable.
Residents further stated that in the past, Sen Kriya's cattle slaughterhouse did not have a permit to drop cows because the Chroy Changva district court repealed the old law not to continue the business.
In this case, if it really happened in the area of his slaughterhouse, the Chroy Changvar district administration would like to advise to stop this activity immediately.
At the same time, on August 27, 2021, the Chroy Changvar District Administration issued a letter rejecting the request for permission to continue the establishment of a cattle and slaughterhouse in Bak Kheng Leu Village, Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
The district administration confirmed that the administration could not sign the transfer because the location was close to the nursery, living near the Victory Monument, near the Moradok Techo Stadium, which affected the living environment of the nearby residents and the surrounding area.
Despite the lack of permission from the authorities, the above slaughterhouse business activities continue to this day. Driving cattle at high speeds and killing cattle in the early morning is always noisy, causing resentment and raising concerns in all public forums and proposing new locations. . However, Senkriya's position is still operating normally, unconcerned.
Poll results: Respect for democracy in the United States is declining globally
A survey by the Pew Research Center surveyed more than 16,000 participants from 16 advanced economies and more than 2,500 from the United States in February. Pew is a non-profit research center based in Washington, DC.
The results showed that 57 percent of respondents worldwide said that US democracy "used to be a good example, but it has been declining in recent years" while 72 percent More of the respondents across the United States expressed similar views.
"Very few people believe that US democracy today is a good example for other countries, and most of them have expressed" grave concern "about discrimination, the report said. "Ethnicity in the United States."
"Between 82% and 95% of respondents outside the United States believe that racism is a serious problem and at least 4 out of 10 call it a serious problem," the report said. At last. ”
