Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon: The new investment law will be an effective and timely tool for socio-economic recovery after the Kovid 19 crisis
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, expressed his firm belief that the promulgation of the new investment law will be an important, effective and timely tool for the restoration of Socio-economic after-crisis Kovid-19 and make Cambodia an attractive destination for investors.
Mr. Prak Sokhon made this statement during a video workshop to disseminate the new Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia to all Cambodian missions abroad and the leaders of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation this morning. November 3, 2021.
Organized this workshop organized by the Council for the Development of Cambodia in collaboration with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation with about 170 participants.
This investment law was drafted in accordance with the guidelines of the Cambodian Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 and has undergone a rigorous study and development by the working group of the Council for the Development of Cambodia from 2015 until its completion. At the end of the first half of 2019, in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum on March 29, 2019.
This investment law is designed to create an open, transparent, predictable and favorable legal framework that can attract and promote quality, efficient and effective investment in Cambodia for social development. - Economy.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon praised and commended the leadership and staff of the Council for the Development of Cambodia for their six years of study, research and drafting of the new Investment Law.
The Deputy Prime Minister also highlighted the negative consequences of the Kovid-19 crisis and the trade war, which significantly reduced the global economy and foreign direct investment flows around the world, as well as power struggles. Of superpowers that are altering international order and putting pressure on the Asia-Pacific region and undermining ASEAN centrality and solidarity and the region's relations with external partners.
However, the Deputy Prime Minister strongly believes that the promulgation of this investment law will be an important, effective and timely tool for the socio-economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis and make Cambodia It is an attractive destination for investors as the Royal Government decides to gradually re-launch economic and national activities to welcome foreign investors and tourists, especially vaccine tourism.
Regarding the vaccination issue, Mr. Prak Sokhon also highlighted the successful vaccination campaign of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which vaccinated its people about 28 million doses, equivalent to more than 86% of the total population. Cambodia has become the number one country in ASEAN and the Asia-Pacific and the sixth largest in the world for vaccinating the population.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, expressed his deep gratitude for the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, who has been instrumental in disseminating the investment law to Cambodian diplomats. Overseas diplomatic missions, a sharp strategy to highlight opportunities in Cambodia to attract more quality investment.
In addition, the Minister highly appreciated the regular cooperation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Cambodian diplomatic missions abroad, which have always contributed significantly to the promotion of investment and promotion of the investment environment in Cambodia. To foreign investors.
