Cambodia to host East Asia Sea Summit in early December 2021 in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is scheduled to host the East Asia Sea Summit in late 2021 in Sihanoukville, which will be Cambodia's first major event after reopening the country in early November after the outbreak. By Kovid 19.
The East Asia Sea Summit 2021 in Cambodia will also take place with the 7th Ministerial Forum of the East Asia Maritime Environment Management Partnership in Sihanoukville. The East Asia Sea Conference 2021 focuses on the sustainable development of the world's oceans.
More than 10 countries from around the world will participate in the forum: China, Japan, the Republic of Korea and many more.
The East Asia Sea Summit in late 2021 is being held in Sihanoukville, which has some of the most beautiful beaches in the world and is now becoming Cambodia's model multi-purpose economic zone, and the city will become a multinational development city.
According to the program of the East Asia Maritime Conference 2021 received from the Ministry of Environment, this maritime conference will share lessons and experiences for the sustainability of coastal and marine environment, as well as jointly establish and reorganize management mechanisms. And set out a clear roadmap for solutions to maritime issues for the coming decade.
The General Assembly is an opportunity for Cambodia to show its contribution to addressing regional and international challenges, along with a high commitment to environmental management and sustainable development. At the same time, it is an opportunity to establish and reorganize existing management mechanisms and promote new opportunities for regional partnerships through innovative technologies, investment and financing to sustain the coastal and marine environment.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has agreed in principle to allow the Ministry of Environment to host the East Asia Sea Conference 2021 and the 7th Ministerial Forum on Partnership in East Asia Marine Environment Management for two days from December 1-2, in Sihanoukville, online and face-to-face meetings following health rules.
