(Phnom Penh): Mr. Oknha Hang Sokun, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Agricultural Community Coalition, signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Mr. Kem Rath Viseth, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Civil Society Forum (CSF). Support and promote the agricultural sector in rural areas in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to reduce poverty in rural areas.
The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding was held this morning, November 3, 2021 at the Phnom Penh Hotel, with the participation of members of the Civil Society Alliance Forum, as well as many members of the Board of the Cambodian Agricultural Community Coalition.
Mr. Oknha Hang Sokun stated that the Memorandum of Understanding is focused on promoting the research of the two institutions to contribute to the development of the agricultural sector in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government to contribute to reducing rural poverty and Achieve the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals 2030 in Cambodia.
Mr. Oknha Hang Sokun added that in order to achieve this goal, the parties will have to cooperate based on the principles of equality, respect and mutual benefit to the extent that: sharing information and experiences related to management and Agricultural community development, strengthening and expanding the capacity of agricultural communities and agricultural community unions through training and education on relevant policies and techniques.
Joint study and implementation of joint projects within the framework of supporting the farming community, cooperation in finding national and international development partners to support the development of agricultural communities in Cambodia, and co-organizing research, conferences, workshops, trainings and discussions. Roundtable for the purpose of promoting and strengthening the role of civil society and agricultural communities in participating in socio-economic development.
Mr. Kem Rathviseth stated that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on the Forum of Civil Society Coalition will act as a facilitator and link civil society organizations as national and international partners with the Coalition of Cambodian Agricultural Communities to help discuss and Exchange ideas by exploring the possibility of finding specific cooperation with each other to jointly assist the agricultural sector.
Mr. Kem Rathviseth added that among the international cooperation partners with the Civil Society Forum, Chinese civil society organizations have expressed many goals in cooperation with civil society organizations in Cambodia. Chinese civil friends who wish to cooperate in the field of agriculture to cooperate with the Alliance of Cambodian Agricultural Communities to help the agricultural sector in Cambodia to grow.
