(Koh Kong): It is planned that Darasakor International Airport, Koh Kong Province will be able to open a test run in December 2021, but due to some delays, this international airport has been postponed until the end of the first quarter of 2022. Face.
This was confirmed by Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, told Fresh News on November 3, 2021.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha confirmed that, in fact, the construction of Darasakor International Airport, Koh Kong Province is scheduled to be completed by the end of October and is scheduled to open in December 2021, but now the trial process has been postponed until early 2022. Or in the first quarter of 2022.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha confirmed that the delay in launching the test was due to the latest inspection by the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
* First, there is some work that the company still needs more time to complete, such as providing information and safety-related documents before the Civil Aviation issues official certification and publicity.
* Second: There was a moderate outbreak of Kovid-19 in the construction site after Pchum Ben, so the construction process was delayed for almost a month.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha said, "The construction company is ready, but according to the inspection and evaluation of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, he may need a little more time to launch a test operation. "So the plan to open at the end of December will be moved to the beginning of next year at the end of the first quarter."
