Minister Thong Khon: Russia supports Cambodia's vaccination tourism strategy and will arrange for people to visit soon
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on November 2, 2021, met with Mr. Anatoly Borovic, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Russian Federation to Cambodia at the Russian Embassy to expand tourism cooperation. Of both countries.
The meeting also aims to re-arrange the return of Russian tourists to Cambodia under the vaccine tourism strategy that the Royal Government has recently announced, especially the opening of safe target areas such as Sihanoukville, Koh Rong and Darasakor. From November 31, 2021 and Siem Reap Angkor during January 2022.
In this meeting, Minister Thong Khon reminded about the support for the development of Cambodia from the people and the Russian government since the liberation of the country from the Pol Pot regime, as well as the process of finding peace in Cambodia by participating as a signatory to the peace agreement. Paris.
He added that recently, President Putin also presented a Medal of Honor to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, expressing his appreciation for the leadership of Samdech Techo to achieve the current peace and prosperity as well as the work. Strive to strengthen and expand friendly diplomatic cooperation with Russia.
The Minister emphasized that under the wise and prudent leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has made progress in vaccination, which is the key to restoring the confidence and credibility of economic and social activities in the context of normalcy. Recently, the tourism sector is also preparing to open in responsible steps.
The two sides also agreed to expand cooperation in the field of tourism and put forward plans to welcome Russian tourists within the framework of Cambodia's vaccine tourism strategy, such as:
First, arrange for a visit by Russian tour companies and Russian media (Farm Trip) in the near future to promote the readiness to receive international tourists.
Second, invite Russian tour companies to participate in a small and manageable exhibition on the occasion of ASEAN Tourism Day 2022 in January from 16 to 22 to meet business with Cambodian tourists as well as local companies.
Third: Organize a tourism business seminar between the two countries.
Fourth: Prepare to promote direct flights between Cambodia and Russia in the future.
Fifth, to organize the program 2022 as the year of tourism and culture between Cambodia and Russia to celebrate the 66th anniversary of the two countries' diplomatic ties.
Sixth, to review and prepare the Cambodia-Russia Joint Work Program on Tourism through the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Cambodia-Russia Tourism Cooperation.
Seventh, expand cooperation on tourism promotion, product development, investment and human resource development.
Ninth: Support the training of Russian-speaking coastal guides.
According to Minister Thong Khon, based on the historical friendship and achievements of the past, Cambodia will be able to attract more Russian tourists. That number could rise further, with Russia being a huge market with a population of more than 146 million.
The Ambassador also thanked the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia for hosting the upcoming ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022 and chairing the 25th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting and related meetings for facilitating the ASEAN Tourism Summit. Russia to the ministerial level, the first meeting will be held on the occasion of the upcoming ASEAN Tourism Forum.
