(Phnom Penh): US investors have expressed optimism about investing in Cambodia, and they will continue to expand their investments and businesses to contribute to the recovery of Cambodia's economy, which has been plagued by Kovid 19.
The meeting between the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and a delegation from the US-ASEAN Business Council was held to strengthen trade relations and promote investment from the United States.
The Minister of Commerce highlighted some of the favorable environment in Cambodia, which is a good opportunity for investment in Cambodia. The investment climate that the Minister mentioned is the success of the successful vaccination of 19 people and the readiness of Cambodia to reopen economic and social activities.
The Minister also mentioned the potential for bilateral trade between Cambodia and the United States, which has continued to grow despite the 19 Kovid Crisis. In the first eight months of 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States amounted to more than 5.5 billion US dollars, an increase of 28.46 percent compared to 2020.
The Minister of Commerce encourages and continues to support the coordination of US companies with any requests and questions can contact the Ministry of Commerce or His Excellency directly to resolve and coordinate with relevant ministries and institutions.
In response, the Ambassador congratulated Cambodia on its success in vaccinating and reopening socio-economic activities. US companies have also expressed optimism about investing in Cambodia and pledged to expand their business in Cambodia. In particular, support for the economic recovery of Cambodia after the end of Kovid-19 and support for Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN in 2022.
The US-ASEAN Business Council delegation thanked the Minister for his continued care, coordination and cooperation with the US-ASEAN Business Council delegation in Cambodia.
Minister Pan Sosak expressed his appreciation and gratitude to the US-ASEAN Business Council delegation and company representatives who took the time to attend the meeting. The Minister also expressed optimism and hoped that all companies would continue to invest and expand their business in Cambodia. Kampot Provincial Governor Attends the Funeral of 7 People Who Met with a Traffic Accident in Dang Tong District
(Kampot): The Governor of Kampot Province, Mr. Mao Thunin, on the evening of November 2, 2021, ordered the authorities to transport the bodies of the seven victims to a traditional ceremony after the victims of a car accident in the district. Flagpole this afternoon.
The provincial governor attended the funeral for 500,000 riel, 150 kg of rice and many other food items.
It should be noted that at least 7 people died in a car accident on Street 41 in Laang village, Laang commune, Dang Tong district, Kampot province on the afternoon of November 2, 2021.
According to Fresh News, the victim's car was traveling from east to west at high speed, causing the car to overturn into a ditch, killing all seven people in it. Died all at once.
The victims who died in the accident were four men, three women and a girl. The identities of the seven victims remain unknown.
According to the commissioner, the accident was caused by a flat tire and overturned in the water. In addition to expressing his condolences to the families of the victims, the commissioner-general ordered troops to intervene immediately at the scene.
Phnom Penh Governor Orders 14 Khan Authorities and Armed Forces to Strictly Apply for Karaoke and Entertainment Club Not to Reopen
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, has issued an order to all 14 district authorities and all armed forces to strictly enforce measures to ban the operation of karaoke and entertainment clubs in Phnom Penh.
The regulation was made at a meeting on the promotion of Kovid 19 vaccine to the people in Phnom Penh to provide all the people in Phnom Penh who need the Kovid 19 vaccine in both basic and local doses. Dose boosted by video and audio conferencing (Video Conference) on the evening of November 2, 2021.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the government has reopened the country in all areas, but clubs and karaoke are not yet allowed to open, that is, only restaurants and beer gardens. Therefore, the 14 district authorities and the relevant forces must take strict action against the theft of clubs and karaoke, as these two locations have the highest risk of spreading Kovid-19 disease.
With the re-establishment of the country, Mr. Khuong Sreng also urged all district authorities and relevant forces to maintain good order, especially the preparation of sidewalks, waste management, because the opening To get the country back on track, it will return to normal traffic congestion, which is a challenge that we need to address better.
