Afghanistan: At least 15 people have been killed in an explosion and gunfire at a hospital in Kabul.
At least 15 people have been killed and 34 others injured in two blasts and gunfire at Afghanistan's largest military hospital in Kabul. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, November 2, 2021.
The official death toll has not been confirmed, but a Taliban security official said on condition of anonymity that at least 15 people had been killed and 34 wounded.
No group has so far claimed responsibility for the attack, but since the Taliban took control of Afghanistan, ISIS has carried out a series of attacks on mosques. And other goals.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX), said that in 2022, the Cambodia Securities Exchange expects many companies to list on the Stock Exchange due to The company that intends to enter the stock market failed in 2021, so the company will rush to register in 2022.
He claimed that the company expects a lot of growth to enter the Cambodian Stock Exchange as private companies begin to change their lives to live with the new Kovid 19 disease, the Royal Government of Cambodia recently announced the reopening of the country. Therefore, local and foreign companies that were previously difficult to travel will gradually return to a better position and thus the issuance of securities will be easier.
Speaking to Fresh News on November 2, 2021, Mr. Hong Sochua added that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been opening up the country for economic tourism, so expect all businesses to improve for businesses that continue to survive. It is now a very strong business.
"In 2021, many companies are late to list on the stock exchange because by 2020, businesses will be affected by Kovid 19, so some businesses planning to list on the stock exchange this year have postponed to next year," he said. "Because next year, many companies are expected to list on the stock exchange."
"In 2021, some business conditions have improved, so in 2022, the business value of companies will be better, which will allow business owners to get a good price and can decide to register to raise additional capital," he added.
He stated that in 2020, the Stock Exchange of Cambodia received 5 companies to list and sell securities, and in 2021 so far received 2 companies listed, but from now until the end of the year is expected to receive. Three more companies have been licensed, while one has already been licensed.
He added that in 2021, in addition to listed companies, if you look at the trading companies, there is a significant increase compared to previous years, the opening of trading accounts, market participation has increased more than before. These show the future advancement of the Cambodian securities sector.
