Be careful, you like to drive fast! Authorities Start Installing Automatic Speed Cameras on National Road 3
(Phnom Penh): Authorities have started installing automatic speed cameras on National Road 3 to prevent speeding, which is one of the main causes of traffic accidents and claiming the lives of people almost every day.
The 135-kilometer stretch of National Road 3 from Phnom Penh to Kampot has been almost completely completed and is now almost four years old. This stretch of road is upgraded to AC concrete. This section of road from Choam Chao, Phnom Penh to Bek Kus, Takeo Province has been widened to more than 24 meters, divided into 4 lanes, while Bek Kus to Kampot has been widened to 12 meters, divided into 2 lanes.
Currently, this section of road is becoming a busy road for people to travel between Phnom Penh and the coastal provinces in the southwest, as well as travel to Takeo and Kampong Speu.
Heang Sotheayut, spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, told Fresh News that the installation of the speed limit camera was an initiative of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, with the approval of Deputy Prime Minister Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng. Ministry of Interior.
He added that the card establishes an automated mechanism for monitoring the speed of drivers on this public road to implement education and fines in accordance with sub-decrees and regulations, based on reports from the basic system. This is also a mechanism to reduce the use of police force to use a small but highly effective recommendation of Samdech Krala Hom, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior.
Accident reports often indicate that speeding is a major cause of road accidents and fatalities on the road. In the first nine months of 2021, there were 1,888 road accidents, 36% of which were caused by speeding and 457 passengers were killed due to speeding.
Mr. Heang Sotheayut confirmed that the automatic speed camera is almost installed and may be launched soon.
According to the young spokesman, who is friendly with the reporter, the automatic speed camera can detect the speed of the car and the data of the car, then send the information and data to the General Control Center. National Police Commission. According to this information and data, the traffic police force can fine the owners of vehicles that violate the speed limit.
In particular, the speed of driving is in accordance with the law and sub-decree on land traffic of the Kingdom of Cambodia. For the city is able to drive at a minimum speed of about 40 kilometers per hour. The maximum speed can be as high as 90 km / h outside the city for light cars and passenger cars, and for 4 lanes (2 lanes to 2 lanes), there is a divider in the middle lane and in the absence of Speed limit badge.
Sub-Decree on Transitional Fines 2020 stipulates that drivers of motorcycles or trailers, trailers or tricycles or four-wheeled motorbikes for speeding from 1 to 19 km / h shall be fined 60,000 Riels and 100,000 Riels for Driving above the speed limit of 30 to 39 kilometers per hour.
In particular, if you drive faster than the speed limit of 30 to 39 kilometers per hour, you will be fined 180,000 riels for light vehicles and 375,000 riels for heavy vehicles.
