Joe Biden's remarks refer to the withdrawal from the 2015 Paris Climate Agreement by former administration Donald Trump, which was formally signed in November 2020. In retaliation, as President of the United States, a key player in this goal, Joe Biden has pledged to further reduce greenhouse gas emissions.
In mid-2017, Donald Trump announced plans to pull the United States out of the Paris Climate Agreement, which was difficult to establish under former President Barack Obama. The withdrawal is for the reason that Mr. Trump himself claimed that it was an agreement that put the United States at a disadvantage and seriously affected the economy because of the killing of American jobs.
However, during his presidency, the president promised that the fight against climate change would only boost economic growth, not harm it. Joe Biden stressed that his administration "will act, not just speak."
Participating officials who attended the COP26 conference expressed support for the promise to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by 2030, but they were surprised by India's 2070 target. However, they still hope that India will follow this plan. Sihanoukville launches Kovid 19 vaccine for 5-year-olds from November 2-6.
