The Taliban (GDI) has launched a successful operation to capture two major armed robbers in the capital, Kabul. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday evening, November 1, 2021.
According to the GDI, the two big thieves were arrested from two areas in the capital Kabul on Monday and were involved in armed robberies and the use of force to rob. Cars and valuables from local homes. Weapons and some vehicles were also confiscated.
The Taliban have been in control of Afghanistan for two and a half months since taking control of Kabul on August 15, 2021. The main issues that the Taliban interim government has been trying to address are fighting terrorism, maintaining security in cities and provinces, mobilizing foreign aid, and especially seeking international recognition.
