China replenishes green momentum for Cambodia's development
The Chinese side encouraged Chinese enterprises to continue to increase cooperation in the energy sector with the Cambodian side and to promote the improvement of industrial structure to jointly promote the green and sustainable restoration of the global economy.
Since 2007, in response to the shortage of electricity supply, the Royal Government of Cambodia has actively implemented the priority power development strategy to fully promote the construction of the power sector. Chinese enterprises have been actively involved in the development of Cambodia's electricity, as well as pushing for Cambodia's energy transformation into a green development formula.
By the end of 2020, Chinese enterprises have built and commissioned 10 hydropower stations, one coal-fired power plant and two heavy-duty gas-fired power stations. Installation volume over 70%
Of the total increase in the volume of electricity throughout Cambodia, the volume of electricity generation will be 80.3% of the total amount of electricity installed in 2020.
