(Sihanoukville): In preparation for the opening of the first phase of the vaccine for tourists at the end of November to be highly effective for safe tourism destinations, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group And the private sector to rehabilitate and promote tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis.
Mr. Thong Khon issued such recommendations this morning, November 1, 2021, on the occasion of presiding over the dissemination meeting on the preparation of Sihanoukville, Koh Rong and Darasakor as a destination for vaccination tourism held in Sokha Hotel, Preah Sihanouk Province, with the participation of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, relevant officials and the private sector.
Minister Thong Khon's six recommendations include:
First, request the Secretariat for urgent cooperation with the administration of Sihanoukville and Koh Kong provinces to appoint a joint working group to start work from now on. The Joint Task Force will act as a hub for information gathering and decision-making in the safety zones identified by the "Vaccine Tourism Strategic Plan".
Second, to request the management of statistics and identity of passengers entering and leaving the target safety area as a core task and to set up a management system with technology.
Third, request the two provincial administrations to pay more attention to the implementation of the criteria of "Clean City Standards", especially the indicators related to cleanliness, sanitation and waste management.
Fourth, request the two provincial administrations to study the possibility of additional air connections, both naval and land connections, especially the connection between one safe area to another safe area. "Sihanoukville - Koh Rong - Darasakor.
Fifth, request the two provincial administrations to pay attention to encourage tour operators under their capacity to implement consistently and better tourism safety rules and procedures, minimum standards in the tourism sector and to monitor Businesses in the provinces that have not yet implemented the Tourism Safety Rules (SOP) need to strengthen the location and request for tourism safety labels before allowing them to continue operating.
Sixth: Request a weekly follow-up meeting in which the person in charge of each plan should update their work on a regular basis.
The Minister added that for international tourists from abroad must travel by plane to Sihanoukville or connect flights from Phnom Penh, which ensures safety for vaccinated tourists, including the movement from the destination safely to Sihanoukville. Koh Rong and Darasakor or to other safe island destinations in the province must travel by ship for the provincial administration to control.
For tourist travel documents, the vaccine is very convenient, you just need to show the vaccination card, test documents 72 hours before arriving in Cambodia. Upon arrival in Cambodia, the rapid test must be repeated to confirm. In the event of a negative case, tourists are free to stay and relax in a safe area for 5 days, but are also required to take the PCR test again on the 4th day, 1 day before departure. Safe areas to other destinations in the country or abroad.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun and Ms. Mithona Phuthong announced their support for the Royal Government's decision to accept the vaccine and pledged to work to strengthen the order in the province with the management of all relevant officials. All are ready to ensure that in case any problems occur immediately can be resolved in time as well.
Public Administration Regulator Explains Dispute Resolution in Public Administration!
(Phnom Penh): In order to contribute to increase the knowledge of the public, the public administration regulator has prepared an article explaining the resolution of disputes in the field of public administration.
Disputes related to the operation of the civil service in the Kingdom of Cambodia shall be resolved by the Administrative Dispute Resolution Council of the Administrative Regulatory Authority (NRA), unless otherwise specified by the relevant regulator.
The decision of the Dispute Resolution Council is the subject of an administrative complaint or appeal to the competent court within 30 (thirty) days from the date of the decision.
The organization and functioning of the Dispute Resolution Council shall be determined by a Prakas of the Minister of Economy and Finance and the Chairman of the Council of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority at the request of the NBTC (Law on Public Administration 2019 Law). On the Organization and Functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority 2021, Sub-Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Sub-Unit of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority 2021).
