The results make Cambodia the number one country in Southeast Asia and one of the most vaccinated countries in the world. This result is a source of pride for Cambodia and also highly appreciated by the national and international community for the operation of the Royal Government and its stakeholders.
The results of vaccination against Kovid 19, which Cambodia has achieved so well, are seen as dependent on a number of key factors, such as the management of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, cooperation between relevant authorities, citizen participation and Cooperation between Cambodia and the international arena as well.
However, the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Supreme Commander of the Battle of Kovid 19 is seen as the most important factor leading to the success of control of Kovid 19. For example, vaccination against Kovid 19. In many countries so far, 19 cases of Kovid vaccination have been largely achieved due to the wrong decisions or delays of the leaders of those countries.
In Cambodia, during the initial vaccination process, there was a lot of controversy because the Prime Minister decided to use the Sinofam vaccine, which has not yet been announced by the World Health Organization. This has led to criticism and advice from civil society organizations and opposition groups.
At that time, if Samdech Techo Hun Sen decides to follow those suggestions, it will definitely affect the vaccination policy and Cambodia will not have vaccines given to the people in time.
