Cambodia, as well as other countries in the world, suffered a severe 19 outbreaks of Kovid after the "Community Infectious Diseases 20" event. The Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has launched a fierce battle against the epidemic, which is considered by Samdech Techo to be a shadowless enemy to protect the lives of the people.
A series of measures have been put in place to prevent the spread and spread of disease through health measures, such as closing the epidemic, closing businesses unnecessarily, closing cross-border travel and encouraging people to take preventive measures. Do not 3 protect. In addition to efforts to prevent the spread of the disease, efforts to identify and treat the dead are also a major effort of the Royal Government.
The team of doctors, nicknamed the "White Army", together with the armed forces and relevant authorities, worked tirelessly under the joint command of the Commander-in-Chief on the battlefield of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to prevent the spread of the disease. And the death of citizens.
Along with the military strategy to prevent the transmission and treatment of citizens, Commander-in-Chief Techo Sen also launched a campaign to vaccinate against 19 Kovid, which is a necessary military strategy to win the battle of Kovid 19.
On February 10, Samdech Techo Hun Sen launched the 199 Kovid vaccination campaign with about 600,000 doses of Sinofam vaccine, the first aid from the Chinese government and people to Cambodia.
The speed of vaccination is a determining factor for the success or failure of the fight against Kovid 19, which is like a battle on the battlefield. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the leader who was soaked on the battlefield in the conflict in Cambodia in the past, decided to go to war with Kovid 19, not unlike the armed war in the past.
In addition to planning the vaccination, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also used both cold and hot politics to encourage people to get vaccinated against Kovid 19 because the initial vaccination, people seem reluctant to get the vaccine.
In order to achieve the Kovid 19 vaccination plan, it is not enough to have a good plan for vaccinating the people if Cambodia does not find the vaccine according to its plan. Therefore, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also set out some necessary tactics to seek the vaccine against Kovid 19.
Regarding the search for the vaccine, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has stated that Samdech Techo is not the commander who sent troops into the battlefield, lacks weapons for battle, and if he enters the battlefield, he will be defeated. Based on this spirit, Samdech Techo also decided to use China as a strategic reference in the supply of vaccines.
As a result, Cambodia ranks first in Southeast Asia and one of the world's most vaccinated countries.
The results of Cambodia's vaccination have also improved the situation in Cambodia for the management of 19 cases of Kovid, with a steady decline in the rate of infection, opening up a wider range of social activities and enabling Cambodia. Decided to open to receive vaccinated tourists as well.
Achieving this vaccination plan, not only the Cambodian people applauded and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his efforts, but also the representatives of UNICEF and World Health in Cambodia highly appreciated this success.
UNICEF Representative in Cambodia, Ms. Furog Fu Yozat, emphasized that "the Royal Government of Cambodia has led the fight against Kovid-19 as well as the provision of vaccines to the people is commendable and the Royal Government of Cambodia is at a high level. "One that can be done is eight months ahead of schedule."
"Cambodia has done a great job in the fight against Kovid 19 and the provision of vaccines to the people," said Ly Itpen, WHO director for Cambodia. Cambodia is one of the leading countries in the World Health Organization (WHO) in the Asia-Pacific region in providing vaccines to the people. "Especially for vulnerable groups as well as front-line teams."
