Analysis: China has always been a practitioner of civilization, ecology and climate governance.
BEIJING: The Chinese government recently released a white paper entitled "China's Climate Change Policy and Operations". This is the second time the Chinese government has published a white paper on climate change since 2011.
China has always been a pragmatist in responding to climate change. Since the implementation of the "Twelfth Five-Year National Development Plan", China has also incorporated climate change responses into national social and economic development plans. Currently, responding to climate change has become China's national strategy and has achieved remarkable results.
Taking about 30 years to achieve carbon emissions reduction after reaching the point of achieving carbon neutrality is the biggest slowdown in global carbon emissions reduction. More than any major developing country. It means that China will face the task of changing the formula of energy and industry more difficult. But difficulties and challenges have never been overcome by the Chinese people.
Recall that in July 2015, Beijing and Zhangjiakou jointly won the right to host the Winter Olympics and the 2022 Winter Paralympic Games. The Chinese government and people have pledged to the world that the Winter Olympics will be a great success and extraordinary.
"The preparations for the Beijing Winter Olympics have been very smooth. We are deeply interested in the response format," Thomas Bach, chairman of the International Olympic Committee (IOC), told reporters recently. With China's Kovid 19 disease, we are full of confidence in the success of the Beijing Winter Olympics.
China will adhere to the basic policy of openness to foreign countries, use the giant market superiority and domestic demand potential, and strive to promote regulatory openness such as laws, regulations and standards, etc., increase intellectual property protection force. Create a business environment with a market that is in line with the law and international to provide fair and equitable market order to national and international enterprises.
I believe that China's development will bring more new opportunities to countries around the world and add more impetus to global economic development.
