(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, called on the general public to start and maintain a special savings account to be able to save with an institution licensed by the National Bank of Cambodia. Money grows as well as security.
Such a call by the Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia was made during the workshop on "Save money now for your future" organized by the National Bank of Cambodia, the Association of Banks in Cambodia and the Microfinance Association of Cambodia. To raise public awareness of the importance of saving money and to participate in the celebration of ASEAN Savings Day.
Kea Boran also told the general public to start cultivating this habit of saving money for children or young children as soon as possible so that he has this important life skill. Effective financial management should start with making a deposit and managing your expenses later.
According to Mr. Boran, in the last five years, 2016-2020, the number of savings accounts has almost doubled to nearly 9 million accounts by the end of 2020 for the entire financial sector. However, there are still many people, especially in rural areas and low-income people, who have not yet used official savings with institutions licensed by the National Bank of Cambodia.
Mr. Bun Yin, Vice President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, stated that the savings of the people in the formal financial institutions, including banking institutions and deposit-taking financial institutions provide benefits for themselves, society and the national economy.
At the same time, the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to strengthen operational cooperation with foreign banks to facilitate cross-border payment and remittance transactions in order to facilitate Cambodian workers working abroad to turn to convenient banking services. Low fees and secure to send money to family members in Cambodia.
Please be informed that the current deposits in banks and financial institutions have increased significantly, as of September 2021, deposits in banks and financial institutions have received more than 37 billion US dollars. From 12.05 million customer accounts.
Tourism Minister Holds Meeting with Darasakor Vacation Company to Prepare for Vaccine Tourism
(Koh Kong): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government-Private Working Group for the Rehabilitation and Promotion of Tourism in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis, on the evening of October 30, 2021, chaired a meeting with representatives of the vacation company. Darasakor to prepare for the vaccination tour in the Darasakor vacation area at the end of November.
The meeting was held at Darasakor Vacation Area, Koh Kong Province, with the participation of Mr. Khim Chandy, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, Representative of Darasakor Vacation Company, President of Asia-Pacific Tourism Association of Cambodia, Representative of Cambodia Association of Travel Agents, Director of Koh Kong Provincial Department of Tourism. Provincial Health Department as well as some other relevant officials.
Minister Thong Khon also advised Darasakor Vacation Company to strive to expand its services to be more diverse in order to attract more tourists with good and affordable services that not only receive guests. International tourists, domestic tourists can also come to enjoy this comfortable place, while now domestic tourists are also starting to travel to tourist destinations.
The Minister stated that in line with the preparation of tourists, vaccines must not forget to strengthen the safety of their places by cleaning and spraying disinfectants frequently in their local destinations to be comfortable. According to the plan "Minimum Operating Standards (SOP) in the new normal path" set by the Ministry of Tourism and the Ministry of Health, especially for national and international vaccination.
In addition, Minister Thong Khon also urged Darasakor Vacation Company to expedite the construction of Darasakor International Airport as soon as possible to launch domestic, regional and international flights, especially connecting Siem Reap-Angkor, which will Launched in January 2021.
In response, representatives of the construction company also pledged to work as soon as possible to be ready to receive tourists, as construction is now nearing completion and only some infrastructure in the passenger building remains. The airport will be ready to open for test flights in early January 2022 and will be officially opened in mid-2022, in which the building can accommodate nearly 1 million passengers a year. Well.
Regarding Darasakor Vacation Area, the company representative also promised to strive to expand its services in the area with a variety of affordable prices that can provide convenience for both national and international guests to enjoy a comfortable location for guests. .
The company representative also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for its efforts to prevent Kovid 19 and the selection of Darasakor as a vaccine tourism area. The company is also committed to implementing policies to guide health and tourism rules to become a safe vaccine tourism destination to reassure tourists.
