Xi Jinping stressed that China has always upheld its international responsibilities in line with its national situation, actively promoting the transformation of green development formulas, and actively promoting the continuous operational force to respond to climate change.
He said China will strive to achieve greenhouse gas emissions reductions after reaching a peak by 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2060. We will fulfill our commitment to join countries to follow the green, low-carbon and sustainable development path.
Xi stressed that developed countries should set an example on emissions reduction issues, fully consider the special difficulties and attention of developing countries, abide by the promise of climate financing and provide support to countries. Developing in technology and capacity building.
Xi Jinping outlined the Operational Initiative on Global Vaccine Cooperation. The first is to strengthen cooperation in scientific research on vaccines and to support vaccine companies in collaborating on research and production with developing countries.
The second is to maintain justice and equality, increase the supply of vaccines to developing countries to implement the 2022 Global Vaccination Targets set by the World Health Organization. Third, support the World Trade Organization (WTO) decision on pardoning vaccines soon and encourage vaccine companies to transfer technology to developing countries.
Fourth, strengthen cross-border trade cooperation to ensure a smooth trade in vaccines and raw materials. Fifth, adhere to a fair attitude towards all types of vaccines by promoting mutual recognition of vaccines based on the World Health Organization (WHO) Urgent Vaccine List.
Finally, the sixth is to provide financial assistance for global vaccine cooperation, especially for developing countries in accessing vaccines.
