Vietnam thanks Cambodian government and people for providing 200,000 doses of vaccine in this difficult situation (Video inside) (Svay Rieng): Deputy Minister of Health Chin Van Thean, on behalf of the Vietnamese government and people, thanked And appreciate the humanitarian spirit of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, which has provided 200,000 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine to its people in this difficult situation.
Mr. Chin Vanthean made this statement after receiving 200,000 doses of 19 vaccines against Kovid syphilis, which were donated by the people and the Royal Government of Cambodia this morning, October 29, 2021. The handover ceremony took place at the Bavet-Mok Pai International Border Crossing, where Cambodia was represented by Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the National Kovid Vaccination Commission 19, represented by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Deputy Minister of Health of Vietnam said, "We are very grateful and appreciative of the support of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia in providing Vietnam with 200,000 doses of Sinofam vaccine to fight 19 Kovid." "
Mr. Chin Van Thean affirmed that this support is a very meaningful gesture, a great source of spirit and material for the Royal Government and people of Vietnam at this difficult time, and shows the traditional friendship between Vietnam and Vietnam. Cambodia is becoming more and more accumulated for the benefit of the people of both countries.
According to the Deputy Minister of Health, the vaccine, which Cambodian aid will be used on this occasion, will be given to its people living along the border with Cambodia to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and ensure proper and fruitful use.
Ms. O Vandin emphasized that in the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who often said, "Cambodia is a small country with a big heart," so the decision to provide 19 vaccines to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam "Help each other in times of need, know good friends in difficult times."
She added that the humanitarian donations on this occasion are also a testament to the deep feelings, solidarity, closeness and good traditional cooperation that the Party and Government of Cambodia and Vietnam have nurtured and nurtured for a long time.
Vietnam is the second country to receive 19 Kovid vaccines after Laos. In addition to providing vaccines to neighboring countries, Cambodia has in the past donated medical equipment to fight the 199 Kovid disease to a network of countries in the ASEAN region.
Ms. O Vandin made this remark on the morning of October 29, 2021, on the occasion of presiding over Samdech Techo Hun Sen, handing over the vaccine aid to the Vietnamese government and people at the Bavet-Mok Pai International Border Crossing. Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province.
Ms. O Vandin said, "The decision to provide Kovid-19 vaccine to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam today is a testament to the great and generous kindness of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the people of Cambodia to the people and The government of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, in line with the motto (help each other in times of need, know good friends in times of difficulty).
