More than 800 Families Affected by Prek Tnaot Flood in Dangkor District Receive Royal Gifts from King and Queen Mother
(Phnom Penh): 837 families living in Sangkat Kong Noy and Sangkat Tien, Khan Dangkor affected by the flood of Stung Prek Tnaot were given gifts by the King and Queen to alleviate their hardships. He was in this difficult time.
This ceremony was held on the morning of October 29, 2021 under the high presidency of His Majesty the King Vor Vieng Chey, presided over by Sri Kongkar Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Royal Palace, His Majesty the King, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. King of Cambodia and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness in Sangkat Kong Noy, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
In fact, on October 24, 2021, the water level of Stung Prek Tnaot River rose sharply, causing the headwaters to overflow, flooding houses and causing direct and indirect effects on many families. In 4 villages in Kong Noy commune, on October 26, 2021, the flood continued to flood 4 other villages in Tien commune as well as some other villages in Dangkor district, Phnom Penh.
The governor said that in this catastrophic situation, the coalition forces and local authorities at all levels of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration have a high degree of cooperation to provide timely relief by evacuating people from the affected areas. Safe place and provided food, clean water, toilets and suitable temporary accommodation, that is, no one lives.
Mr. Khuong Sreng further stated that seeing the hardships of the people, His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, the highest revered person, through Samdech Chao Fah Veang, Deputy Prime Minister, donated royal humanitarian gifts to distribute to the victims. Due to the flood, 837 families living in the affected areas, 491 families in Kong Noy commune and 346 families in Tien commune.
The Governor of Phnom Penh further stated that the noble and noble royal deeds of virtue, humanity and Brahma Vihear now really reflect the highest devotion with all his strength, body and intellect. The intellect of His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, the highest reverence for the motherland to solve and alleviate the hardships of his people at all stages.
On that occasion, Samdech Chao Feang Vor Vieng Chey, President of Sri Kongkar Kong Sam Ol, said that after receiving the information about the flooding of people's houses due to the flood of Prek Tnaot and seeing the suffering of the people, His Majesty the Queen. The Khmer mother also assigned the prince to bring this royal humanitarian gift to distribute to 837 families in Dangkor district.
Samdech Chao Fah Veang further stated that the royal gift of the King and Samdech Mey must be given to the 837 families, each family received a T-shirt, 50 kg of rice, 10 masks, 2 boxes of noodles, 10 cans of fish. A tent, a kit (which includes a blanket, a scarf, a mosquito net) and a budget of 400,000 riels.
On that occasion, the Prince also instructed all citizens to follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health as well as the Royal Government to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, especially to implement "3 do not and 3 "Protect" so that together we can prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
