During the 17 years of his reign, the King upheld his duties and responsibilities as stipulated in the Constitution in the service of religion, humanity, education, social affairs, welfare and livelihood of the people. Across the country and bring happiness for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
He studied at Norodom Primary School and later went on to study at Descartes High School, both of which are located in Phnom Penh. At the age of nine, he was sent by his father to Prague, former Czechoslovakia, in 1962 as part of a neutral foreign policy and friendship with all countries that respected Cambodian sovereignty.
There he exhibited unparalleled prominence in the pedagogical system, civil affairs, and excellent manners. After that, he attended elementary school, high school and music school, where he studied classical music and dance until 1975. King Norodom Sihamoni was fluent in linguistics, fluent in French and Czech. He is also fluent in English and Russian.
In 1981, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni traveled to Paris to teach ballet and assume the role of President of the Khmer Dance Association. He lived in France for almost 20 years, where he often traveled to Prague, where he spent much of his youth. Not only that, he was the only Khmer king capable of having Sovanny in Czech.
