Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: Promoting the Internal Tourism Movement is to Boost Economic Growth from the Kovid Crisis
This statement was made by the Deputy Prime Minister at a ceremony to announce the implementation of the "Policy to promote the tourism movement" on the afternoon of October 28, 2021, with the participation of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government-Private Working Group for the Rehabilitation and Promotion of Tourism in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis, as well as a number of other relevant officials, which were made via remote video.
The Deputy Prime Minister added that up to now, the transmission of 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia is under good control, with the infection rate and mortality rate being low. This result is the most important foundation for advancing the internal tourism movement, which is an important part of the gradual reopening of all socio-economic activities in line with the new normal trajectory.
He also instructed the Ministry of Tourism to work closely with the provincial administration and relevant ministries and institutions to promote the evaluation of domestic tourism in order to ensure the safety of tourists and strive to organize tourist destinations within its jurisdiction. Attraction and safety in accordance with the method of determining the area or destination of safe tourism to attract domestic and international tourists.
Minister Thong Khon stated that, in general, the policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement in 2021-2023 are as follows:
First, the implementation of the policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement in 2021-2023 with high efficiency, depending on the commitment and participation of relevant ministries and institutions at all levels, local authorities, the Armed Forces and Citizens in practice in accordance with their respective roles, duties and responsibilities.
Second, to achieve a successful recovery of domestic tourists, it is necessary to rely on key determinants such as the speed of vaccination 19, the status of the management of 19's 19, the readiness of the tourism business along the new normal trajectory and psychological factors. .
Third, to ensure that local tourism activities can resume, the most important thing is to increase public confidence in travel decisions. In addition, the convenience of traveling or organizing other leisure activities is also a necessary factor to promote local tourism activities and the readiness of tour operators.
* Promoting the confidence and trust of domestic tourists through the planning and management of safe domestic tourist destinations in the capital-province.
* Promoting the resumption of business - tour operators in the new normal trajectory by continuing to implement financial support, incentives and study, develop new support measures and organize training courses to strengthen tourism skills.
* Facilitating the internal tourism movement, including businesses - tour operators, national tourists - domestic foreigners
* Develop tourism products to serve the internal tourism movement through continuous efforts to organize and create new tourism products to attract the internal tourism movement at the main poles.
Dissemination and mainstreaming of public awareness through the launch of strategies to raise public awareness within the framework of the "Visit Our District" campaign under the spirit of "Patriotism, Know the Territory".
