The Senate will convene a meeting of the Standing Committee on November 1 to determine the date and agenda of the fourth extraordinary session.
(Phnom Penh): The Senate will convene a meeting of the Standing Committee on November 1 to set the date and agenda of the fourth extraordinary session. This is according to the announcement of the General Secretariat of the Senate, which was received by Fresh New Network.
1. Examine and decide on the request of the Sixth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft Constitution on the amendment of Article 19 new, Article 82 new, Article 106 new (a), Article 119 new and Article 137 new of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 3 And Article 4 of the Additional Constitution to ensure the normal functioning of national institutions in the agenda of the fourth extraordinary Senate session.
2. Examine and decide on the request of the Sixth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the approval of the supplementary agreement to the agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations regarding the adjudication under Cambodian law. Crimes committed during the period of Democratic Kampuchea on the arrangement of the transitional period and the termination of the Extraordinary Chambers into the agenda of the Senate for the fourth extraordinary term.
3. Examine and decide on the request of the Second Committee of the Senate to put the draft law on public-private partnership on the agenda of the Senate as the extraordinary fourth legislature.
4. Determine the agenda, date and composition of the Secretary of the Extraordinary Session of the Senate for the 4th Extraordinary Legislature. The Ministry of National Defense vaccinated 19 Kovid 19 troops, 2,759,844 military families and citizens, the second 2,732,380 people and the second dose 852,125
