Mr. Sok Loo Urges Battambang Municipality to Strengthen Local Security and Eliminate Gambling and Drug Problems
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, urged the Battambang Municipal Administration to continue to strengthen cooperation with the relevant forces and professional officers to maintain good security in the city, especially to strengthen the policy of safe villages and communes to fit the word clean city. .
Mr. Sok Lou made this remark during a meeting with civil servants, commune chiefs and the three types of armed forces in Battambang City on the morning of October 28, 2021 at Battambang City Hall with the participation of Mr. Pheng Sithy, Battambang Mayor, all Deputy Governors, Sangkat Chiefs and Armed Forces of the three categories and Battambang City Hall officials also participated.
After the welcome report from Mr. Pheng Sethy, Governor of Battambang Municipality on the results of past work, Mr. Sok Lou said that today he met with civil servants, commune chiefs, armed forces in the entire Battambang municipal administration to get to know each other. To increase the closeness and cooperation on behalf of the provincial administration.
The provincial governor stated that in order to continue the sustainable service of the public service to the people, the development work of the city order, especially the policy of safe villages, communes, sanitation, urban environment, drug crackdown, homeless gambling and other anarchy in Battambang city. Well, to fit the name of a clean city.
Mr. Sok Loo continued that in addition to the core work of the leadership, each official must do more social work, humanitarian work that the general public is in need of us to help them, which happened in all circumstances on time, this is an important task. One that brings the leadership of civil servants closer to our people at their local level.
On that occasion, he stressed that in the case of gambling, the authorities must crack down and not leave any rest, and must not take money from the owners of gambling houses, if any authorities are involved and behind, please withdraw immediately because If this is the case, then it is impossible to crack down. The provincial governor also announced his phone number to the general public to receive and receive information from all quarters, easy to take action.
Mr. Sok Lou also stressed that why Battambang city still has gangsters, young people and homeless people and garbage in some places, what professional managers are doing left. This can not be allowed to continue, the municipal administration must deal with this as soon as possible and better.
The Governor of Battambang Province reminded all City Hall officials to respect the discipline, respect the time, work hard, respect their respective roles and responsibilities and respect the assignment of the leadership, especially to maintain internal unity to continue. Sustainability for the better.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to continue to support the garment and tourism sectors for another three months.
(Phnom Penh): In order to help the recovery of the special economy in the field of garments - textiles, footwear, travel products, bags and tourism, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to continue to support these two sectors for an additional three months from October to December 2021.
This assistance is provided by providing benefits to suspended workers for the garment sector and tax incentives for the tourism sector.
Guidelines for Additional Measures to Continue Managing Impacts on Key Sectors of the Economy in the Context of the Crisis, Restoring and Promoting Cambodia's Economic Growth After the Kovid-19 Crisis (Round 10) by the Royal Government of Cambodia, Fresh News Network News Received on October 28, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to help the following two sectors:
* Continue to provide a stipend of US $ 40 per month to 1 worker working in the tourism sector, such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies for an additional 3 months from October to December 2021. Enterprises and businesses in the tourism sector must contribute on a voluntary and practical basis in addition to what the Royal Government has to offer.
