(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovanrith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, on the morning of November 28, 2021, requested the 8 conflict resolution working groups to pay attention to resolving disputes according to their technical roles and experiences to be successful and jointly complete. Local conflicts for the people to live in peace, happiness and development in all areas in accordance with the policy of the head of the Royal Government.
He said this during the meeting to announce the decision on the establishment of working groups to resolve disputes and requests of people in the provinces, districts in Kampong Chhnang, with the participation of the Deputy Governor and Deputy Director. Units around the province.
Mr. Sun Sovanrith said that according to the reports of the eight districts in Kampong Chhnang province, there were 716 cases of disputes and other requests from the people in that province. He said that 363 cases have been resolved and 187 cases are being resolved and 168 cases are still unresolved.
The provincial governor requested that the eight conflict resolution teams, upon receiving this decision, visit all communes and districts from November 1 until the end of November. In particular, within a week, report the results of the dispute resolution to the Provincial Secretariat for Dispute Resolution in a timely manner.
The provincial governor hopes that the eight conflict resolution teams will pay attention to resolving disputes according to their technical roles and good experiences to successfully end conflicts at the local level so that our people can live in peace and happiness. Achieve development in all areas in accordance with the policy of the head of the Royal Government.
On the occasion of the meeting, the four Deputy Governors provided some good experiences in resolving past disputes in the districts so that all working groups in the province have the basis and experience during the visit. To resolve disputes and requests of people in the eight districts in Kampong Chhnang province.
