In an interview published by CNN on Thursday, the Taiwanese president said that Taiwan has extensive cooperation with the United States, aimed at strengthening the island's defense capabilities. Answer the question, how many US troops are on Taiwan? "Not as many as everyone thinks," she said.
Tensions in Taiwan, which is legally within China's sovereignty, have escalated after US President Joe Biden announced that he would help protect the island if China attacked. . China has spoken out strongly against the United States and called on the United States to rectify its mistakes and stop seeking "independence" for Taiwan because it will fail.
The 4th ASEAN-Russia Summit was held in conjunction with the celebration of the 30th anniversary of the dialogue partnership between the two sides, with the participation of Russian President Vladimir Putin and heads of state. Other ASEAN countries except Myanmar have no participating positions.
According to the announcement of the results, as the coordinating country for the ASEAN-Russia Dialogue, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued the ASEAN Joint Declaration, which highlighted the achievements of cooperation and proposed a number of actions for The future will be shared between ASEAN and Russia to further enhance this partnership.
The Summit adopted three key documents: (1): ASEAN-Russia Statement on Cooperation in Combating Illicit Drug Trafficking (2): Joint Statement of the ASEAN-Russia Summit Fourth, building a region full of peace, stability and sustainability (3): Comprehensive action plan to implement the strategic partnership between the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and the Russian Federation (2021-2025).
Separately, two other documents were noted, including: (1) the revised road map of ASEAN-Russia trade and investment cooperation and (2): the ASEAN-Russia Trade and Investment Work Program for the year. 2021-2025.
