Kun Nhem: The Ministry is studying the possibility of finding ways to encourage the use of more new cars
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, confirmed that the Ministry of Economy and Finance is studying the possibility of finding ways to encourage more new cars. In Cambodia.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Kun Nhem's participation in the press conference on the progress of the implementation of the collection of import duties on existing duty-free vehicles through video system on October 27, 2021.
Mr. Kun Nhim stated that "The Ministry of Economy and Finance is studying the possibility and encouraging car users to find ways to use new cars and also do not encourage the use of used cars (used cars). Going forward.
Mr. Kun Nhim said that older cars have an additional charge using the tax rate factor, with older cars having higher tax rates. This is to make the old market more integrated and replace it with new cars.
He added that the permit for used cars (used cars) to enter Cambodia has been around for a long time. It is not just cars that Cambodia allows to be imported, there are many other used items that Cambodia allows to be imported.
"When it comes to used cars, we also think about it, not that we do not think about it, because it is time to consider the environment and the safety of consumers," he said.
He said that new cars are now hitting the market more as before, while older cars are gradually declining. However, Mr. Kun Nhim stated that the Royal Government does not have a policy to prohibit the import of used cars. Boryakha Community Learning Center, a Japanese people's aid, was officially inaugurated.
(Pailin): The Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports under the leadership of Pailin Provincial Administration on October 28, 2021 organized the inauguration ceremony of Boryakha Community Learning Center.
The event was presided over by Ms. Ban Srey Mom, Governor of Pailin Province, Mr. Nou Sles, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and a delegation from the Embassy of Japan. In Cambodia, Pailin Constituency MPs, provincial education officials, as well as many teachers participated.
The provincial governor continued that there are 3 buildings of this community learning center: one in the campus of Boryakha Primary School, one in Krachap village, Otavao commune, and one in Dis Thmey village, Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district. The single standard model is 11 meters wide, 16 meters long, equal to 3 rooms and 2 bathrooms, fully furnished and equipped.
Mikami Masahiro said this was the first time he had visited Pailin since Japan was appointed ambassador to Cambodia for two years, never visiting Pailin. He added that the Royal Government of Japan, as well as the people of Japan, are happy to receive cooperation with Cambodia through Children Without Borders, and in the future will continue to enhance good relations with each other. .
Mr. Nou Sles said that he would like to join in appreciating and thanking the people as well as the Royal Government of Japan for providing school building assistance to Pailin Province to facilitate the absorption of knowledge and skills to grow crops for livelihood.
He added that, as Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has always paid attention to the field of vocational education and training, he has taken this education sector first among all sectors because it is important for the development of society. To make progress only today, while the Japanese philanthropists provide a lot of specialized school buildings and study materials to Cambodia.
