The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen attended the 18th ASEAN-India Summit, which was also attended by Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi and other ASEAN leaders, except Myanmar.
The ASEAN Fund was established in 2020 to respond to 19 cases of Kovid, with the aim of mobilizing financial resources to address the shortage of medical equipment, to support research and development of drugs for Kovid 19, and to respond to And emergencies in the future.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated: "(At the 18th ASEAN-India Summit), the Prime Minister thanked India for its contribution of US $ 1 million to the ASEAN Fund for Corruption. 19 and encouraged India to support ASEAN regional integration and the implementation of the work plan of the Initiative for ASEAN Integration (IAI) Phase 4 (2021-2025), focusing on connectivity and digital education.
In his efforts to boost trade and economic recovery, the Prime Minister also encouraged both sides to make efforts to simplify and open the ASEAN-India Trade Agreement (AITIGA).
