Mr. Mar Yarith: Journalists can hide the identity of the source if the information may endanger the source
(Phnom Penh): In order for a news article to gain the trust of readers, journalists should reveal the identity of the source of information to the reader. But in some cases, journalists can hide their identities if they understand that the broadcast could endanger the source. This was confirmed by Mr. Mar Yarith, President of Fresh News Training Center (FTC) to the trainees last weekend.
According to Mar Yarith, hiding the source is something that needs to be done to protect the security of the source, including hiding the name, hiding the location, various identities of the source and even the sound being modified so that the source can not be found. . But doing so purely makes the reader of the article may not trust the writer, suspecting that it may be just a fabrication.
Confidentiality of Sources It is essential for journalists to maintain confidentiality if it is deemed that the leak could be harmful to the source. The rights of journalists in this regard are also enshrined in Article 2 of the Law on the Cambodian Press, which states that "journalists have the right to confidentiality of their sources."
(Siem Reap): Fifty poor families in Kampong Khleang commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province received a charity donation from a local organization through a group of young artists.
Fifty poor families in Kampong Khleang commune received rice and other food items from the Sharing Arts Youth Team. Representative of the Youth Sharing Arts Group, Mr. Ream Mony Silong, said that the gift package was received from Panha Foundation for Education in Cambodia through his team, which provides to needy families, the elderly and orphans.
Mr. Mony Silong stated that the gift package provided to the people in Kampong Khleang commune who were in need during the 19-year period of Kovid include: 20 kg of rice, 1 kg of garlic, 2 bottles of fish sauce, 2 bottles of soy sauce, 1 kg of sugar, 3 kg and a half kilos. 1 gram of alcohol, 1 bottle of soap, salt and mask.
According to Mr. Vichet Monisilong, the "Sharing Arts Youth Group" was established at the end of September 2021 in order to alleviate the hardships of the poor people in Kampong Khleang commune.
He said the next goal would be to continue to share the hardships of people in other areas by seeking charitable help from local or international artists and organizations, regardless of political affiliation. . Comment: US should stop playing with fire over Taiwan issue
BEIJING (Reuters) - The recent call by the United States for Taiwan's energetic and meaningful participation in the United Nations (UN) system is once again seen as a violation. On China's red line around the Taiwan issue. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday, October 28, 2021.
The US Secretary of State's comments on Tuesday this week seriously violated the one-China principle, as well as the three joint statements between China and the United States, which are the political foundations of the two countries' relations, and betrayed the promises made by Washington. Committed as well as violating international standards.
Five decades ago, the 26th session of the UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 2758 by an overwhelming majority and restored all rights of the People's Republic of China in this international body. The resolution resolves the issue of China's representation at the UN in terms of politics, law and procedures.
Even the United States itself has made it clear in its joint Sino-US statement that it recognizes the government of the People's Republic of China as China's sole legitimate government and recognizes China's position that China Unique by Taiwan is part of China.
The one-China principle is a universal consensus and an internationally recognized standard for governing international relations. To date, a total of 180 countries, including the United States, have established diplomatic ties with China in accordance with this principle.
Today, however, some politicians in Washington still choose to ignore history, facts, and international law and try to go against the power of the United Nations. The Taiwan issue is related to China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. Therefore, Beijing will never accept compromises on any issues related to its core national interests.
It should be noted that anyone who plays with the fire will burn himself. Therefore, the United States should stop commenting as well as its wrongdoings and dangers. At the same time, Washington should fully implement its commitments and abide by UN resolutions, and take concrete steps to restore Sino-US relations and maritime relations between China and Taiwan.
