(Phnom Penh): Immediately after receiving the hammer of the ASEAN chair, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced that Samdech is a Cambodian Prime Minister who has held the hammer of the ASEAN chair up to three times. Samdech Techo thanked all the people who voted for Samdech in leading Cambodia.
"I am the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has held the ASEAN chair three times," he said on his Facebook page. I would like to take this opportunity to thank my compatriots who have supported me in leading Cambodia, enabling me to participate in regional and international affairs through ASEAN. ”
It should be noted that after concluding the 38th and 39th ASEAN Summits and the three-day busy summits hosted by Brunei, Samdech Techo Hun Sen received the hammer to chair ASEAN on the afternoon of the 28th. October 2021.
This is the third assignment for Cambodia to host this important regional summit and summit after becoming a member of ASEAN on April 30, 1999. Hosted the first time in 2002 and the second time in 2012.
With the task of hosting this important summit, Samdech Techo stated that on behalf of the people and the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech is extremely proud to take over the rotating chairmanship of ASEAN for 2022.
