(Svay Rieng): A young man died suddenly due to lack of caution, causing him to fall into a rubber crusher, crushing bones, causing surprise to the same workers and reporting to the authorities.
This incident happened on October 27, 2021 at 3:45 pm at Manva factory in Sala Tean village, Chrakmtes commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province.
According to the police, the victim was 18-year-old Pang Vanda, a laborer living in Svay Paem village, Prey Tay commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province.
According to witnesses who worked with the victim confirmed that before the incident, the young man was working as usual, but somehow suddenly fell into a rubber crusher, crushing bones, causing surprise.
Authorities confirmed that the cause was due to the victim's lack of care, negligence, causing such death. At present, the body has been recorded and handed over to the victim's family for a traditional ceremony.
