(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Vietnam have agreed to hold the 12th meeting on cooperation and development of border provinces, which is scheduled to be held in Vietnam in 2022. The actual date and venue of the meeting will be announced via diplomatic channels. This is according to the official Facebook page of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng.
This agreement was made on the occasion that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior of Cambodia, chaired the 11th Meeting on Cooperation and Development of Cambodia-Vietnam Border Provinces with Mr. Pham. Binh Minh, Deputy Prime Minister of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, on October 28, 2021.
The meeting was held in the spirit of the 10th Meeting on Cooperation and Development of Cambodia-Vietnam Border Provinces on January 9-10, 2019 in Ho Chi Minh City, Socialist Republic of Vietnam. The 11th meeting was also attended by leaders of relevant ministries and institutions of the two countries and provinces bordering Cambodia-Vietnam.
Through this meeting, the two sides discussed important agendas such as the results of cooperation between countries and border provinces through the organization of telephone dialogues and video conferences. Increase investment, continue to support border provinces and increase more effective cooperation to address timely challenges and practical needs.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Mr. Pham Binh Minh, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, praised the work achieved from the 10th meeting until now.
