Samdech Techo Hun Sen Attends the 4th ASEAN-Russia Summit, Putin Considers ASEAN Work as His Priority
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 29, 2021, continued to attend the 4th ASEAN-Russia Summit, the last meeting for the ASEAN Summit and related summits in 2021, which took place for 3 days via video system.
The meeting was attended by Russian President Vladimir Putin and other ASEAN leaders, with the exception of Myanmar.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that at the summit, the ASEAN-Russia Head of Government approved three important documents, including: 1. Comprehensive Action Plan for the Implementation of the ASEAN-Russia Strategic Partnership; 2021-2025, 2: ASEAN-Russia Declaration on Building a Safe and Sustainable Zone, and 3: ASEAN-Russia Cooperation on Global Drug Solution and Counter-Narcotics.
ASEAN-Russia Summit As Cambodia is a facilitator of the ASEAN-Russia Dialogue Partnership, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was invited to represent ASEAN to read the common interests of ASEAN in this meeting to the President of Russia.
In that interest highlighted some important issues. With regard to political-security cooperation, ASEAN understands that as the world enters a new era of technology, building a close and strong partnership to address common issues in this area is crucial. In this regard, ASEAN would like to express its satisfaction with the organization of the first ASEAN-Russia Information, Communication and Information Technology Dialogue.
ASEAN also thanked Russia for its support in providing training on counter-terrorism and transnational crime to experts from ASEAN member countries and encouraged Russia to provide more training. ASEAN is expected to receive Russia's support for the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Vision and to consider possible cooperation in other ASEAN priority areas.
ASEAN also appreciated Russia's work with the ASEAN Clean Cities Project and welcomed the ASEAN-Russia Clean Cities Innovation and Sustainable Urban Project proposal. At the same time, ASEAN is pleased that both sides have agreed to enhance tourism cooperation to the ministerial level.
In terms of socio-cultural cooperation, ASEAN would like to thank Russia for providing training for health professionals from ASEAN member countries in 2019-2021 and encourage Russia to continue to support this sector with assistance. Support in building general human resources in the region. ASEAN also looks forward to the preparation and approval of the ASEAN-Russia Education Action Plan 2021-2025.
At the meeting, the Russian President stated that Russia supports the core role of ASEAN in the mechanisms established by ASEAN, such as the East Asia Summit, the ASEAN Regional Forum, and the Defense Ministers' Meeting.
The President also mentioned that he has known many ASEAN heads of government and worked together for many years and was very pleased with the deepening relationship between ASEAN and Russia.
The President stressed that ASEAN-Russia cooperation must continue to maintain security and stability in the region. The Russian president has made promoting cooperation with ASEAN a priority for him.
