(Phnom Penh): Thursday, October 28, is the last day of the ASEAN Summit and related summits in 2021. The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen today continued to attend the 18th ASEAN-India Summit.
The meeting was attended by Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi and other ASEAN leaders, with the exception of Myanmar.
Kao Kim Hourn, Deputy Prime Minister, emphasized that at the meeting, the ASEAN and Indian Heads of Government approved the ASEAN-India Joint Declaration on Cooperation on the ASEAN Vision on the Indo-Pacific.
At the meeting, the ASEAN-India Heads of Government made a number of points, noting that despite the 19 Kovid Crisis, the cooperation between ASEAN and India is still good and progressing.
The ASEAN-India Prime Minister described 2022 as the year of ASEAN-India friendship, as it marks the 30th anniversary of the ASEAN-India Dialogue Partnership. Especially on the 30th anniversary of this relationship, how to promote programs and activities to celebrate the 30th anniversary of this relationship.
The ASEAN Heads of Government welcomed India's support for ASEAN's efforts to rebuild the ASEAN countries from the 19-year crisis and thanked India for its contribution of $ 1 million to the ASEAN Fund for the Response to the 19-crisis crisis.
The ASEAN-India Head of Government is committed to promoting and strengthening trade, investment, energy, finance, science and technology, innovation and the digital economy. The ASEAN-India Prime Minister encouraged the ASEAN-India Business Council to continue its role in promoting trade between ASEAN and India.
The ASEAN Heads of Government thanked India for its support in building ASEAN capacity through training by providing 1,000 doctoral scholarships for students from ASEAN member countries to study in India.
The ASEAN-India Heads of Government recognized the importance of strengthening cooperation on ASEAN connectivity. In particular, efforts must be made to further promote the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025.
The ASEAN-India Heads of Government also praised and emphasized the ASEAN Concept on Indo-Pacific Politics. The ASEAN-India Heads of Government agreed that ASEAN and India must promote cooperation to ensure peace, stability and security in the Indo-Pacific region.
The ASEAN Heads of Government requested India to continue its support, especially on cooperation in the Mekong sub-region.
The ASEAN-India Heads of Government discussed regional issues such as the South China Sea and the crisis in Myanmar.
Cambodia's Ministry of Public Works and South Korea's Ministry of Personnel Management sign a memorandum of understanding
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 28, 2021, the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Public Works of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Personnel of the Republic of Korea was held at the Ministry of Public Works. "Management of human resources in the field of public functions."
Welcoming the cooperation agreement, Mr. Kim Woo-ho of the Ministry of Personnel Management of the Republic of Korea expressed his pleasure at the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding and strongly hoped that this special cooperation would Can train many professionals for the field of public functions.
Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works, praised the efforts of the two institutions to establish a good bilateral cooperation partnership to the present and in the future.
Meanwhile, the Minister of Public Works of Cambodia highlighted two important points:
1). Through this bilateral cooperation agreement, the two institutions will be able to achieve the strengthening, building and developing human resources in the field of public functions effectively, responding to the actual situation of the two countries.
2). To ensure the smooth and effective implementation of this Memorandum of Understanding, both sides need to develop an annual plan and cooperation activities that are realistic and feasible in the context of Kovid-19.
Finally, both the Minister of Public Works of Cambodia and the Minister of Personnel Management of the Republic of Korea are committed to implementing this cooperation as a practical activity to contribute to the further expansion of bilateral cooperation between the government and the people. People of both Cambodia and Korea.
Minister Thong Khon Explains the Strategic Plan for the Opening of Vaccine Tourism (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government and Private Working Group to Rehabilitate and Promote Tourism in and After the Kovid Crisis - 19 explained in detail the strategic plan on the opening of vaccination tourism in order to implement the vaccination tourism plan more effectively.
Mr. Thong Khon explained this on the occasion of Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Committee for Tourism Development, presiding over the launch of the "Strategic Plan for Vaccine Tourism". With the participation of many relevant officials through the remote video system this morning, October 28, 2021.
The purpose of this strategic plan is to start promoting the re-opening of international tourists step by step, based on the principle of maintaining a balance between socio-economic activities and ensuring public safety and health for citizens and tourists in line with the spirit of action. Safe travel and tourism to contribute to the development of Cambodia's tourism sector to become a quality, safe and sustainable tourism destination.
To achieve the vision and objectives, the strategic plan identifies four key goals:
* Goal 1: Identify potential, safe and low risk markets.
Goal 2: Management of international tourist flows to prevent and reduce the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
Goal 3: Strengthen the safety and quality of Cambodia's tourism services in line with the new normal trajectory.
Goal 4: Increase mutual trust and confidence between market sources and Cambodian tourism destinations.
The compilation of this strategic plan is based on a step-by-step approach to reopening international tourism, including:
* Step 1 Re-start: Re-start receiving international tourists by setting a pilot project at the end of November 2021, starting in Sihanoukville and Koh Rong, Sihanoukville and Darasakor area of Koh Kong province and then In Siem Reap in January 2022.
Step 2: Regional Reopening: Start accepting international tourists to other safe tourist destinations after the successful pilot project of the first step.
Step 3: Full reopening: Full vaccination tour across the country.
The strategic plan sets out four strategies, including:
Strategy 1: Identify the source of the vaccine tourism market.
Strategy 2: Travel management before departure and arrival at the international airport.
Strategy 3: Prepare the tourism industry in line with the new normal trajectory.
Strategy 4: Identify and manage safe tourism destinations.
Mr. Thong Khon added that the strategic plan outlines specific approaches to identifying safe tourism areas or destinations based on four performance indicators, including:
1: Vaccination rates aimed at building community immunity
3: Ability to respond and treat and manage the potential risk of a new mutation virus
4: Preparation of the tourism industry.
The implementation of this strategic plan is thoughtful, proactive and prudent, with options for opening and closing in each step according to the actual evolution of the situation. Establishing a Cambodian entry permit application system is an effective tool for managing special situations for implementing "open-close" in each step of the strategic plan.
The options for opening and closing will focus on three aspects, including: Scenario 1: zoning, Scenario 2: Pre-selection, tourism activity options, Scenario 3: Time factor.
These three aspects require the joint thinking and joint responsibility of all stakeholders to ensure the successful and safe implementation of this strategic plan based on the quadratic principle of public-private-people and tourists. Partners in bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
