New Zealand Prime Minister Jacinda Ardern said last week that New Zealand would end its austerity measures when about 90 percent of its population had been fully vaccinated. So far, about 72 per cent of New Zealanders have been fully vaccinated, while nearly 87 per cent have received their first dose.
General knowledge: Which countries have tested nuclear weapons and how many times?
(World): Everyone knows that the United States is the only country in the world that has used nuclear weapons to destroy enemies during the war. However, from 1945 to the present, at least eight countries have conducted a total of more than 2,000 joint weapons tests, nearly half of which were conducted by the United States itself.
