(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has requested that Russian President Vladimir Putin continue to provide assistance, including the necessary equipment, to combat systematic organized crime. The Prime Minister welcomed Russia's commitment to the fight against terrorism and transnational crime, especially in the areas of security, technology, communications and information.
The above request and statement was made while Samdech Techo Prime Minister was attending the 4th ASEAN-Russia Summit, which was held on video on October 28, 2021. The meeting was attended by Russian President Vladimir Putin and other ASEAN leaders, with the exception of Myanmar.
In addition to the above, Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulated the 65th anniversary of friendly relations and bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Russia.
Samdech Techo also asked Russia to help promote the negotiation of a free trade agreement between Cambodia and the Eurasian Economic Union. Samdech Techo also thanked Russia for supporting Cambodia's human capacity building and offered additional opportunities for professional officers to continue their studies and participate in training, especially in science and technology.
As a dialogue partner of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization, Samdech Techo stressed the importance of strengthening relations between ASEAN and the Shanghai Cooperation Organization and supported Russia's proposal to enhance this relationship.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo expressed his intention to study the possibility of inviting the President of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization as the guest of honor of ASEAN at the 41st ASEAN Summit when Cambodia will chair ASEAN in 2022.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, also raised some issues related to cooperation between ASEAN and Russia.
Samdech Techo said that as the world enters a new era of technology, building a close and strong partnership to solve common problems in this area is very important. As a member of ASEAN, Samdech Techo expressed his satisfaction with the organization of the first ASEAN-Russia Information, Communication and Information Dialogue.
He also thanked Russia for its support in providing training on counter-terrorism and transnational crime to experts from ASEAN member countries and encouraged Russia to provide more training. He is expected to receive Russia's support for the ASEAN vision on the Indo-Pacific and to consider possible cooperation in other ASEAN priority areas.
In strengthening economic cooperation, Samdech Techo stressed that ASEAN and Russia must fully implement the revised roadmap for trade and investment cooperation between ASEAN and Russia and trade and economic cooperation programs. ASEAN-Russia investment in 2021-2025, especially investment in food, agriculture, transportation, energy and tourism.
In line with living with Kovid-19 on a new normal path where technology will play an important role, Samdech Techo welcomed Russia's initiative to designate 2022 as the year of ASEAN-Russia scientific and technological cooperation.
As an ASEAN member, Samdech Techo also praised Russia's work with the ASEAN Clean Cities Project and welcomed the ASEAN-Russia Clean Cities Innovation and Sustainability Project proposal. At the same time, Samdech Techo expressed his pleasure that ASEAN-Russia has agreed to enhance tourism cooperation to the ministerial level.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized this in the ASEAN-India Summit held on video on Thursday, October 28, 2021. The meeting was attended by Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi and other ASEAN leaders, with the exception of Myanmar.
In his remarks before reaching the ASEAN-India issue, the Prime Minister highlighted the importance of respecting multilateralism. Samdech Techo said that in the context of the growing trend of protectionism and globalization, Cambodia still has strong faith in the multilateral mechanism. Especially in the context of resolving the Kovid-19 crisis and rehabilitating and stimulating economic growth.
He stressed that building regional trust through practical cooperation in line with the objectives and principles of the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Vision (AOIP) and India's Indo-Pacific Initiative is also an important response point. .
During the meeting, Samdech Techo expressed his support for the launch of the ASEAN-India Joint Statement on Cooperation on the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Perspective.
Samdech Techo expressed the hope that ASEAN-India relations will be stronger and as the ASEAN Chair in 2022, Cambodia is ready to co-organize, celebrate and celebrate this great opportunity. Ministry of Labor and Stakeholders Celebrate World Day for Occupational Safety and Health
In order to prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the workplace, the Minister also reminded the factory owners to pay attention, including:
