(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment, represented by Mr. Van Monineath, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development (SSD) and the Asian Vision Institute (AVI), represented by Mr. Keo Piseth, Deputy Director of the Institute, signed a Memorandum of Understanding to increase the work. Cooperation in environmental management and sustainable development.
The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding was presided over by Mr. Tin Ponlok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment on behalf of Minister Say Sam Al on October 27, 2021 at the Ministry of Environment.
Mr. Keo Piseth said that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding today is another important event for AVI Institute because it shows the growing trust and confidence by the Royal Government of Cambodia on AVI and Cambodian intellectuals in Participation and input for the formulation of national policies that will determine Cambodia's future development path.
He said the cooperation between the two institutions will focus on joint policy research, monitoring and evaluation and human resource development through short- and long-term training and awareness-raising. Public on a wide range of topics, including environmental protection, biodiversity conservation, natural resource management, climate change, sustainable leadership, innovation, economic cycles, and sustainable development.
