Accounting and Auditing Regulators Open Forum on Accounting and Auditing Obligations and Benefits to the National Economy
The purpose of this forum is to promote and mainstream the understanding of accounting and auditing obligations, as well as to present the benefits of accounting and auditing obligations to the national economy, and to provide insights into the implementation of accounting and auditing obligations of some regulators.
Mr. Bou Tharin, Director General of the Accounting and Auditing Regulator, said that in recent years, the Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced a number of strategies, programs, legal and regulatory reforms aimed at facilitating, promoting and promoting Investment and business to ensure economic growth.
Mr. Bou Tharin added that within the legal framework and regulations for the accounting and auditing sector, there are three basic laws and regulations that have been implemented, including:
1: Law on Accounting and Auditing, April 20162: Sub-Decree on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing, June 2020 and 3: Prakas on the Obligations to Submit Financial Statements to Independent Auditors In July 2020.
He said that starting from these laws and regulations, three essential obligations for enterprises and non-profit organizations have been established, including:
1: Obligations to keep the accounting records 2: Obligations to prepare financial statements in accordance with the applicable standards and 3: Obligations to submit the financial statements to an independent audit in accordance with the conditions prescribed by law.
At the same time, Mr. Sou Socheat, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, stated that the Company has an obligation to keep a record and to undergo an audit of the financial statements.
Mr. Sou Socheat emphasized that the financial statements are important because they indicate whether the company is really profitable or not, in order to inform its investors.
The Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia stressed that if the company does not hold the list or audit the financial statements, the company will be punished according to law.
It should be noted that from 2021 onwards, the Accounting and Auditing Regulators will implement strict and thorough measures on the implementation of the accounting and auditing obligations of enterprises, in case of violations, enterprises will be punished in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.
