Scientific Advisors Urge Leaders to Have Specific Action Plans to Climate Change
LONDON (Reuters) - A group of 38 scientific advisers from various governments have urged their leaders to articulate action plans, not just promises on how to keep global warming at bay. At 1.5 degrees Celsius. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, October 28, 2021.
A new United Nations report on Tuesday states that the current commitment to reduce greenhouse gas emissions into the atmosphere is geared towards global warming. 2.7 degrees Celsius in the 21st century.
The UNEP annual report warns that today's commitment will reduce greenhouse gas emissions projected for 2030 by an additional 7.5 percent from the previous commitment. If this trend continues throughout the century, it will lead to a temperature rise of 2.7 degrees Celsius above pre-industrial levels.
