(Phnom Penh): No matter what Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always said and requested, the heads of state and government of the East Asian Dialogue Partners see and agree that multilateralism is a key policy in Overcome Kovid 19 and resolve crises.
This view was expressed at the 16th East Asia Summit, which was held on video on the night of October 27, 2021. The East Asia Dialogue Partners has 18 member countries, including 10 ASEAN members and eight dialogue partners: Australia, China, India, Japan, South Korea, New Zealand, Russia and the United States.
Today's meeting was attended by nine ASEAN heads of government, while Myanmar was absent along with the heads of state and government of the eight partner countries, as well as the Director-General of the World Health Organization and the Director-General of the World Trade Organization. Well.
According to Kao Kim Hourn, the ASEAN Heads of State and East Asia Summit Partner discussed a number of topics. But before the start of the meeting, the East Asian Dialogue and Heads of Government heard an update from the Director-General of the World Health Organization and the Director-General of the World Trade Organization on the state of health and trade in the wake of the Kovid crisis. 19 for the past 18 months.
The Heads of State and Government highlighted ASEAN's central role in the East Asia Dialogue Framework and the will of ASEAN to continue to play an important role in the East Asia Dialogue Partnership Mechanism. Not only that, the Heads of State and Government of East Asia Dialogue Partners stressed the importance of ASEAN's concept of the Indo-Pacific to ensure peace, stability and security in the region.
The Heads of State and Government of East Asia also discussed a number of key issues on cooperation in preventing and addressing Kovid 19. In particular, the fight against and promotion of Kovid 19 vaccine.
The heads of state and government of East Asia have agreed to boost and revive the economy in the wake of the Kovid 19 crisis. In particular, strive to promote other sectors such as tourism to return to a better state, promote cooperation in the field of energy that supports the environment, promote cooperation in education and so on.
The heads of state and government of the East Asia Dialogue Partners agreed to develop further plans for East Asian cooperation. In addition, there was an exchange of views on regional and international issues such as the South China Sea, the Korean Peninsula and Myanmar. In particular, the heads of state and government of the East Asia Dialogue Partners support ASEAN's role in resolving the crisis in Myanmar through the mechanisms put in place in the past.
At the meeting, all countries supported multilateralism, which is an important factor in economic cooperation, security and economic recovery, especially the fight against Kovid 19. The meeting also discussed how to support tackling the challenges of climate change, especially at the upcoming meeting in the United Kingdom.
The East Asian powers support the core role of ASEAN in maintaining peace, stability and security in the region, and support ASEAN's central role in promoting cooperation. Not only that, but it provides support and assistance to ASEAN, especially in working to succeed in the fight against the 19-Kovid epidemic and to recover the economy after the 19-Kovid crisis.
In addition, for resolving issues in the region, the dialogue partners supported and encouraged ASEAN's core role by providing full cooperation and partnership to ASEAN.
Please note that October 27 is the second day of the ASEAN Summit and related summits hosted by Brunei. Today's meeting has four agendas: the 24th ASEAN-Japan Summit, the 1st ASEAN-Australia Summit, the 24th ASEAN Plus Three Summit and finally the Summit. 16th East Asia The meeting started from early morning until late at night.
The ASEAN Summit and related meetings will close tomorrow.
