Director General of Customs: No more tax exemption or reduction on duty-free vehicles, duty-free left-hand drive vehicles by December 31, 2021 and right-hand drive vehicles by June 30, 2022
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, confirmed that the General Department of Customs has no policy to exempt or reduce tax on duty-free vehicles after 10% concessions have been achieved so far.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Kun Nhem's participation in the press conference on the progress of the implementation of the collection of import duty on existing duty-free vehicles via video system on October 27, 2021.
Mr. Kun Nhim emphasized that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has provided all possible capabilities at the level of executive and technical work for the owners of vehicles under various license plates and duty-free and import duties throughout the country to meet tax obligations.
Responding to the question of whether the General Department of Customs has any other preferential policy on duty-free vehicles that take refuge under various license plates, duty-free and import duty, then decided to provide a 10% tax reduction and suspend the crackdown on vehicles in the country for a while. Past?
"It may not be possible to reduce it further because the 10 percent tax cut will also reduce the customs duty, so it would be appropriate to come in and meet the tax obligations," Kun Nhim said.
Mr. Kun Nhim said that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia within its jurisdiction is meeting to discuss as much as possible to help reduce taxes on left-hand drive vehicles that take refuge under various license plates and duty-free and right-hand drive vehicles. Tax-free.
In addition, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia said that the tax relief must also take into account those who import cars and have paid the tax, which is in accordance with the law to pay full tax to enter the national budget.
In fact, from September 9, 2021, when the General Department of Customs notified the duty-free vehicles to pay the tax until October 26, 2021, which is 40 days, there are 352 owners of left-hand drive vehicles. Came to pay taxes, tax revenue of 5.8 million US dollars.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, stated that from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia notify duty-free vehicles and both duty-free vehicles. Other license plates, both right and left, came to pay the tax, then the smuggling of right-hand drive cars through various corridors from Thailand into Cambodia no longer.
Mr. Kun Nhem made this statement at a press conference on the progress of the implementation of the collection of import duties on existing duty-free vehicles this morning, October 27, 2021, via video.
He added that at present, buyers of right-hand drive cars are burdened with both steering and taxes, so it is no longer possible to take refuge under other license plates, and the market for right-hand drive cars in Cambodia is declining. To zero, no one wants to buy a right-hand drive car anymore.
