(Phnom Penh): The assailant who killed Chea Bunheng by brutal torture, murder and rape in the past in Chbar Ampov district and was arrested by the authorities will be sentenced by the court on November 16 Upcoming 2021.
On the morning of October 27, 2021, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court held a trial in this case involving the perpetrator, On Phamon. Following the hearing, the President of the Trial Chamber announced that the verdict will be announced on 16 November 2021.
It should be reminded that on January 2, 2021, the body of the victim boy was found in a lake forest along Tiger Road in Boang Kanh 1 village, Prek Eang commune, Chbar Ampov district. At that time, the specialized police force immediately launched a search until the night of April 5, 2021, and arrested the perpetrator at Chroy Ampil pagoda in Chroy Ampil village, Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov for questioning.
After receiving a confession that he killed the child victim because he was angry, the grandmother-in-law hit him on the head once and forbade him to listen. At noon on April 6, 2021, the specialized police force brought the perpetrator back to the scene to simulate the act of killing his nephew.
In front of the police officer, the assailant confessed that he had actually killed the victim, who was his nephew, because he was angry and hit the victim twice on the head while he was not allowed to hit anyone on the head. By telling the victim not to listen, the assailant attacked and killed the victim.
A 10-year-old boy disappeared on March 31, 2021 and was found dead in the forest on April 2, 2021, along Tiger Street in Boangkanh 1 village. Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov is suspected of murder. The victim was identified as Chea Bunheng, a resident of Chroy Ampil village, Kbal Koh commune.
