(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the ASEAN Plus Three Mechanism, which includes ASEAN member countries plus China, Japan and South Korea, continues to be an indispensable driving force in promoting cooperation. In East Asia, as well as in responding to crises effectively.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized this at the 24th ASEAN Plus Three Summit held on October 27, 2021. In the presence of ASEAN and Plus 3 leaders, Samdech Techo emphasized that in the context of the continued spread of Kovid-19, ASEAN + 3 is still an important growth engine for promoting socio-economic development in the region. And universal.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen provided some views to participate in strengthening ASEAN Plus Three cooperation. Those views include:
First, Cambodia appreciates the active efforts of the Plus Three countries in contributing to the fight against Kovid-19 by providing vaccines and medical equipment to Cambodia and other ASEAN member countries. At the same time, in the spirit of continuing to promote the health and well-being of the people, Samdech Techo announced the support for the release of the "ASEAN Plus Three Leaders' Statement on Mental Health Cooperation among Adolescents and Children."
Third, Samdech Techo requested ASEAN Plus Three countries to continue to enhance the effective implementation of the ASEAN Plus Three Action Plan on Reducing the Economic Impact of Kovid-19 and the ASEAN Plus Three Economic Cooperation Work Program 2021. 2022.
Samdech Techo stressed the need to ratify the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) from ASEAN Plus Three countries to ensure the entry into force of this agreement in early 2022 to promote the restoration and promotion Regional economic growth.
Fourth, Samdech Techo Prime Minister highly appreciated the progress of the implementation of the ASEAN Plus Three Cooperation Plan 2018-2022.
The Minister of Water Resources is continuing to lead the intervention to close the dam site to avoid any possible risk to the people living in front of the water.
