However, after the flood in Stung Prek Tnaot, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has already prepared 36 heavy machinery, large and small sandbags, rock nets and intervention forces along the Stung Delta Dam. To prevent the risk of flooding, which can cause flooding to people's homes in the western part of Phnom Penh and Kandal province, ie 24 hours a day.
According to the report of Dangkor district authority, the dam in Stung Prek Tnaot affected 4 villages in Dangkor district, including 53 villages of Kantuy Teuk, 93 houses in Thmor village, 85 villages in Kraing village. A total of 306 houses in 74 villages, however, the disaster did not last any longer if it was prevented in time.
As of this evening, the situation at the site of the dam has been controlled and is being monitored for fear of another spill that could affect residents.
