Australian Ambassador: Over the next three years, Australia will provide about A $ 15 million for the implementation of the Social Accountability Framework in Cambodia.
This statement was made by the Australian Ambassador on October 27, 2021, on the occasion that he was allowed to meet with Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, at the Ministry's office.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked the Australian Government through the Ambassador and expressed his belief that this assistance is also a contribution to the implementation of the Royal Government of Cambodia's 10-year national program to continue the process of decentralization and reform. Decentralization as well.
In connection with the above, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also informed about some updates related to the work of decentralization and deconcentration reform in Cambodia. This format has prepared a national plan for the next 10 years from 2021 to 2030.
