Regarding the issue of cooperation between law enforcement forces of the two countries, the Ambassador informed Samdech Krala Hom that although Cambodia has faced the situation of Kovid 19, but he highly appreciated this good cooperation, in which some programs continue to be implemented. Like training, capacity building and cooperation, research and suppression of some crimes also continue to actively cooperate with each other.
Mr. Pablo Kang also informed the Prince that while the Royal Government of Cambodia is preparing to reopen the border, the Australian side also organized a training program to strengthen the capacity of law enforcement forces, especially immigration officials to strengthen and increase Efficient management of border gates to be effective when processing border reopening.
In this regard, Prince Kralahom also expressed his appreciation for the cooperation between the two sides in the past. He also called on the Australian side, through the ambassador, to work more closely on drug-related crime, which is on the rise in the world.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked the Government of Australia for its continued support to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the past, both in the prevention of Kovid 19 disease and in support of various sectors in Cambodia, including strengthening cooperation. Law Enforcement Work - KOICA Provides Online Training on "Capacity Building on Mechanisms for the Promotion and Protection of Human Rights in Cambodia"
KOICA has resumed its online training, considering that it will be difficult to implement a direct training program in Korea this year due to the Kovid-19 epidemic. The purpose of this online training is to contribute to the achievement of the capacity to understand the international human rights system and to develop human rights policies.
This year, KOICA organized an online training course on "Capacity Building on Mechanisms for the Promotion and Protection of Human Rights in Cambodia" from 2 to 8 November 2021. The 7-day online training course is for 22 officials from the Cambodian Human Rights Committee.
This important training course is designed to: First, provide references to the Korean experience for the improvement of human rights in Cambodia; Second, to assist in the improvement and modernization of peace and education. Human Rights 3: Strengthen the capacity of civil servants of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to strengthen human rights policy.
In addition, participants will create an action plan that incorporates knowledge from learning, discussion, experience and exploration during the training session. The action plan is the main activity of the program, which gives participants the opportunity to write actionable and feasible action plans to provide options as well as solutions to issues raised in the country report.
In Cambodia, KOICA works on a wide range of technical aspects of programs and projects that have a significant impact on Cambodia's development, such as improving nutrition and student well-being, capacity building of teachers, public health, agriculture, and infrastructure. Innovative ship.
From 1994 to 2020, KOICA invited about 3,200 government officials to participate in short-term training and master internships in the Republic of Korea under the KOICA-KOICA Capacity Building Program. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Continues to Attend the 24th ASEAN Plus Three Summit
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 27, 2021, attended the 24th ASEAN Plus Three Summit, a meeting between the leaders of ASEAN countries and the leaders of China, Japan and Korea. South.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that at this meeting, the ASEAN Plus Three Heads of Government approved a document, the Joint Declaration of the ASEAN Plus Three Leaders on Cooperation on Mental Health, Youth and Children. ASEAN Plus Three Leaders also approved a document, the Fourth Progress Report on the Implementation of the ASEAN Plus Three Cooperation Action Plan 2018-2022.
ASEAN + 3 leaders noted the growth of cooperation within the framework of ASEAN + 3, which began in 1997, when there was a financial crisis in Asia. Since then, the ASEAN Plus Three Leaders' Annual Meeting can be considered as an important mechanism for East Asian cooperation as well.
At the meeting, ASEAN + 3 leaders highlighted the work done together in the fight against Kovid 19. In addition, the three countries also pay attention to help ASEAN countries, especially in the field of public health, which is an important work.
The ASEAN Plus Three Prime Minister also highlighted that the ASEAN Plus Three Work Plan and Cooperation will be completed this year and will be completed next year, and the promotion of a new ASEAN Plus Three Work Plan for 2023-2027. And to be adopted in 2022 during Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN.
In addition, the ASEAN + 3 Heads of Government also highlighted the cooperation that needs to be continued: economic recovery, strengthening economic cooperation. Promoting, in particular, the framework for regional economic partnership in all fields, which must be ratified by ASEAN Plus Three countries to ensure that this agreement enters into force in early 2022.
The ASEAN Heads of Government requested the three countries to continue to support the existing mechanisms, especially the framework for travel and the establishment of new mechanisms for public health within the ASEAN framework. In addition, the ASEAN + 3 heads of government also discussed the situation in the region, especially the situation on the Korean Peninsula and in Myanmar.
