ACT meets with Kampong Chhnang journalists to strengthen their ability to write and disseminate information in a professional manner
(Kampong Chhnang): The Organization for Conflict Resolution (ACT) on the afternoon of October 26, 2021 at Chamkar Leap Restaurant, Kampong Chhnang City held a meeting with journalists in 7 institutions in Kampong Chhnang to help strengthen the capacity of Journalists in writing and disseminating information in accordance with the code of ethics and professionalism and the law on the press.
In this meeting, the journalists of each institution raised the issue of writing and disseminating information in the past, which challenges for the ACT team to guide and address in order to strengthen their ability to write and disseminate information. Comply with professional ethics and in accordance with the law on the press of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
"In order to be an honorable and valuable journalist in the society, we must adhere to the ethics and professionalism of journalists and abide by the law on the media," said Hang Chakra.
At the same time, in writing news, you have to be a journalist, not a jurisdiction or a court, and remember the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to say, "Do not violate the rights of others and do not Distort the truth.
