In the first nine months of 2021, there were 1,257 cases of dengue fever and three deaths compared to the same period in 2020, a decrease of more than eight times to 9,128. Eleven deaths. Despite the decrease, the cases are scattered across four geographical areas, especially in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu and Takeo. For some provinces, there are no cases of dengue fever, such as Prey Veng.
Dr. Huy Rekul, director of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Laboratory, told Fresh News that the drop in dengue cases was due to the fact that people were more aware of preventive measures and cared for their children. When he was sick, he was rushed to a government hospital for timely treatment.
"On behalf of the leaders of the National Dengue Fever Program, I would like to express my deep gratitude for the constant encouragement of the leaders of the Ministry of Health, especially Prof. Mam Bun Heng, Minister of Health, who worked hard. However, I have received good cooperation with national and international partners, especially cooperation at both national and sub-national levels, in addition to the Cambodian Red Cross.
Mr. Huy Rekol said that the Cambodian Red Cross, headed by Luang Men Norodom Monineath Sihanouk as the Honorary President and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as the President, pays high attention to the well-being and rescue of vulnerable people everywhere. And all the time, especially to improve living standards, education and well-being.
In fact, during the rainy season, there may be various diseases, including dengue fever or chickenpox, which are life-threatening, so the Cambodian Red Cross has always been involved in the prevention and control of dengue fever or chickenpox. Very effectively, by applying Abet spray, tiger mosquito repellent, which is a transmitting agent of dengue fever and chi, especially to educate people in the backyard.
On that occasion, Dr. Huy Rekul expressed his gratitude and thanks to Luang Men Norodom Monineath Sihanouk and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, leaders, leaders and volunteers of the Cambodian Red Cross who always participate in all activities to help improve life and well-being. Of the people in all circumstances and at all times.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Pheng, Permanent Vice President of Prey Veng Branch Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, told Fresh News that every rainy season, the Prey Veng Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross as well as the Provincial Health Department always cooperate to educate people about the disease. Others, especially dengue fever and chickenpox, which cause serious health hazards leading to loss of life.
At the same time, the Cambodian Red Cross Youth Volunteer, Miss Touch Theary, also vowed to continue educating the people about the prevention of dengue fever and chickenpox, as well as other activities, despite the situation of Kovid 19.
It should be noted that under the humanitarian activities and work to improve the lives and well-being of the Cambodian Red Cross and the Cambodian Red Cross Branch, especially the outreach to educate people in the backyard about dengue fever and chickenpox, people raised similar opinions. It's a very special work activity that has helped raise awareness of the most effective preventive measures that can save people from the dangers of these diseases.
Ms. Yim Navy, who lives in Kampong Leav commune, Prey Veng city, Prey Veng province, said, "The work of educating our people in the villages of the commune is very good because we have a better understanding of the prevention and elimination of tiger mosquito nets. As a transmitting agent of dengue fever and chickenpox. "In the past, our people here have always been reluctant to understand these protection rules."
Ms. Sem Yoeun, who lives in Kampong Leav village, Prey Veng city, Prey Veng province, also said, "I am very happy to receive continuous attention after all the leaders, especially during the rainy season, the Ministry of Health and the Cambodian Red Cross. "Working together to educate about health care to avoid various diseases, especially dengue fever and chickenpox, we have a better understanding and no more worries about this disease."
