(Phnom Penh): Watch the full video of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the ASEAN Summit, ASEAN-Korea Summit, ASEAN-China Summit and ASEAN-US Summit on October 26, 2021. Watch the full video: Samdech Techo Hun Sen attends the 9th ASEAN-US Summit, Mr. Biden declares strong support for development in ASEAN
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continues to attend the 9th ASEAN-US Summit on the night of October 26, 2021.
The meeting, hosted by Brunei Darussalam, was attended by US President Joe Biden, his first meeting with ASEAN leaders after winning the US presidency. The meeting was also attended by eight other ASEAN leaders, with no representative from Myanmar.
Kao Kim Hourn, Deputy Prime Minister, said that during the meeting, the ASEAN and US Heads of Government praised the progress and achievements of the ASEAN-US Strategic Partnership. In particular, cooperation in many areas, such as Kovid 19, which the United States has provided a lot of support in the bilateral framework, including assistance to ASEAN and individual member countries.
In addition, the ASEAN Heads of Government commended the US support for ASEAN Community Building, ASEAN Integration and the Fight against Kovid 19. In particular, promoting economic development, increasing trade and investment.
US President Joe Biden has announced that the United States will provide an additional $ 102 million for cooperation with ASEAN, and the United States will continue to play a key role in ASEAN in regional cooperation, especially in the Indo-Pacific framework.
The ASEAN Head of Government also stated that ASEAN will promote other sectors, especially digital. The ASEAN Heads of Government also pledged to maintain peace, stability and security in the ASEAN region. The ASEAN and US Heads of Government also announced that next year the United States and ASEAN will celebrate the 45th anniversary of the US-ASEAN partnership.
According to Kao Kim Hourn, the ASEAN and US heads of government also exchanged views on the situation in Myanmar and the South China Sea.
President Joe Biden also said that what the United States is having with ASEAN is a strong relationship and the United States is highly committed to continuing to support ASEAN by continuing to cooperate in many areas. The president said that in the past, the United States has provided more than 40 million doses of 19 vaccines and more than $ 200 million in aid to fight 19 measles.
The president said the United States should share one billion doses of the vaccine.
The US President also announced the opening of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) in Hanoi, Vietnam. Mr Biden said ASEAN has played a key role in the region, not only in economics and markets, but also in promoting regional cooperation between ASEAN and the United States in the region.
The US President also expressed hope that ASEAN would join the United States in the fight against climate change. The US President also mentioned the role of ASEAN in facilitating, in particular, security cooperation.
It should be noted that today, Samdech Techo Hun Sen spent a full day attending the ASEAN Summit, the ASEAN-Korea Summit, the ASEAN-China Summit and the latest ASEAN-US Summit. Mr. Heng Sour: Youth is a potential resource and a core force driving growth and socio-economic development.
