(Phnom Penh): The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on the night of October 26, 2021, announced the provision of 200,000 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine to the Vietnamese government to help prevent Kovid 19 disease, according to Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry. Health and the chairman of the National Committee for the Kovid 19 vaccination nationwide told Fresh News earlier.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has appointed Ms. O Vandin, High Representative of Samdech, to hand over the vaccine to the Vietnamese government on the morning of October 29 at the Bavet-Mok Pai border in Svay Rieng province.
Vietnam was the second country in Cambodia to provide 19 doses of Kovid, while Laos was the first country to provide 200,000 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine on September 28.
