Well-known businessmen: Cambodia-Korea free trade agreement will bring more Cambodian investment, production, processing and export
(Phnom Penh): After the free trade agreement between Cambodia and South Korea was officially signed on October 26, 2021, Cambodian businessmen have expressed their congratulations that this agreement will make Cambodia accept More and more Korean investors are coming to Korea to produce and process products for export, as the traders are ready to co-invest as well as prepare products for export to Korea.
At a time when Cambodia is peaceful, social well-being through the Kovid 19 vaccination has reached almost the entire population and safety factors will be able to attract investment in light, medium and heavy industries to Cambodia in the future. .
He said that although it was seen that Cambodia could benefit from an imbalance with Korea, it would be better not to have an agreement.
Neak Oknha Sear Rithy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Wordbridge Group, believes that through the Cambodia-Korea agreement, investors will look to Cambodia for investment, and in order for Cambodia to benefit from this agreement, local investors must be prepared. Ready to welcome investors from abroad to invest together for production and export to Korea.
He believes that Cambodia should strengthen the processing of food products, fruits and industries that the Korean market is in need.
He said that with the participation of stakeholders, both producers, exporters and exporters, the private sector, as well as cooperation from the public sector, will make Cambodia's exports ahead of proportion with. And import.
He said that as a private sector that invests in agriculture and agro-production, he expects that after the trade agreement between Cambodia and Korea will help expand the export market, increase volume and get more value, while in the past, Cambodia relied heavily on Exported to two neighboring countries, Thailand and Vietnam.
The Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement was officially launched on July 9, 2020 via video by the two countries' trade ministers, and went through a total of 12 rounds of negotiations before reaching its signing. Now.
The agreement will boost export growth, increase gross domestic product and increase employment opportunities, as well as help the two countries' economies recover more quickly from Kovid-19. Promote more Cambodian exports to the Republic of Korea, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
