More than 2,000 tons of rice a day are exported to Vietnam through Prey Vally international border crossing in Svay Rieng province, but the price of rice is lower than last year
(Svay Rieng): About 2,000 tons of rice a day is sold to Vietnam by traders at the port of the military canal at the Prey Vally International Border Crossing in Svay Rieng province, but farmers have complained about the low price of rice. More than last year due to the Kovid 19 crisis.
The source added that "the collection of rice from farmers to produce cheaper than 2020 is the reason for the high cost of services on transportation costs, workers to lift the car, unload the boat and pay the Vietnamese authorities is in a boat. The Vietnamese authorities took 1,500,000 VND, equivalent to 275,000 riels, and then they sent a boat to transport rice in our Khmer port.
Sources from rice traders said, however, that it was good that the Svay Rieng provincial authorities had facilitated relations with the Vietnamese side, asking Vietnam to come and collect rice for the Cambodian ferry port. In September and October 2021, an average of more than 2,000 tons of rice per day will be exported to Vietnam by the Vine soldiers, and in the near future, the rainy season will come. In addition, rice exports to Vietnam will double.
