Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks ASEAN Leaders to Accelerate Decisions on Accepting Timor-Leste (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks Cambodian Leaders to Accelerate Decisions Acceptance of Timor-Leste as a new member of ASEAN, as Samdech noted that the country has made great efforts to meet the conditions in line with this Southeast Asian organization.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's proposal was made at the 38th and 39th ASEAN Summit via video this morning, Tuesday, October 26, 2021. The meeting, hosted by Brunei Darussalam, was held under the theme "We take care, we prepare, we move forward".
In addition to the key issues on the Kovid 19 pandemic and the recovery of ASEAN countries after the Kovid 19 crisis, the topic of Timor-Leste's application for ASEAN membership was also discussed.
Timor-Leste has been known to seek ASEAN membership for many years, but has not yet achieved results due to disagreements from some ASEAN member states. Cambodia has made great efforts to help Timor-Leste become a member of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations.
At the ASEAN Summit, which was not attended by Myanmar, Hun Sen said he saw Timor-Leste work hard to meet ASEAN requirements, but some ASEAN member states ignored Timor-Leste's efforts.
Samdech Techo also expressed concern over the isolation of Timor-Leste in the event of geopolitical competition in Southeast Asia.
With the above concerns, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the leaders of all ASEAN member countries to expedite their decision to accept Timor-Leste as an ASEAN member.
