General knowledge: There is a place on earth where there has been no rain for more than 2 million years
Technically, the term "desert" is defined as the area with the lowest rainfall of less than 25.4 cm per year. The Sahara receives less than 2.54 centimeters of rain per year.
The driest place in the world after the dry valley is in the Atacama Desert of Chile, where some areas have been without rain for almost 200 years and the average annual rainfall is less than 0.01 cm. Thus, compared to all the sandy beaches, it ranks as the driest desert in the world, or 254 times drier than the Sahara.
