Rice at Banteay Srei roundabout is attracting the public
(Siem Reap): Banteay Srei district is a district with beautiful Banteay Srei temples that attract tourists to visit this temple. After visiting the temple, tourists who continue their journey to Phnom Kulen must have seen the big roundabout in this town.
In the past, this roundabout was left untreated. At the end of 2020, the district administration began to rehabilitate with ornamental flowers and finally prepared to plant rice. The Banteay Srei district administration has switched from planting flowers to planting rice and is attracting the public to visit, not to mention planting flowers.
Heng Piseth, Banteay Srei district administration official, said that the reason why the district changed from flowers to rice was to make a difference and to share the rice with the local poor. Mr. Piseth added that planting rice provides more benefits than planting flowers, because when the flowers are damaged, it does not yield anything, but this season is also the rice planting season, so take this opportunity to plant seasonally and harvest rice. You are poor too.
Now the round rice has started to bear attractive fruit. Passengers who pass through this area rarely miss it, as they often visit and take pictures of themselves with rice in this circle.
Mr. Heng Piseth stated that the district administration is open to the public and has paved roads for easy access. However, he called on people to take care of the environment and not to pick up the rice that is growing well.
It should also be noted that the Banteay Srei district administration under the mandate of Mr. Khim Finang began to improve the Banteay Srei roundabout in December 2020, with a shower road. During the rice planting season, red brick roads were added to make it easier to walk, exercise and attract tourists.
