The Accounting and Auditing Regulator reminds enterprises to pay attention to the proper performance of their duties for the benefit of the enterprise, the public and the Royal Government.
(Phnom Penh): In response to the request of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, on the morning of October 25, 2021, the Accounting and Auditing Regulator of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority cooperated with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to organize an outreach workshop on "Accounting and Auditing Obligations" and "Relevant Provisions" for Members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Bou Tharin, Director General of Accounting and Auditing, and was attended by the management and officials of the Accounting and Auditing Regulator and Mr. Nguon Meng Tech, Director General of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and colleagues. And there are more than 225 participants in the Zoom program.
On that occasion, Mr. Oknha Nguon Meng Tech made a welcome speech and expressed his willingness to cooperate with the regulator to encourage members to participate in the implementation of the obligations required by law.
Mr. Butharin gave the opening remarks at the workshop, highlighting the benefits of accounting and auditing laws and the importance of workshops for enterprises, and outlined the obligations that enterprises must comply with in accordance with applicable laws and regulations related to the accounting sector. And auditing.
He stressed that the enterprise has to perform three essential obligations: to keep the accounting records, prepare the financial statements in accordance with the accounting standards in force and submit the financial statements to the independent audit in accordance with the law.
He also reminded all enterprises to pay attention to the proper implementation of obligations for the benefit of enterprises, the public and the Royal Government. Failure to comply with any obligation is subject to transaction penalties in accordance with the Sub-Decree on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing.
It should also be noted that the enactment of laws and regulations related to accounting and auditing is not a restriction or restriction on the business rights of investors and businessmen, but rather a tool for the promotion, protection, protection and Support business, investment, strengthen fiscal revenue and the national economy.
After the opening remarks of the Director General and the presentation by the technical officer on the legal aspects and relevant legal documents, the participants further clarified the implementation of the above three obligations and all the questions and questions raised by the participants During the workshop, Mr. Seng Tola, Deputy Director General, gave a clear answer to the workshop.
Please be informed that from 2021 onwards, the Accounting and Auditing Regulators will implement strict and thorough measures on the implementation of the accounting and auditing obligations of the enterprise. .
The Director General thanked and wished the management and officers of the Accounting and Auditing Regulators and the management of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and all the trainees good health, happiness and success in all tasks and avoiding all 19 Kovid diseases. Each other.
The Stung Bot-Nang Ian border crossing is a new international port that Cambodia and Thailand have agreed to build to serve the transportation of goods across the two countries' borders, and the Poipet international border crossing is reserved for tourists.
To serve the operation of this international border crossing, Cambodia and Thailand have built a bridge across the border and built various administrative buildings to provide services at this port. Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurates a bridge across the two countries' border and opened the construction site of various administrative buildings on April 22, 2019.
Currently, both Cambodia and Thailand are speeding up the construction of buildings and infrastructure to provide services on the transportation of goods across the border between the two countries. Construction is almost complete, too.
The opening of the new Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ian International Border Crossing is the opening of a new page in history to facilitate cross-border trade between Cambodia and Thailand and to promote the logistics system in Cambodia.
Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and Mr. Jurin Lak Sanavisit, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Commerce of Thailand, on October 25, 2021, met yesterday to speed up the opening of this port. The reunion follows Sok Sokretya's request for the Thai side to expedite the opening of the gate in September.
During the meeting, Jurin Lak Sanavisit asked Cambodia to prepare containers and relevant authorities to facilitate the official opening of the Stung Bot-Nang Ian international border crossing in January 2022.
