(Phnom Penh): Police from the Criminal Bureau of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie arrested a man who was the owner of a car dealership on the afternoon of October 24 and sent him to court in connection with the non-performance of obligations for traded instruments. In case of non-cash check (check), more than 200,000 USD.
According to the police, the owner of the car, Phat Vuthy, alias Chruy, male, 42 years old, is a salesman and resides in Kork Chambok village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the complaint, Phat Wutty borrowed money from creditors three times, totaling $ 463,300, to buy 11 cars to put up for sale at a profit to repay the plaintiff. .
However, when the owner of the car sold the car, the suspect did not return the full amount to the plaintiff, more than 200,000 US dollars was missing, and the suspect used two checks to give to the plaintiff, who were all dirty. There is no deposit in the bank and even avoid the debt.
During the interrogation phase, the owner of the car that was the victim of the criminal lawsuit acknowledged the truth, but he paid the money to the plaintiffs in a series of stages and there was no fraudulent idea not to pay.
