(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has urged ASEAN to focus on promoting the socio-economic digital transformation, especially in promoting the adoption of digital technology for business to promote sustainability and development resilience. Area.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks on the afternoon of October 25, 2021, on the occasion of Samdech's keynote address via video at the closing ceremony of the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit under the theme: "Building a Digital Future". "Our sustainability."
Samdech Techo noted that the development of the digital economy is bringing many opportunities that not only provide new sources of economic growth, but also can increase economic productivity.
He added that accelerating regional and global integration is also one of the top priorities to promote recovery and promote sustainable socio-economic development. ASEAN must continue to adhere to a multilateral approach, strengthen globalization and strive to achieve the regional integration agenda under the ASEAN Vision 2025 to strengthen closer ties between social and economic life.
Samdech Techo added: "We need to pay more attention to the important tasks, including: promoting the liberalization of trade, services and investment more fully and in depth, facilitating cross-border travel. "Safe, capacity building of micro-enterprises, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) and so on."
Taking this opportunity, Samdech also mentioned some important roles of the private sector in contributing to the achievement of priority work and ASEAN work plan in 2022 as follows:
First, make the most of the existing ASEAN Free Trade Agreement, especially the ASEAN Agreement (RCEP), which is scheduled to enter into force in early 2022 to boost trade and investment activities, especially direct investment promotion. From abroad to create jobs, increase people's income and boost economic growth.
Second, contribute to the development of human resources through the transfer of technology, knowledge and skills, especially the development of digital skills, as well as the promotion of science, technology and innovation through cooperation with business and foreign direct investment that helps reduce The digital gap and the development of the digital economy in the region.
Third, to enhance cooperation between the public and private sectors, especially through public-private partnership mechanisms in order to mobilize financial resources for the development and implementation of initiatives to help meet the financial needs for Rehabilitate socio-economic development.
