(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on October 25, 2021, sent a letter of respect to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to express his gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Techo for the initiative. Amend the Constitution to determine the top leadership "has only one Khmer nationality" which was approved by the National Assembly on October 25.
The Prime Minister's high initiative in drafting the Constitution confirms the deep patriotic and unwavering patriotic ideals of the Prime Minister to the motherland.
In addition to my sincere greetings and unwavering devotion, I would like to extend my best wishes to Samdech Techo Prime Minister so that he can achieve new great achievements in his noble mission. Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. National Assembly fully approves draft law on public-private partnership
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia has fully approved the draft law on public-private partnership proposed by the Royal Government. This approval was made in the plenary session of the National Assembly on October 25, 2021 by a vote of 107 out of 111.
The National Assembly session was chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, with the participation of 111 members of the National Assembly. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who initiated the law, and representatives of relevant ministries will also attend the meeting.
The draft law on public-private partnership was approved by the Plenary Session of the Council of Ministers on October 8, 2021 and submitted to the National Assembly. After being handed over to the National Assembly's Expert Review and Study Committee, the draft law on public-private partnerships was submitted to the plenary session for discussion and approval.
The draft law will establish a clear, transparent and accountable legal framework and complement some of the necessary procedures and guidelines that the Concession Law does not provide, in other words, to ensure that the project development process is mechanized. The NRC operates in accordance with a common framework and procedures provided and / or promises to provide state financial support and / or other support for the project.
The draft law also sets out the procurement procedures for the selection of private partners to implement the PBV project. And financial support mechanisms, as well as investment incentives for the NRC project.
The draft law on public-private partnerships will be an important legal framework for creating a conducive environment to further promote private sector participation in the development of public infrastructure and the provision of better public services to boost economic growth. Recurrence after the Kovid-19 crisis subsides and strengthens Cambodia's regional and global competitiveness.
This draft law on PNR is a new law instead of a law on concessions and is not a law on amendments.
At the same time, in order to fully and systematically implement the provisions of this draft law in accordance with the vision set out in the policy document on the development of the NRC mechanism for the management of public investment projects 2016-2020.
The draft law provides two key benefits: expanding the public financial space and the efficiency and innovation of the development and implementation of private sector projects.
