More than 600 troops ready to save people from the flood in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Troops from various units totaling more than 600 people and rescue equipment are ready to rescue people in Dangkor and Kambol districts facing flood tonight.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and in charge of Disaster Operations, Ministry of National Defense, told Fresh News on the night of October 25, 2021, the prepared forces include: 400 bodyguard commanders, 120 special zone soldiers, these forces joined the Phnom Penh Unity Command to hold the dam.
Separately, 120 naval forces with 30 units are ready in the special zone for intervention. In addition, there are some forces from the 70th Brigade, Special Forces Command and Engineering Command General Command.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, had issued an order to the army to be ready to rescue the people. In particular, it must be ensured that the floods will not affect the lives of the people.
Please note that the rain flowing from the Oral Mountains in Kampong Speu is filling the Stung Prek Tnaot and flooding some areas along the river in Dangkor and Kampol. Authorities have called on residents living along the river to be on high alert for the floods.
