Kovid 19 Vaccination Commission Continues to Donate 52 Vaccination Trucks to Capital-Provincial Health Departments
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for the Kovid Vaccination 19 Framework in Cambodia, on the afternoon of October 25, 2021, handed over an additional 52 vehicles for transporting vaccines to the Capital Health Department. 25 provinces with large population.
Ms. O Vandin said that the vehicle for transporting the vaccine, which was handed over to the Capital-Provincial Health Department on this occasion, was purchased with the help of philanthropists through Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
She added that the vaccine truck had to be ordered from abroad because it was not available in Cambodia. This vehicle is also suitable for transporting vaccines, which in the rear are stored in the air conditioner to ensure the quality of the vaccine.
According to Ms. O Vandin, this car is very important to serve the benefits of vaccination against Kovid 19 to people across Cambodia.
Please be informed that so far, a total of 100 Kovid 19 vaccination vehicles have been handed over to the 25 Capital-Provincial Health Departments, this is the fourth time.
UN envoy praises achievements in Libya since ceasefire
Tripoli: The United Nations (UN) envoy to Libya on Sunday praised the achievements of the Libyan 5 + 5 Joint Military Commission (JMC) since its visit. The signing of the Comprehensive Ceasefire Agreement in Geneva, Switzerland, a year ago. This was released by the Xinhua News Agency on Monday, October 25, 2021.
The UN envoy added that in early October, the JMC had just achieved another major goal by signing a comprehensive action plan for the removal of all mercenaries, foreign fighters and foreign forces. Libyan territory.
A serious armed conflict erupted in Libya in April 2019 between the military based in the east and the Libyan government in Tripoli, lasting more than a year before the commission. The JMC was formed with 10 military members from both sides (five on each side) and signed a ceasefire agreement in Geneva in October 2020. Cambodia, Korea to sign free trade agreement tomorrow
The Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement will be the second free trade agreement after the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement.
The agreement will further promote Cambodia's exports to Korea, including garments and textiles, electronics, especially agricultural products.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of October 25, 2021, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Commerce confirmed that the signing took place in the presence of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and his party. Korea.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated that "tomorrow, the 26th, there will be the signing of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement made by His Excellency Minister Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and the Korean component online."
According to Mr. Pen Sovicheat, after the signing of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement on October 26, 2021, both parties must meet their respective internal conditions.
The agreement shall pass through the Council of Ministers, then to the National Assembly, the Senate, before being signed by the King of Cambodia.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat confirmed that the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement will be launched in 2022 after the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement is launched in early 2022.
He stressed that the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement aims to strengthen economic partnership and expand the liberalization of bilateral trade, with mutual benefits aimed at enhancing economic benefits and the well-being of people and businesses. Of both countries.
Bilateral trade relations between Cambodia and Korea have been running smoothly. In fact, in the first eight months of 2021, from January to August 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and Korea reached more than 514 million US dollars, an increase of 11.52% compared to the same period in 2020.
In the first eight months of 2021, Cambodia exported more than 129 million US dollars to Korea, while imports from Korea amounted to more than 385 million US dollars. Cambodia's exports to Korea include garments, electronics, footwear, beverages, rubber bags, medicines and cardboard, etc.
While Cambodia imports most of its goods from Korea, such as textiles, trucks, beverages, electronics, machinery, home decor, medicines, soaps and plastic products.
Ministry of Water Resources announces flood risk in 14 Cambodian capitals and provinces
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on October 25, 2021 issued a notification on the weather situation, confirming the flooding in Phnom Penh, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Kandal, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Kampong Thom.
It is forecast that on October 25, 2021, this active low pressure will gradually develop into a low pressure or typhoon, reaching southern Vietnam on October 27, 2021. The above phenomenon will decrease the effect to low pressure when approaching the southern part of Cambodia.
According to the forecast, the weather in Cambodia from October 27 to 28, 2021 will be as follows:
1: Lowlands: Cloudy skies with moderate to heavy rain mixed with moderate gusts of rain and flooding in Phnom Penh, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Kandal, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang. Pursat and Kampong Thom provinces.
2. Dangrek Plateau and Cardamom Mountains: Cloudy skies with moderate to heavy rain mixed with strong gusts and floods in Mondul. Kiri, Tbong Khmum and Kampong Cham provinces.
3: Coastal areas: Cloudy skies, moderate to heavy scattered rain mixed with gusts will cause flooding in Kampot and Sihanoukville provinces. There will be rain, wind and high waves on the sea surface.
In light of the above-mentioned weather conditions, the public should be informed and take extra precautions to avoid any possible accidents.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has been closely monitoring this natural phenomenon and will provide further information in case of climate change.
