Chinese Foreign Minister visits Qatar for talks with Taliban
Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on March 25, 2013 Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on March 25, 2013 Qatar on October 25-26. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday afternoon, October 25, 2021.
Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin told a news conference in Beijing that the two sides would exchange views on the situation in Afghanistan and topics of common concern.
In mid-August, the previous Afghan government collapsed as the United States and its allies withdrew troops from the country, bringing the Taliban to power in a swift offensive. China has since pledged aid to the neighbor, urging the Taliban to crack down on all forms of terrorism.
The National Assembly presents the official results of its plenary session, which discussed and approved four agendas.
(Phnom Penh): On Monday morning, October 25, 2021, the National Assembly will continue its session to discuss and approve four agendas, including amendments to the Constitution regarding the determination of a single Khmer nationality for the Prime Minister, National Assembly President and Senate President. And the President of the Constitutional Council.
The meeting was chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and was attended by 111 members of the National Assembly. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who initiated the law, and representatives of relevant ministries will also attend the meeting.
In this plenary session, the National Assembly fully approved all agendas, including:
1: The election gives confidence in the addition of members of the Royal Government to HE Pa Socheatvong, Senior Minister in charge of special missions.
2. Approval of the Draft Law on the Approval of the Supplementary Agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations regarding the prosecution under Cambodian law of crimes committed during the period of Democratic Kampuchea. On the arrangements during the transition and completion of the Extraordinary Chambers.
3. Approval of the draft Constitution on the amendment of Article 19 (new), Article 82 (new), Article 106 (new), Article 119 (new), Article 119 (new) and Article 137 (new) of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 3 and Article 4 of the Constitution to supplement the process. As usual of national institutions.
4. Approve the draft law on public-private partnership.
