(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on October 25, 2021, attended the 72nd Meeting of the World Health Organization in the Western Pacific via video, in which he shared the song Five experiments in the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received a little earlier.
Please be informed that this is the annual meeting of the Minister of Health, which is attended by all 37 member countries and territories from 25 to 29 October 2021 in the form of a hybrid with a direct participation in Himeji, Japan and via video.
* First: Express appreciation for the significant achievements of the last year under the leadership of Dr. Cassay and the team of the World Health Organization. Cambodia supports the "Vision for the Future" document, which was adopted by member states two years ago and remains a guideline for the work of member countries.
* Second: Cambodia is a small country with a wide heart. Last year, Cambodia successfully managed to respond to 19 cases of Kovid, with fewer than 500 cases and no deaths. Under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as the support of all sectors and society as a whole, Cambodia has been able to continue to manage the 19 cases of Kovid.
* Third: Like other countries, Kovid 19 virus continues to circulate in Cambodia. We are working to prevent the spread of the virus, along with implementing three preventative measures. We are now in the process of revising the Kovid 19 response strategy to learn "how to live with the virus" while allowing for the safe reopening of schools and the economy.
Professor Mam Bunheng emphasized that he wanted to share four key factors that contribute to the success of Cambodia's response.
- First: Leadership in decision making and approach to the participation of the entire government - Second: Investment in health security and health systems - Third: Public participation, community and individual participation - Fourth: Solidarity And partnership.
* Fourth, Cambodia has made great efforts and ambitions to launch the national campaign to vaccinate Kovid 19 by vaccinating people from the age of 6 onwards in accordance with the "Flower Strategy" of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. As of October 24, 2021, 85.36% of the target population of 16 million people aged 6 years and over received 19 Kovid vaccines.
And fifth, stopping the epidemic is our common goal. Peace, social security, solidarity and cooperation are essential. Cambodia is working together with other countries, the World Health Organization and all partners for a better future towards a healthier and safer world.
The Minister of Health also stressed that Cambodia fully supports the leadership and coordination of the World Health Organization in the global response to Kovid 19 and expressed his deep gratitude to the World Health Organization (WHO). Special thanks to Dr. Takeshi Kasai, Regional Director of the Western Pacific and all member countries who have joined forces to fight Kovid 19 and are moving towards a better future.
