Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said that empowering the capital-provincial administrations to approve investment proposals of less than $ 5 million would force more factories to be set up in the provinces. That will contribute to reducing poverty in rural areas as well.
