At the meeting, Cambodia and Vietnam briefed each other on the current situation in their respective countries and the government's priorities, focusing on tackling the global epidemic of Kovid 19 virus and reviving the country's economy at the same time. Only one.
Both sides are pleased to note that despite the challenges posed by the global Kovid-19 pandemic, traditional friendship and close ties, as well as cooperation between the two countries, have continued to grow in all areas, including politics. And security, response to the global epidemic, Kovid-19, trade and investment, education and culture, tourism, energy, connectivity and cooperation between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs.
The two Co-Chairs stressed the important role of the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs in strengthening and expanding relations and cooperation between the two countries, based on the spirit of good neighborliness, solidarity, trust, mutual understanding and cooperation. Respect each other.
Regarding cooperation in the fields of defense and security, the two sides stressed the importance of strengthening coordination to prevent and combat criminal offenses, including drug-related crimes, smuggling and trafficking in timber and illegal weapons. Timely exchange of information.
Regarding border cooperation, the two sides welcomed the exchange of instruments of ratification of two key legal documents to record the completion of 84% of the demarcation and official demarcation of the land border between the two countries. The two sides agreed to speed up talks to find a mutually acceptable solution to the remaining 16% of the land border.
Both sides noted with satisfaction the positive trend of bilateral trade between Cambodia and Vietnam, despite the difficult economic situation prolonged by the global epidemic. Trade volume has steadily increased from $ 5.26 billion in 2019 to $ 5.33 billion in 2020 and will reach $ 6.03 billion in the first seven months of 2021. .
