Recently, Dr. Sok Sokretya visited the potential of tourism in Sisaket province, which borders Cambodia, especially the international border with Oddar Meanchey. On that occasion, Mr. Sok Sokretya also met with Mr. Vathana Puthychat, Governor of Sisaket Province to discuss the connection and promotion of tourism between Sisaket Province of Thailand with Cambodia.
Since Sisaket is one of Thailand's potential tourist destinations and borders Cambodia, Dr. Sok Sokretya sees it as a good point for Cambodia to attract tourists from this province to Cambodia if not for good cooperation. Between Sisaket province and tourism potential in Cambodia, especially Siem Reap.
In this spirit, Dr. Sok Sokretya made a number of proposals to the Governor of Sisaket Province to help encourage tourists to come to Cambodia, including the development of tourist areas along the border between Sisaket and Cambodia's bordering provinces.
During the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya also informed the Governor of Sisaket Province about the purpose of cooperating to promote the "Two Kingdoms, One Tourism Destination" campaign by organizing the "One Visa for Two Countries" project and further discussing cooperation with Sisaket Province in Opening a single visa to receive international tourists visiting both Cambodia and Thailand.
He also informed the Governor of Sisaket Province about the project to develop tourism destinations in Cambodia, especially recently, the Royal Government of Cambodia approved the implementation of the Siem Reap Provincial Development Master Plan 2021-2035. At this point, he saw opportunities for the development of religious tourism products, such as the worship of nine ancient Buddha statues, pagodas and the worship of nine sacred statues in Angkor and on Mount Kulen.
Mr. Sok Sokretya also requested for cooperation in monitoring the situation of the Kovid-19 epidemic at the Cambodian-Thai border.
It should be noted that during the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya also asked the Governor of Sisaket Province to examine the possibility of providing health and safety services to Cambodians living along the Cambodian-Thai border and Cambodian migrant workers working in Sisaket Province. Like the Thai people.
Dr. Sok Sokretya also informed about the outstanding leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to make Cambodia achieve complete peace, political stability and socio-economic development. .
