After heavy rain, Kampong Speu provincial authorities forced to open a stairway dam in Samrong Tong district, but did not cause harm to the people, the governor called on people to be more careful
(Kampong Speu): After a heavy rain in all districts in Kampong Speu province, the dam ladder was flooded with a lot of water that is beyond the capacity to store water, so the authorities were forced to open some water while At the bottom of the dam, there are also people living, but officials confirmed that some of the water is not dangerous to people.
It should be noted that this stairway dam is 2,600 meters long and is located in Kraing Ampil commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province.
However, Mr. Vy Samnang, on October 23, 2021, led the working group and relevant departments to inspect the situation and immediately resolve all the impacts caused by the floods, especially called for people. Extra caution.
Speaking to reporters, Mr. Vy Samnang said that throughout the night, the rain scattered in all districts in Kampong Speu province and caused some villages and communes to be flooded, houses, infrastructure and other agricultural crops to face. Will this flood.
He said that under the intervention of the district and municipal authorities and relevant departments, the situation was eased, the water flowed only for a short time, but in some vulnerable areas it took a long time.
Governor Vy Samnang only called on the people living downstream of the dam to show the utmost sympathy, as he claimed that the situation would return to normal in the short term.
Regarding the flood situation, Mr. Nhanh Cheab Hong, Director of Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, confirmed by telephone that the flood was not yet at the emergency level because the flooding was only for a short time. There will be no problems after the intervention, but if the rains continue in the next few days, challenges will likely arise on housing infrastructure, agricultural crops and mixed crops.
