(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that 30 years after the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991, Cambodia has become a country with high responsibility to the international community on an equal footing. The right to have a government that is fully responsible to its citizens for building a peaceful future, stability, dignity and development.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon further stated that Cambodia has clearly defined in its Constitution, upheld and protected the values, interests and national and international policies, and Cambodia will adhere to and absolutely protect independence, sovereignty, neutrality, permanence and integrity. Territory, as well as a strong commitment to fulfill all its international obligations in the region as well as globally.
