Starting from the first meeting also paved the way for a series of talks between Cambodians on all sides, especially Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, with the coordination of friendly countries, also reached the last meeting and advanced To the signing of an agreement on a common political solution of Cambodia on October 23, 1991 in France.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon once again expressed gratitude to all friendly countries that contributed to the 23 October 1991 Paris Peace Accords, a historic turning point 30 years ago.
General Knowledge: Who was the first successful aircraft builder?
The idea of building an airplane dates back to ancient Greece from 400 BC to the end of the 19th century, and caused a series of deaths during the testing of both machines. To be successful, they had to wait until the early 20th century.
On December 17, 1903, Wilbur and Orville succeeded in flying a machine-controlled, heavier-than-air aircraft. Wilbur flew for 59 seconds at an altitude of 260 meters, a great achievement. Both of their planes are named "The Flyer". Two years later, they also achieved an official aircraft that could be used for air travel.
The Wright brothers began selling aircraft in Europe before returning to the United States in 1909. Both became wealthy businessmen as their aircraft sold well in Europe and the United States. Wilbur died of typhoid fever in 1912, while Orville died in 1948 of a heart attack.
Although many different types of aircraft preceded the Ray family, most people considered the two to be the first successful aircraft builders. From the first aircraft that the Wright brothers built, this spacecraft has evolved to the present day.
