Experts view the insurance sector as an important financial safety net to protect against business or eventual health problems.
(Phnom Penh): Experts in the financial sector consider the insurance sector as an important financial safety net to help protect customers in case of business or health problems for any reason.
Seeing this importance, three associations, including the Banking Association of Cambodia, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and the Insurance Association of Cambodia, organized a joint workshop on "Benefits of Using Insurance Services" to raise awareness of the role of banking and financial institutions. And insurance companies to share experiences and practical work in the insurance sector in banking and finance.
Kea Boran encouraged the general public, especially those in rural areas, to understand the importance of protection and insurance services, as this will definitely contribute to creating a financial safety net in society to reduce risks. Individual and family level.
Huy Vatharo, President of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, said: "In the daily life of the individual, there are various risks that are events or accidents that happen by accident, causing financial difficulties, but those risks "Can be managed through a transfer to an insurance company."
He added that everyone should be aware of the risks they face and buy insurance that has the appropriate scope to protect those risks to maintain their financial stability when risks arise.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Superintendent of the National Bank of Cambodia Credit Insurance Services Provides a financial safety net that will ensure the ability to repay debts when customers face business or health issues that affect the source of income to repay their loans. To avoid selling collateral to pay off customer debt.
Mr. Bou Chanpirou, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, said that the insurance sector is a non-bank financial service that has been playing an important role in supporting the social security and economic sector.
He said that although the Kovid 19 crisis continues to spread globally, affecting the growth of the Cambodian economy and economy, the Cambodian insurance sector will continue to grow, maintaining a positive growth rate of about 8% in 2020. Increase by about 10 percent in 2021.
He said that despite this growth, if we look at the insurance contribution rate in the Cambodian economy is only 1.04 percent and the insurance density is only about 17.26 dollars per person in 2020 is still low. Compared to the region.
