Thai Minister of Industry Wants to See Cambodia Support Its Investors (Video inside) (Thailand): Thai Minister of Industry Surya: Rongcheung Rongroeurngkit has asked Cambodia to provide support to Thai investors seeking business partners and Cambodian investors to strengthen sector ties. Trade between the two countries is better.
Mr. Suryak Chhongrongroeungkhet's request was made during a meeting with Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia, who is visiting Thailand.
During the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya and the Minister of Industry of Thailand discussed the focus on investment and raised some issues to find a compromise for investors between the two countries. Especially Thai investors in Cambodia.
During the meeting, the Thai Minister of Commerce praised the Royal Government of Cambodia for giving importance to the food processing industry, agro-industry, tourism industry and automobile industry. The Minister is confident that Cambodia will be successful in the Industrial Revolution 4.0 (digital technology) in the near future, and Thailand is always ready to cooperate with Cambodia.
The minister also expressed high interest in cross-border trade between the two countries. The Thai Minister of Industry said that cross-border trade really contributes significantly to the economy between the two countries. The minister also expressed the expectation that the trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand would be even larger than at present.
Responding to the request and desire of the Minister of Industry of Thailand, Dr. Sok Sokretya promised to bring this proposal to the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen for review.
Dr. Sok Sokretya also informed the Thai Minister of Industry that Cambodia really needs the support of the Royal Government of Thailand to strengthen the expansion of small and medium enterprises (SMEs), especially in the field of tourism. Mr. Sokretya also expressed strong hope that the goods resulting from the cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand will be distributed and recognized around the world.
Samdech Techo's personal adviser also thanked the Royal Government, business people and the people of Thailand for their active support of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in Cambodia, which has grown steadily every year. As for border trade between the two countries during this period, let the Thai side reduce some unnecessary procedures.
During the meeting, both sides also stressed the importance of the Thai and Cambodian tourism industries. The uniqueness of this business is that it uses less capital but is more profitable. In particular, the unique product of Angkor Wat, Cambodia, a World Heritage Site, attracts tourists from around the world.
During the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya also informed his Thai counterpart about the Royal Government of Cambodia's readiness to reopen the country in all areas by the end of October 2021, by reducing the number of foreign tourists. . He also briefed the Thai Minister of Industry on Cambodia's success in combating Kovid 19 and vaccinating more than 85 percent of the country's population.
