Today marks the 30th anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords! Sihanouk-Hun Sen pushes for this agreement
The war between the Phnom Penh army of the People's Republic of Kampuchea, led by Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, was backed by Vietnam and with the Soviet Union as the backbone of the Khmer Rouge army, loyalists of Sihanouk and Ta Son San. The Cambodian-Thai border, backed by China and the United States, for about a decade still encroached on Cambodian territory and could not keep Cambodians safe.
It is a precious fortune for the Cambodian people that the dark pages of the war have gradually faded after Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, then known as Comrade Hun Sen, worked hard to find them. Find a negotiation to end the flames of war that plague Cambodian society through the Paris Peace Accords, an agreement to end the political crisis and war crisis in Cambodia.
But there are some views that do not understand that. The weakening of the Soviet Union's influence over the Cambodian government, the end of the Cold War, and the support of foreign friends were all contributions to the search for peace in Cambodia. But the diminishing influence and contribution to finding a solution for a friendly country is not the only cause of extinguishing the flames of war in Cambodia.
Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, also highly valued the characters of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the characters pushing for this agreement. Dr. Sok Touch argued that there are some countries that, although the superpower has collapsed, has not been able to find an agreement that leads to peace. Countries include Afghanistan, Angola and Nigeria.
For achieving this agreement, Dr. Sok Touch gave another high value for Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Mr. Sok Touch considered Samdech Techo as the water that flowed through all obstacles and problems of Cambodia leading to this peace talks.
Mr. Sok Touch pointed out that at that time, Samdech Techo was a party that covered up to 90 percent of the territory that the tripartite forces could not defeat the Cambodian regime. For this reason, if Samdech Techo Hun Sen does not open talks to bring Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and the other parties out of the forest, the Paris Agreement could not exist.
Through Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message, as well as Dr. Sok Touch's statement, it is clear that the October 23, 1991 talks were born out of the spirit of national unity, born of Khmer and Khmer.
The Paris Peace Accords paved the way for Cambodia to build a new regime, have elections and a constitution, and end the Vietnamese military presence on Cambodian soil. In particular, this agreement brought the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, back to Cambodia on November 14, 1991, establishing a new Kingdom under a single constitution, a single force and a single administrative region. .
The Paris Peace Accords also helped Cambodia to make steady progress from a quiet country from an economic ally to an internationally recognized country in terms of economy, politics, development and many other areas. Also, under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia from the Cambodian People's Party emerged from the election headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Overall, October 23, 1991 was a clear demonstration of the steps taken to end the conflict between Cambodians and Cambodians under Cambodian family negotiations, not foreigners. October 23 has become a mirror of the spirit of unity that Cambodian politicians of all persuasions and all Cambodians should adhere to in solving national problems to avoid the flames of war and push the nation forward.
