Preah Sihanouk provincial authorities launched an operation to crack down on forest encroachment in Prey Nob district, arrested 43 people, 6 of whom were sent to the provincial commissioner for further action
(Preah Sihanouk): The Joint Forces of Preah Sihanouk Province on October 22, 2021 launched an operation to crack down on illegal forest encroachment in Prey Nob District, detaining 43 people, of which 6 were sent. Hold the provincial police commission to take further action. This is according to Mr. Kheang Phirum, spokesman for Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall, confirmed to Fresh News on the night of October 22.
He said that 37 other stakeholders, after being questioned and contracted, were asked by their commune chiefs to return home.
The spokesman said that the operation to crack down on illegal forest encroachment was carried out with the guidance of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, the provincial governor, and the coordination of the procedure by the prosecutor of the provincial court. Went to the scene for the second time to arrest 43 people who were on the scene, 08 women.
It should be noted that at 2 pm on October 21, 2021, yesterday, the Forestry Administration District, in cooperation with the Prey Nob and Stung Hav District Unity Command, inspected and prevented the clearing of forest land at the bottom of the pot in Tuol Toteung village. 2 Toul Toteung commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
According to Mr. Kheang Phirum, when the joint team arrived at the scene, they saw 58 people clearing forest land and setting up tents for shelter. The joint team advised them to stop. Activity and return home.
Around this case, he confirmed that according to the answers of the people, both in and outside the province were deceived by brokers organized by the organization to clear the forest to divide the land.
It should also be noted that the joint team spent many hours explaining the law and other instructions, but they did not listen and used violence to throw gas canisters at the police to avoid clashes. Only then did the joint team withdraw to wait for further guidance.
The provincial administration calls on all citizens not to be deceived by brokers and crooks by inciting them to encroach on forest land, take ownership or encroach on private land and use violence against public officials. This will make you a criminal and will face further legal action. Evergrande escapes debt default after paying more than $ 80 million in interest
The payoff is the latest development in a series of events that have attracted the attention of many world-class investors in the near-collapse of this huge company.
For more than a month now, there has been speculation of bankruptcy for the company, fueling a credit crunch among other indebted real estate developers and undermining confidence in the real estate market. China, which accounts for about a quarter of the Chinese economy.
US bans import of Malaysian rubber gloves due to forced labor
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States has banned the import of rubber gloves from a Malaysian glove maker on allegations of forced labor. According to Reuters.
Malaysia is home to millions of migrant workers looking for work in manufacturing and agriculture, but critics say they are often abused.
The U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) announced a ban on imports of Supermax rubber gloves on Wednesday after an investigation found signs of forced labor in the company's manufacturing operations. .
The U.S. Customs and Excise Department did not provide details on allegations of labor abuse at the company, which exports gloves to more than 160 countries and can produce up to 24 billion gloves. Condoms per year.
