Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Encourages US-ASEAN Business Council to Examine the Potential to Increase Trade Activities in Potential Sectors in Cambodia
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng received this encouragement on the occasion of Samdech received a delegation from the US-ASEAN Business Council via video from the Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of October 22, 2021.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked for the important discussions and exchanges of opinions that will contribute to serve the interests and support each other to respond to the impact and challenges posed by Kovid's disease 19. He said that turning problems into opportunities is very important in the current situation to live normally in a new way.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng strongly believes that through close cooperation in key areas such as security, trade, health, finance and technology, will continue to create and expand opportunities for bilateral and multilateral cooperation. To contribute to the rapid restoration of the socio-economic situation for Cambodia and the United States, as well as ASEAN and the world as a whole.
The Prince also expressed his pleasure in discussing various issues at the current meeting to seek opportunities as well as solutions to challenges to support the restoration of the economic and social situation in the context of normal living. New trajectory and after the end of Kovid-19, as well as support for Cambodia in its role as chair of ASEAN in 2022.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also informed the delegation of the US-ASEAN Business Council about the current situation and general situation related to security, public order and social security, which is part of the main work under the responsibility of the Ministry of Interior. It is also an important core task that supports and fundamentally ensures the development of all sectors of society.
He pointed out that in the first nine months of 2021 compared to 2020, the general security and public order situation in Cambodia has improved, with all kinds of criminal offenses decreased by 9% while the management of law and order. The results were significant, with the accident rate reduced by 22 percent and the fire accident rate by 42 percent.
At the same time, the Royal Government also plans to issue the first $ 300 million in public securities. This is according to the draft law on finance for management in 2022, which was received by Fresh News on October 22, 2021.
The issuance of state securities and development partner loans has been made clear by the Royal Government that it will not create a debt burden for Cambodia, as Cambodia's public debt situation is still assessed as "sustainable" and "low risk".
The draft Financial Law for Management 2022, which was approved by the Cabinet on October 22, 2021, states that the initial public offering of $ 300 million to finance public investment projects to promote Economic growth and productivity include economic recovery projects to live with Kovid 19 in the new normal trajectory, and digital technology and infrastructure projects.
The government has stated that "the initial public offering of securities and loans of this size will not create a debt burden on Cambodia, that is, technically, the state of Cambodia's public debt is still assessed as" sustainable. " And "low risk", with all of Cambodia's key debt indicators below the benchmark ratio.
