(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed his opinion that the printing of photos with the autographs of King Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kong will stand on the same car 30 years ago. 30,000 riel banknotes are the right thing to do and should not be placed on the back, but on the front.
Dr. Sok Touch highlighted this at the Roundtable on "30th Anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords" organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia this morning, October 22, 2021. The forum discussed much about the Paris Peace Agreement on October 23.
On that occasion, Dr. Sok Touch also expressed his views on the printing of photographs of the relics of His Majesty the King and Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the new banknote. Mr. Sok Touch raised three aspects to show that the printing of pictures of this historic event on the banknote is correct.
The first aspect is the first round of talks in 1987 in France, when Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen met as Cambodians and sat on the same seat. Did not meet as King or as a representative of the Government of the State of Cambodia.
The second aspect is that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the person who mediated and negotiated to end the war, and the third aspect is that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the one who restored the royal power to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk after his disappearance in 1970.
Please note that on October 18, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to put in circulation 30,000 Riel banknotes. This banknote was printed to celebrate the 30th anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords and the 30th anniversary of the return of King Norodom Sihanouk to Cambodia on November 14, 1991.
The pamphlet highlighted the portrait of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk in the foreground, and in the background placed a portrait of the portrait of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen Kong and stood in a car together when Samdech Norodom Sihanouk re-entered the country. November 14, 1991
On the way back to the country, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen went to parade His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Mey directly from Beijing to Phnom Penh. Separately, by car from Pochentong Airport to the Royal Palace, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was in the car with Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, while Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen was driving with Samdech Mey.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen told Lim Chea Vutha, Director General of Fresh News, that on the day of his entry into Cambodia, Samdech was like a brave bodyguard, always wearing a bulletproof vest and standing bravely beside him while doing so. Travel from the airport to the Royal Palace. Samdech Techo further stated that at that time, if anything happened to him, he would hug him to protect the bullets.
