Deputy Governor of Kratie Province Inaugurates a New School Building in Chhlong District Donated by ChalFan Cambodia
(Kratie): Mr. Phim Phea, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, on October 22, 2021, inaugurated a new primary school building at Veal Kanseng Primary School, a donation from ChalFan Cambodia. Located in Kampong Damrey Commune, Chhlong District, Kratie Province.
Mr. Phim Pheara stated that the project was being implemented by a local partner organization, the Cambodian Association for Rural Development (KAFDOC), to ensure that all children receive quality education through Use modern technology, reform teaching and learning methods, and strengthen the involvement of relevant communities.
In addition to two new school buildings, the project has built seven separate modern library buildings, seven latrines, two water wells, drilled two solar wells, upgraded classrooms into five libraries, and set up three computer labs. 48 desktop computers and more than 23,000 reading books, 17 laptops, 119 reading and math study materials and 294 tablets with Khmer reading software installed.
He urged parents to get their children vaccinated so that their children can come to school and become human resources for nation-building and poverty reduction.
Prasan Verma, Country Director of ChalFan Cambodia, and Roh Sun-joon, Country Director of the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KICA), also said that the project was designed to ensure that children in remote areas can access the Internet. Get the same quality education as urban children.
The project initiates modern methods and technologies, including helping children learn better through older students, teaching younger students, using information technology in teaching and learning, using tablets to monitor and evaluate student learning outcomes, and using programs. On tablets to attract children to study, etc., and the development of human resources is a priority for (Kayaka) in Cambodia.
