(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia expects that the Cambodian economy in 2022 will grow by 4.8% in 2022, which will bring the gross domestic product (GDP) to reach 30,544 million dollars. This is according to the summary of the draft law on finance for management 2022, published by the Ministry of Economy and Finance on October 22, 2021.
The draft law on finance for management in 2022 has been fully approved by the Council of Ministers.
As for the forecast for Cambodia's economic growth at 4.8 percent due to the continued growth of key economic sectors such as:
The livestock sub-sector is expected to continue to grow strongly due to the continued increase in pig production, coupled with the government's intervention measures and the implementation of projects of development partners.
Annual average inflation is projected at a manageable level of 2.8% in 2022 due to the expectation of a return to normal food prices. The riel exchange rate is estimated to remain stable at around 4,065 riel per US dollar in 2022 due to the increasing use of the riel.
Although the economy in 2022 is expected to recover at 4.8 percent, Cambodia still faces a number of challenges and risks, both domestic and foreign, that will affect economic growth and hamper development. Overall.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Commissioner Warns of Legal Action Against Border Police Officers Related to Transnational Crime and Drug Offenses
(Banteay Meanchey): Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sithi Loh has warned to take specific legal action against any police officer standing along the Cambodian-Thai border who is involved in the crime of smuggling people to Thailand. Illegal or related to drug trafficking and other crimes that damage the reputation of the force.
Such a warning by Major General Sithi Loh was made on October 21, 2021, yesterday, when he inspected the situation along the Cambodian-Thai border and held a meeting to strengthen the daily work of the police. Border guards at the 807th Border Guard Police Headquarters, Boeung Trakoun checkpoint, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
At the same time, Major General Sithi Loh also urged all brigade commanders to have internal unity, strengthen the cooperation force with the relevant authorities and the Thai side to facilitate the work. All forces must work together to prevent cross-border crimes, especially transnational human trafficking (migrant workers, brokers), economic crimes (tax evasion and right-hand drive vehicles) and drug trafficking.
In addition, the General Commissioner also issued an order for all border police forces to pay attention to strengthen the work efficiency, be ready 24 hours a day, build shelters for military equipment, control ammunition / weapons, grow crops, raise fish, raise animals to Support daily feeding to improve the lives of border police.
