China Strongly Condemns and Rejects EU Report on Relations with Taiwan
BEIJING: China strongly condemns and strongly rejects the so-called report on political relations and cooperation between the European Union (EU) and Taiwan and urges the European Parliament to immediately stop its words and actions. Which undermines China's sovereignty and territorial integrity. This is according to a release by Xinhua on Thursday, October 21, 2021.
Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin made the remarks at a daily press conference on the adoption of the so-called report on political relations and cooperation between the EU and Taiwan, approved by the European Parliament.
Wang stressed that there is only one China in the world and that Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory. The one-China principle is the international consensus and political basis of China's diplomatic relations with the European Union.
He added that the report, approved by the European Parliament, was a serious violation of the basic norms of international relations, the one-China principle and the EU's commitment to Taiwan.
