This morning, the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a roundtable discussion on the "30th anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords".
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, October 22, 2021, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will hold a roundtable discussion on "30th Anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords" with colorful speakers to discuss the events and achievements of the agreement. This one.
Speakers at the discussion included: Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Ms. Chak Sopheap, Executive Director of the Cambodian Center for Human Rights, Mr. Ou Chanrath, Founder of the Reform Party of Cambodia, Dr. Meas Ny, Social Development Analyst and Monitoring; and Mr. Yang Saing Koma, Chairman of the Local Democratic Party Executive Committee.
On October 23, 2021, the agreement on a common political solution to the Cambodian conflict, commonly known as the "Paris Peace Agreement", will be 30 years old. For the past 30 years, Cambodia has gone through countless disciplines and difficulties, large and small, to achieve complete peace and development as it is today.
Thirty years after the Paris Peace Accords, Cambodians of all political and social backgrounds are hopeful and have seen peace and national reconstruction with pride, beginning with the goodwill and mature leadership of the class. Lead the country and all relevant political parties.
Political stability and sustainable national development are indispensable for Cambodia's own will, sense of responsibility and shared commitment to the cause of peace and national unity. At the same time, the international community has a worthy contribution to the process, especially the Paris Peace Accords.
Achievements after the Paris Peace Accords are responding positively to the current evolution of the concept of a world culture of peace and the goal of sustainable development based on universal values of respect for the right to life, freedom and justice. Solidarity, mutual tolerance, human rights, brotherhood, equality and the improvement of people's lives.
The Paris Peace Accords still have moral values and an important historical and political legacy, but they cannot be used as a tool to draw the international community into the internal affairs of a sovereign state, Cambodia. Internal issues of Cambodia must be resolved by Cambodia under Cambodian internal law. The international community cannot use the pretext of human rights and democracy to violate a sovereign state.
Even so, the Paris Peace Accords remain the subject and political agenda, which is hotly debated almost every year. Especially when the internal political situation is not good and every anniversary of this agreement among some Cambodian politicians and some foreigners.
Dr. Kin Phea said that the roundtable discussion organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia was aimed at reviving the spirit of national reconciliation. In particular, the process of peace and full national unification in all aspects through the win-win policy of Prime Minister Hun Sen looks at the achievements of Cambodia in the 30 years after the agreement and the location where Cambodia is and consider The future and vision for Cambodia.
At the same time, this roundtable will serve as a venue for the expression of views for the nation from all social and political trends in the context of Cambodia's pluralistic society.
