(Prey Veng): The Cambodian Red Cross branch in Prey Veng province on October 21, 2021, launched an education campaign, sprayed mosquito repellent and sprayed abattoirs on people in their backyards in four communes: Kampong Leav, Baray, Navy, Takor in Prey Veng City, Prey Veng Province to prevent dengue fever and chickenpox.
The process of this campaign took place for two days on October 21-22, 2021, which was attended by Mr. Sok Pheng, Permanent Vice President of the Prey Veng Branch Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, the Department of Health and other working groups of the Cambodian Red Cross. .
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Pheng said that in Prey Veng province, every rainy season, the Cambodian Red Cross branch as well as the provincial health department always cooperate to educate people about various diseases, especially dengue fever and chickenpox. Causing serious health hazards leading to loss of life.
Mr. Sok Pheng said that although this year there were very few cases of dengue fever and chicken fever in Prey Veng province, but the team continued to work hard like rain without stopping under the encouragement and guidance of Samdech Honorary Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who advised the branch to continue to pay attention to the well-being of the people, especially during the rainy season, which may cause dengue fever and chickenpox.
According to Dr. Chim Hao, Deputy Director of Health of Prey Veng Province, as of the first nine months of 2021, there were no cases of dengue fever, but there were 10 cases of chickenpox.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Health has encouraged people to participate in eliminating the tiger mosquito sanctuary around his home in his village, this is the key to help prevent the spread of dengue fever.
Transmission of dengue fever or chikungunya depends on the dengue transmission agent, tiger mosquitoes, which transmit dengue fever. . Experts expect easing of stimulus for foreign investors and travelers to help real estate recover
(Phnom Penh): Real estate experts in Cambodia applauded and expressed their optimism about the real estate sector after the Royal Government decided to ease restrictions on foreign investors and travelers who have fully vaccinated into Cambodia.
Experts say the decision will boost the real estate sector after a two-year slump due to Kovid 19.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to reduce the number of vaccinations for foreign investors who have been fully vaccinated against Kovid 19 to three days and for foreign travelers to Cambodia for seven days.
Chrek Soknim, president of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Appraisers, said: "This is a good sign for the recovery of the real estate sector in Cambodia when the Royal Government decides to try to open the way for foreigners to travel to the country. "Cambodia is an opportunity for travelers to reconsider investing in real estate in Cambodia and look for more investment opportunities in the near future."
He said that not only is it a good sign for the real estate sector, but also a positive sign for the condominium sector, the condominium sector will start to recover a bit because the condominium sector is a sector to serve foreigners, so when foreigners come to buy condominiums Will start next.
Mr. Chrek Soknim stated that China is the first investor to come to Cambodia and invest in real estate because most of the real estate projects in Cambodia are mostly Chinese, so the entry of the project owner will bring more investors. More.
