(Preah Vihear): Many people representing the people living in the economic village, Chhean Mok commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province, gathered this morning, October 21, 2021, in Tbeng Meanchey district hall to meet with the district governor. And asked for their fingerprints to be returned after they were stamped by a villager to make a plot of land for their house, but instead used to build a temple.
She said that they agreed to give a thumbs up to the village members because she was a friend in the village, so they did not ask for a clear debate. But they came here just to ask for the fingerprints from the district governor to take back, because they are afraid they will use their fingerprints to do things they do not know.
As for Mr. Ton Hom, the second deputy head of Chhean Mok commune, he said that he received this document from the Tbeng Meanchey district governor and he also gave it to the villagers to give to the villagers to give a thumbprint to build the temple, not to make a plot of land. .
On the other hand, Mr. Nuth Sophoan, Tbeng Meanchey District Governor, could not be reached for comment this afternoon by phone call but no one answered. However, the district governor confirmed to reporters yesterday morning that the case for the villagers to give a thumbprint is not to build a temple, but to clearly demarcate his land to avoid future land changes.
