Chey Sambo Handicraft Exports 30 Tons of Cashew Nuts to Japan and Plans to Expand Export Market with Lack of Capital
(Kampong Thom): Seeing the demand for cashew nuts in the international market, Chey Sambo Handicraft in Kampong Thom province of Ms. In Lay Huot, which is currently processing cashew nuts for export to Japan, plans to expand production and export market more than before.
In Lay Huot, owner of Chey Sambo handicraft, told Fresh News that in 2022, she plans to collect 1,000 tons of mango seeds from farmers for processing and export to the international market. But now her craft is facing a lack of additional capital to expand production.
She called on banks to facilitate lending to women entrepreneurs, as well as provide low interest rates and long-term repayments.
Chey Sambo Handicraft was established in 2019 by collecting cashew nuts from 100 families growing on more than 700 hectares in Kampong Thom province. This handicraft created by this Cambodian woman has the ability to process 10 tons of cashew nuts per month.
Chey Sambo Handicraft exported more than 7 tons of cashew nuts for the first time to Japan in early June 2021. So far, she has exported three cashew nuts, about 30 tons.
In Lay Huot said that in addition to the Japanese market, she plans to expand exports to three other markets, including the United States and Australia. In addition to the international market, Chey Sambo Handicraft also supplies local markets such as the Sambor Prei Kuk tourist site and the Khmer Organic Cooperative. National University of Management, Kovid 19 test, management team and faculty to reopen school (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): The National University of Management (NUM) on October 21, 2021 tested 19 Kovid virus to the management and faculty as well as its staff to reopen the first step school with the permission of The Royal Government of Cambodia, from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, after the university is ready.
Testing for Kovid 19 for management and faculty as well as staff of the National University of Management is part of the Ministry of Education's 11-point guideline dated 27 September 2021 on reopening higher education institutions. Public and private. According to Dr. Hor Peng, Rector of the National University of Management, the first step is to open 10 classes at his school, with five morning shifts and five afternoon shifts.
Dr. Hor Peng added, "If the first phase of the test is successful within two weeks, the university will look into the possibility of opening more classes."
The Royal Government of Cambodia's decision to reopen higher education has also shown strong support from higher education experts. Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, said that there are 128 higher education institutions nationwide, of which 48 are public and 80 are private, located in 20 provinces and the capital.
