Comment: China has gone through great hardships, both nationally and internationally, and has never changed its original intentions for the past 50 years: Commemorating the 50th anniversary of the reorganization of China's new legal seat at the United Nations Nation
BEIJING, Oct. 25 (Xinhua) - The time of October 25, 1971, local time at the United Nations Headquarters in New York, was a turning point in the history of new Chinese diplomacy. The 26th United Nations General Assembly adopted a majority vote in Resolution 2758 on the reorganization of all legal rights of the People's Republic of China at the United Nations.
China has gone through great hardships, both nationally and internationally, and has not changed its original intentions for the past 50 years. As the world's largest developing country and a permanent member of the UN Security Council, China has always adhered to the objectives and principles of the UN Charter and has widely disseminated The spirit and philosophy of multilateralism.
At a new starting point in its history, China will continue to raise the banner of multilateralism, continue to support the work of multilateral mechanisms that put the United Nations at the core through practice, as well as push multilateralism to start a new process and push for co-operation. Nations to play a bigger role in the new historical process to promote the formation of a common destiny of mankind.
