There are bars and massage parlors operating in Takhmao City and some other districts in Kandal Province that are in violation of the authorities' ban
(Kandal): Drinks and massage parlors in Takhmao City and other districts in Kandal Province have been operating, increasing the high risk of transmission of Kovid 19 virus in violation of the provincial authorities' ban.
According to the report, on the night of October 19, 2021, the bars and massage parlors opened normally under the guise of pretending to sell only plain food, but secretly selling alcohol and sex massage in violation of the ban. Of the Royal Government.
Some bars secretly hide guests in closed rooms, which is a high risk of contracting Kovid 19 virus.
The source also claimed that during the cover-up, they only deceived the outsiders, but in fact, the shop owner embedded the sale of alcohol, placing female escorts nearby, contrary to the royal "3 do not and 3 protect" measures. The government and some get together happily drinking alcohol.
This has led to criticism from residents who are afraid of transmitting the Kovid 19 virus, calling it a violation of the Kandal provincial governor's ban.
However, Kruy Malen, director of the Kandal provincial administration, confirmed to Fresh News that the provincial administration would take action on the case and continue to call on the public to adhere to good health rules to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 virus.
