Men Sopheak, President of the Cambodian Rubber Developers Association and President of Sopheak Nika Investment Company, which grows and exports rubber, told Fresh News on October 20 that rubber exports to Vietnam for 2021 are still good. Improved by increasing both quantity and price.
He said that Vietnam is a big market for Cambodian rubber, as the country dares to buy rubber from Cambodia at high prices and large quantities.
He also said that for his own rubber exports increased by about 10%. However, he said that during this year's Kovid outbreak this year, exports to Vietnam faced few challenges related to handover due to restrictions on the parties and lack of transportation due to the low number of ships that brought To have a delay in the delivery of goods.
Trade between Cambodia and Vietnam increased by 90.9% year on year, while in the first nine months of this year, the trade volume between the two countries was about 7.2 billion US dollars. .
According to a report by the Ministry of Agriculture, Cambodia's agricultural products have entered 90 global markets, with Cambodia's neighbors Vietnam and Thailand being potential markets for Cambodia's agricultural products.
Aso volcano, a tourist attraction on the southern Japanese island of Kyushu, sent ash and smoke up to 3.5 km above the sky when it erupted at around 12 noon in Tokyo. . The Japan Meteorological Agency has raised the alert level for the volcano to three, while the highest level is five.
It should be noted that Aso volcano had a mild eruption in 2019. In 2014, Japan experienced one of the worst volcanic eruptions in nearly 90 years, killing 63 people on Mount Ontaki in September.
Royal Government officially announces the implementation of Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035
(Phnom Penh): After being officially approved by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on March 30, 2021, only on October 20, 2021, "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021 - 2035 "was officially announced by the Royal Government under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, representing Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that this master plan is an important strategic document that reflects the long-term vision of tourism development in Siem Reap and surrounding areas, as well as serving the development of Siem Reap as a whole.
Meanwhile, the strategic objectives that will be set out by the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035 are three that complement each other: 1: High quality tourism. 2. Smart tourism. Development and conservation of cultural resources and the natural environment.
According to Minister Thong Khon, the master plan is organized into three chapters, with an introduction, conclusion and annexes.
Chapter 2: The Master Plan sets out the Siem Reap Tourism Development Strategy, divided into 6 sections, including:
Part 3: There are two strategies to promote and attract tourists, including: 1. Attracting important international tourism market sources and promoting the local tourism movement to Siem Reap. 2. Promoting tourism in all forms and by all means.
Section 4: There are three strategies to enhance the quality and sustainability of tourism development, including: 1. Improving the quality of tourism, including improving the quality of services in the tourism industry, strengthening Siem Reap as a safe and healthy tourism destination. Resilience to disasters, crises, infectious diseases and crises. 2. Human resource development in tourism. 3. Promoting local economy through tourism development.
Section 5: There are three strategies for environmental management, including: 1. Waste and solid waste management. 2. Promoting green areas. 3. Protecting natural ecosystems.
Section 6: Infrastructure development and strengthening strategies to support tourism, including: 1. Promoting domestic and international connectivity, such as strengthening land, air, water and rail connectivity. Improving the infrastructure to support tourism as much as possible, including the development of infrastructure, clean water, electricity, roads connecting tourist destinations, and telecommunication and internet services to serve the tourism sector in Siem Reap.
Overall, the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035, prepared by the harmonization of all relevant sectors, accompanied by a comprehensive monitoring and evaluation mechanism for all tourism development activities, is an important tool as a road map. To lead the public, private, people and development partners to participate in socio-economic development.
In order to promote the implementation of the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035 to achieve success, efficiency and effectiveness, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth made some recommendations for implementation from the end of 2021 to 2023 as follows:
Second, request all stakeholders to adhere to the spirit of ownership, common thinking and joint responsibility in implementing the action plan of this master plan in accordance with the strategic goals and strategic measures set out, especially the implementation activities in the short term. And medium.
Third, all must participate in the strict implementation of standard operating procedures, tourism safety rules and guidelines, including health measures, administrative measures, legal measures and educational measures issued by the Royal Government and relevant ministries and institutions.
Fourth, the relevant ministries and institutions and provincial authorities must jointly strengthen the properties of Siem Reap in attracting domestic and international tourists through:
* Accelerating the completion of 38 road improvement projects in Siem Reap city, along with the addition of sidewalks for cars, roads for motorbikes, roads for bicycles, poles and public lighting, as well as for the official side of the road, to speed up the development of Chong Khneas Port. According to the standard of the tourist port, taking into account the fitness to support new tourism services and products.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister also called on all ministries-institutions, authorities at all levels, sub-national administrations, the private sector, the people and tourists, as well as all stakeholders to actively and responsibly participate in the implementation of the master plan. Successful tourism development in Siem Reap 2021-2035 to contribute to the restoration of the future of Cambodia's tourism sector towards the prosperity of "Cambodia: the Kingdom of Wonder".
Kampong Thom Provincial Administration Continues to Suspend the Sale of All Kinds of Alcohol and Business Activities, Karaoke Club, Bar, Disco, Beer Garden and Massage for another 2 weeks
(Kampong Thom): The Kampong Thom Provincial Administration has issued a decision to temporarily suspend the sale of all types of alcohol, gatherings for drinking and business activities, karaoke clubs, bars, discos, beer gardens and massages for another two weeks from the 20th. October to November 2, 2021 to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in the province. This is according to the decision received by Fresh News.
The provincial administration has stated that "temporary administrative measures must be implemented to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Kampong Thom province, which will last for two (2) weeks from October 20, 2021 to October 2. November 2021. "
The provincial administration has said it will temporarily suspend the sale of all types of alcohol in markets, restaurants, cafes, cafes, cafes, beverages, food and beverage businesses and all alcohol distribution depots.
In addition, there should be a temporary suspension of gatherings or gatherings of all kinds of alcohol and gatherings or gatherings of singing or dancing.
