Spokesperson of the Ministry of Information: The report issued by Cambodia is a dishonest report and intentionally accuses the authorities.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Information made the remarks after the Cambodian Journalists' Association (CamboJA) released a report alleging that the Ministry of Information allowed authorities to accuse journalists of disrupting their work.
At the same time, Cambodia claims that local officials at various locations have used the Ministry of Information's notices to justify the expulsion of journalists who try to cover land disputes or evictions, including threatening to take action. The law, if the journalist fails to leave, and in some cases there are criminal charges.
Regarding this report, the spokesman of the Ministry of Information, Mr. Meas Sophorn clarified as follows:
1: The report issued by Cambodia is a report that is not honest and intentionally accuses the competent institutions that are performing their roles and responsibilities in accordance with the law in force.
2: This report also does not study thoroughly the legal documents issued by the Ministry of Information in the past, and this association always opposes all decisions of public institutions and never accepts confirmation or explanation. Interpretation of public institutions: or competent institutions from time to time.
3. This association always issues reports or statements accusing the competent institutions that perform their duties according to the law that the competent institutions violate the rights and freedoms of journalists or threaten to suppress the rights of journalists.
4: Recording the case of journalists who are legally responsible for what they have done as a violation of the right to freedom of expression is a record that does not fully reflect and is accurate at all. According to the facts and legal facts of each case. At this point, it can be said that this report is intended to mislead the public about the law enforcement of the authorities.
