(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ken Sambath, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on October 19, 2021, explained about the tax exemption for associations and non-governmental organizations, stating that the tax exemption was Provided through income.
In the program "Tax of Cambodia" on the tax obligations of organizations - Associations online this morning, October 19, 2021, Mr. Ken Sambath stated that "Incentives for associations and non-governmental organizations must be provided. "Income tax exemption period."
Mr. Ken Sambath explained that the income that is exempted from the income of any association in the event that the income of that association is not used for the personal benefit or of the shareholders or individuals.
As for the NGO, he said that the income of any NGO that is organized for the purpose of religion, charity, science, literature, education, and there is no share of property or income used. For private gain.
Mr. Ken Sambath said that the tax-exempt income includes: funds or legal gifts from individuals, legal entities, resources and assets of the NGO, or any other source of income except income. Which conducts separate business activities.
Emphasize that associations or non-governmental organizations that have separate activities and are not in their purely targeted are considered separate business activities that must be registered and taxed in accordance with applicable tax laws and regulations.
Associations and non-governmental organizations that have separate business activities must:
1. Distinguish between capital, assets, assets, assets, employees, managers and other financial information to serve associations or non-governmental organizations and to serve specific business activities.
2. Implement the rules and principles of ordinary accounting in accordance with Prakas No. 1820 MEF.PrK dated 25 December 2015 on the determination of rules and procedures for the implementation of ordinary accounting for small taxpayers.
3. Implement accounting rules in accordance with the international accounting standards of Cambodia in accordance with the provisions on income tax for intermediate or large taxpayers. The Ministry of National Defense vaccinated 19 Kovid 19 soldiers, military families and citizens for the first time 2,759,844 people, the second time 2,732,380 people and the boost dose of 679,934 people
