(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, the new Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, in front of the traders in Banlung Market, promising to solve all the problems that have occurred and for the traders to contact him personally to find a solution.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun made this promise on October 19, 2021, on the occasion of leading professional officers of relevant units, Banlung Municipality and Laban Siek Sangkat authorities to meet and discuss some issues. To solve the problem of the people, the group of traders in Banlung market.
During the meeting with the traders, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun also inquired about some challenges between the traders and the investment company of Banlung Market. The traders insisted that the provincial authorities help solve some problems, such as their narrow stalls. The market investment company has dismantled and built a new stall, promising that when it is built and handed over to the original owner to sell in the same stall location without a lottery.
In addition, the vendors said that the owners of Banlung Market Investment Company could not allow the vendors to sell the old place because the construction of new stalls was done according to the standard and some old stalls disappeared because the construction team went straight to the road. Corner of the street (entrance-exit) so the old stall owners can lose their place to get justice together, traders must draw lots.
In addition, in order to find a solution for all the business people, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun advised the business people to choose their representatives to meet at his office later.
He promised to improve the hygiene and cleanliness in Banlung Market to make it easier for customers to go out and buy food and other groceries to increase revenue.
At the same time, the provincial governor also announced the good news that the Royal Government will reopen the economy throughout the country, which provides good opportunities for all business people. In order to show his sympathy on behalf of the provincial leadership, he also brought some money to the grandmother, who was old but could sit and shop in Banlung Market.
The printing and circulation of 30,000 riel banknotes, a new model in this market, has been cited by financial experts as not affecting inflation or depreciating the riel.
Dr. Mey Kalyan, Economic Specialist and Senior Advisor to the Supreme National Economic Council, said that the introduction of the new 30,000 Riel banknote will not affect the economy or the value of the riel. To celebrate and commemorate the 30th anniversary of the Paris Peace Accords.
Oknha Huot Ieng Tong, President and CEO of Hatta Bank, said that despite the new currency circulating in the current market, it will not cause inflation because the National Bank of Cambodia has carefully considered before printing and placing Let the circulation of 30,000 riel banknotes, along with the introduction of some strategies to maintain the stability of the riel banknote.
He added that the dollar auction that the National Bank has done in the past is also a strategy to stabilize the riel. He said that despite the spread of Kovid 19, the current use of the riel is increasing, which makes the riel more valuable. Hatta Bank also contributes to the promotion of the use of the riel by providing loans in riel more than 10% and keeping the riel in excess of the amount set by the National Bank.
Please be informed that in order to maintain the stability of the riel against the US dollar, as well as to stimulate economic activity during the Kovid 19 outbreak, the National Bank of Cambodia has launched a series of dollar auctions. In September, the National Bank of Cambodia put up for auction more than $ 100 million, and this October, $ 200 million. The intervention of the National Bank has stabilized the exchange rate at around 4,100 riel per dollar.
