Road 70B badly damaged by sand truck, authorities warn to close business at that location
(Kandal): Drivers of sand-trucks from the excavation sites and large sand depots continue to illegally transport on Road 70B from Arey Ksat ferry port to Khsach Kandal district without fear of the law. Causing sand and soil to fall on the road and damaging many roads.
In this regard, Mr. Nop Dara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, warned for the last time to all business owners and drivers, if they continue to disobey the law when they are caught, they will confiscate the car and close the business place without any problem. No more exceptions.
Mr. Nop Dara warned on October 18, 2021, on the occasion of the representative of Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, to hold a meeting with the business owners of sand, stone and stone depots and the owners of sand and stone trucks and representatives of the owners of the Borey. Land-sand in Khsach Kandal and Lvea Em districts in Svay Chrum commune hall.
Mr. Nop Dara added that the Governor of Kandal Province always takes care of the well-being of all people throughout Kandal Province. The people affected by the sand truck and the owner of the depot caused difficulties, he ordered lower-level officials to come down and solve it immediately.
Mr. Nop Dara also instructed all business owners to transport sand and sand to check the transportation must be legal, respect the contract, while the business owner must have a valid license, comply with the law and the contract to listen to the instructions. Of the authorities. If it is seen that they do not listen and do not follow the principles, the authorities will follow the law.
In addition, he also asked the competent force to identify the driver of the sand truck in accordance with the law, to have a driver's license and to check for drugs. For those trucks, if they do not follow the instructions, the authorities and professional officers must cooperate to seize the trucks and fine them according to the law.
