While genes have a major influence on sex, the environment plays an important role for the sexes of some species. Researchers are beginning to notice that the unusual trend among frogs living in polluted lakes is that many male frogs have changed their sex to females. Studies show that these toxins restrict the production of sex hormones in male frogs and in turn increase female sex hormones.
