(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, National Gendarmerie and Prey Veng Provincial Gendarmerie together took only two days to break up a case of premeditated murder: a friend stabbed a friend to death Reaching the capture of the killer.
The operation was led by Brigadier General Sam Tola, Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, under the coordination of the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor and the Prey Veng Provincial Prosecutor, under the direct supervision of Mr. Touch. Inan, Deputy Commander, received expertise and carried out research on all relevant targets by Mr. Soeur Panha, Director of the Provincial Gendarmerie Crime Research and Suppression Department.
A report by the Kandal Provincial Armed Forces, released by Fresh News on the morning of October 19, 2021, shows that this premeditated murder occurred on the night of October 13, 2021 at the intersection of Street 261 in Ampil Teuk village. Sambour Meas commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, after receiving information from residents, found the body of a man on the morning of October 14, 2021.
Immediately after receiving the information, the provincial and district specialized forces inspected the bodies at the scene, looking for evidence based on the technical experience of the experts. The body of the victim was Nguyen Dang Chung, a 40-year-old Vietnamese man (with a residence permit), a construction contractor. Currently living in a rented house in Sangkat Steung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
In front of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, the suspect, Sreng Tay, confessed that on the day of the incident, the victim called him to see the construction work in Phnom Penh. At noon, the suspect took a taxi from A house in Prey Veng province around Chbar Ampov market with a sharp knife and a yellow plastic stick in his pants pocket in order to stab the victim because he had lied many times, wasting time and money many times .
After dropping off the motorcycle, he went to attend the funeral of the victim, who was a friend living in the same village the next day (acting normally so as not to be suspected) but was arrested by the military police. Coordinated the procedure from the Prosecutor of Kandal and Prey Veng Provincial Courts.
Once again, the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with the Prey Veng Provincial Gendarmerie, brought the suspect to the location where he dropped the motorcycle into the pond (findings) and handed it over to the victim's family. There, and continue to search for knives and other artifacts near the scene, but did not find without remembering the exact point, there is a lot of weeds and the day of the rain.
Currently, the suspects and exhibits of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie have built a case to be sent to the Kandal Provincial Court and sent to the provincial prison. The Royal Government of Cambodia selects the Shenzhen Institute of Urban Planning and Design to develop the Sihanoukville Development Master Plan into a Multi-Purpose Special Economic Zone
The development of a master plan for the development of Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model special economic zone is part of the Royal Government of Cambodia's medium- and long-term strategic considerations to promote sustainable and environmental development in line with development policies. Cambodia Industrial Sector 2015-2025, to achieve the vision of Cambodia to become a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Cambodia's main economic pole, Sihanoukville is a highly developed area due to its geographical location by the sea, deep-sea ports, airports and many tourist beaches.
In fact, in recent years, Sihanoukville has changed dramatically, turning from a quiet province with a busy and vibrant economic activity in tourism and industry, especially in rural areas. Mainly link domestic production and trade to countries in the region.
Taking into account these potentials, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out its vision to turn the province into a multi-purpose model economic zone and an important economic pole in attracting and absorbing foreign investment that could lead to " A new locomotive for promoting national economic growth.
The master plan will also be a roadmap for facilitating the implementation of all activities between stakeholders, including the public, private and development partners, based on common goals and clear responsibilities through setting directions for mobilization, attraction and mobilization. Resources, business activities and investments to achieve the long-term vision of the Royal Government.
The selection of UPDIS Institute for the master plan for the development of Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model special economic zone is due to the fact that the institute has more than 30 years of experience and has organized about 5,800 projects around the world, especially as a leading institution in Development of Shenzhen city development plan.
UPDIS will use this experience to develop a master plan for the development of Sihanoukville into a high-quality multi-purpose special economic zone that reflects Cambodia's vision and development direction and can be implemented in accordance with the political context. Cambodian economy and society.
