Takeo Provincial Police is searching for the perpetrators of the case of violence at a cockfight in the middle of a quiet forest in Bati district to be punished according to the law
(Takeo): The Quick Reaction Team of Takeo Provincial Police on October 18, 2021 issued a statement regarding the case of violence between a group of cockfighters and a group of journalists in Tbeng village, Kraing Thnong commune, Bati district, Takeo province. Posted on October 16, 2021.
Takeo Provincial Police confirmed that on October 16, 2021 at 14:30 pm, a violent incident occurred in Tbeng village, Kraing Thnong commune, Bati district, Takeo province, caused by a group of unidentified suspects. Who went to hide the cock in the forest west of Tbeng village, far from the town which borders Chamlong village, Tbeng commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province.
The above case injured two journalists: the first named Set Lot, male, 39 years old, living in a rented house in Phum B, Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh and the second named Som Ron, male 37-year-old living in a rented room in Trapeang Thleung III village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, suffered minor injuries.
Immediately after receiving information about the case of cockfighting at the above location, Major General Sok Samnang, Commissioner of Takeo Provincial Police, ordered the Bati District Police Inspectorate and the District Administrative Unity Command led by Bati District Governor to visit. It was not until 17:30 that the Bati District Police Inspectorate received a complaint from the two victims as journalists.
Takeo Provincial Police confirmed that "Currently, the specialized force is building a case and continue to identify the perpetrators to be punished according to law."
Please be reminded that while the police are busy in the campaign to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, not only in Bati district, but also in Takeo province, gangs of addicts and cockfighting gamblers have secretly gathered to bet on each other. Put chickens in remote places away from the town, which is geographically easy to escape when the authorities crack down one by one.
