104 Cambodian workers who cheated brokers were sent back to Cambodia by Thai authorities
(Banteay Meanchey): At least 104 Cambodian workers who cheated their recruiters to find work in Thailand were deported to Cambodia by the Thai authorities on October 19, 2021 through the Khok Song commune. Ta Praya exits through the corridor of Obi Choan, O Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province.
It should be informed that the Thai authorities inspected the Thai-Cambodian border and arrested 104 Cambodians who illegally crossed the border into Thailand at Payu Khaliptan Park in Sa Kaeo Province.
After questioning the authorities, all Cambodians also admitted that they paid each broker from 6,000 baht to 9,000 baht to enter Thailand.
In addition, in the evening of the same day, after being convicted and fined, the Thai authorities will send them back to Cambodia through the Khok Song commune, Ta Praya district through the three-story corridor. Ochrov, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authority would like to appeal to all citizens, please do not cheat brokers, which cost a lot of money, so people, please wait a while, it is not too late because the wrong border. Access to their territory is not guaranteed to be easy, as Thailand is tightening its efforts to curb the spread of Kovid 19, like Cambodia.
