Mr. Ly Chantola: Judicial police do not recognize the rights and role of lawyers is one of the five major challenges
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of Cambodia, on October 18, 2021, stated that some judicial police officers who do not recognize the rights and roles of lawyers are one of the five major challenges.
Addressing the closing ceremony of the 26th Annual General Meeting of the Bar Association under the chairmanship of Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, Mr. Ly Chantola claimed that according to the report of the General Assembly and the leadership of the Bar Association for the past year, the Bar Association Achieved a lot of work and achievements, despite the obstacles caused by Kovid 19.
But at the same time, the Bar Association still sees five challenges and difficulties, including:
1: The performance of the bar is difficult to achieve as planned, especially cooperation with national and international institutions due to the spread of Kovid 19.
2. The performance of some judicial police officers is still problematic because they do not recognize the rights and roles of lawyers. On August 25, 2021, Mr. Ly Chantola decided to set up a working group to research the rights of lawyers at this stage of judicial police officers.
4: Some rights of lawyers are violated. Some of the work of lawyers is done by intermediaries in various institutions such as courts, judicial police units, cadastral departments, the Ministry of Commerce, tax units, etc.
