Chinese astronaut Wang Yaping's training: "As long as male astronauts can do it, I can do it"
Wang Yaping is a female astronaut. He is also known as "the astronaut". Due to this flight mission, she will accomplish many "first" tasks, such as the first female astronaut to enter China's first space station, the longest-serving female astronaut in China, and probably the first female astronaut to leave the room. China's first spacecraft.
Compared to male astronauts, female astronauts are weaker than this, it is true, so during normal training, she made a strict request to herself. While training endurance in a high-speed centrifuge, she suffered from 8G gravity acceleration, making it difficult to breathe.
In rescue training, whether it is a forest with many wildlife or a sea of sand with a storm of sand in the sky or a sea with big waves, she is facing serious tests of harsh environments. When participating in the 300-meter race, she ran three minutes faster than the standard score.
Only after becoming an astronaut did she realize that the life of an astronaut is subject to long and arduous training and repeated challenges. Wang Yaping never thought of giving up on the path of dreaming into space, she competed with herself and overcame herself.
For example, when in space, blood needs to be pumped. In the past, she did not dare at all and just brought beets to practice. Unexpectedly, when the astronauts practiced pumping blood, he bravely tried it first and achieved a good and fast pump. He said that after becoming an astronaut, I found that I did many things that I could not do before, making me feel like I have achieved something incomparable.
The first endurance training was a difficult discipline for Ms. Wang Yaping, she got only second grade points. This training requires a lot of abdominal and back muscle strength, and he is thin and lacks muscle, so he trains more every day to increase cardiovascular function and muscle strength.
By the end of 2011, in this exam, Ms. Wang Yaping got the first level score. In space, when wearing a uniform to go out of the spacecraft, astronauts have to rely on the upper limbs, so for female astronauts who are able to perform tasks outside the spacecraft, what should be done to increase the strength of the upper limbs? The only way is to practice!
The effort always paid off, and Wang Yaping eventually trained her arm muscles. Once, after training, he went to a massage therapist and reminded him that there was bad news, your forearm is bigger than before! But Ms. Wang Yaping reacted differently than a normal woman, she said happily, "Very good!" It shows that I have exercised and my muscles have increased.
To Wang Yaping, being an astronaut is not only a career, but also a job she loves. His love for work gave him constant motivation to keep him going.
This fascinating space class has inspired tens of thousands of children to enjoy science. After that, Ms. Wang Yaping received letters from many students, she also went to some schools to exchange experiences with students. Students' aspirations for space and curiosity about scientific exploration have grown significantly.
Many children who were not yet born when they saw the video clip of Ms. Wang Yaping asked her when to teach in space. This also encouraged her to want to go to space again to bring children to see something new and new.
In contrast to her eight-year mission to space, Wang Yaping has one of her biggest worries, her five-and-a-half-year-old daughter.
However, this little girl is proud of her mother's work. One time after returning from kindergarten, he said to his mother, "Mom is an astronaut, but I know you are also a teacher of space." Her daughter is also very fond of large spaces and often asks her mother to tell her about space.
