(World): Normally the beaches are covered with sand, but in the US state of California there is a special beach that instead of sand is covered with millions of pieces of glass and glass debris.
During the early 20th century, from 1906-1967, three landfills were set up, containing glass and glass waste. Over the decades, pieces of discarded objects have been in contact with the surrounding elements, including rocks, sea, and sand, making them round and smooth and no longer have sharp edges.
