In a meeting with the Korean Chamber of Commerce on Thursday this week, Ms. Chreung Botum Rainsy, Cambodian Ambassador to the Republic of Korea, mentioned the economic potential, favorable conditions and investment opportunities in Cambodia after Cambodia and Korea signed a free trade agreement on This coming October 26th.
Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed to Fresh News on October 16, 2021 that the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement will be signed by Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak. With the Korean side on October 26 online.
The free trade agreement between Cambodia and Korea will be the second free trade agreement after the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China. The agreement will further promote Cambodia's exports to Korea, including garments and textiles, electronics, especially agricultural products.
In the first eight months of 2021, from January to August 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and Korea reached more than 514 million US dollars, an increase of 11.52% compared to the same period in 2020.
Cambodia exported more than $ 129 million worth of goods to Korea, including garments, electronics, footwear, beverages, rubber bags, medicines and cardboard.
Imports from Korea amounted to more than $ 385 million. Cambodia imports most of its goods from Korea: textiles, trucks, beverages, electronics, machinery, home decor, medicines, soaps and plastics.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated that after the signing of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement on October 26, 2021, both parties must meet their respective internal conditions. The agreement shall pass through the Council of Ministers, then to the National Assembly, the Senate, before being signed by the King of Cambodia.
He said that the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement will be launched in 2022 after the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, which was launched in early 2022. Mr. Ly Chantola: 110 Candidates for the 10th Mandate Bar Association
