Doctors carry Kovid 19 vaccine to a 93-year-old woman in Kampong Chhnang province's Boribo district who could not travel to the injection site
(Kampong Chhnang): A 93-year-old woman living in Thlok Chrov village, Anchanh Rong commune, Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, who wanted to be vaccinated with Kovid 19 but could not travel to the place, was vaccinated by doctors with a backpack. This morning, October 16, 2021.
Although she is very old, Ms. Sao Horn expressed her understanding of the importance of the vaccine that helps protect her from serious illness in case of this devastating infection from her family.
Since the announcement of the campaign, she has wanted to get vaccinated, but due to her advanced age, she has not been able to travel to the vaccination site on her own.
Seeing this and following the Commission's guidelines for vaccinating 19 Kovid vaccines across the country, the doctors carried the vaccine to her home. Ms. Sao San has been vaccinated with 19 vaccines against the virus, while the second dose will be given on November 6, 2021.
At the same time, Ms. Sao Horn expressed her deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for giving her the opportunity to be vaccinated now. She also thanked the doctors who brought the vaccine to her home.
Please be informed that in the past, Ms. O Vandin, as the chairperson of the Commission for the vaccination of Kovid 19, the national framework has always advised and reminded all doctors to carry the Kovid 19 vaccine to the people at home. In case they find it difficult to travel to the injection site.
Kandal Provincial Governor Orders Lvea Em and Khsach Kandal District Authorities to Seize Sand Trucks and Close a Sand Depot Immediately After Causing Falling Sand, Dirty Road and Damaged Road
(Kandal): A large sand depot of Pov Soeng, which violated the instructions of the authorities after the owner of the depot used a sand truck, causing the road to fall and damage the roads in Lvea Em and Khsach Kandal districts. Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, ordered the arrest and closed the sand depot temporarily, waiting for a legal solution.
Immediately after the order, on the evening of October 15, 2021, Mr. Kan Sokkay, Governor of Lvea Em District and Mr. Bun Pheng, Governor of Khsach Kandal District, led their respective joint forces to seize 17 sand trucks, temporarily close the sand depot and Summoned a representative of Borey Tuol Sangke, a group of car owners, a representative of Pov Seng's sand depot to educate and set according to legal principles.
The sand depot is located in Svay Chrum commune, Khsach Kandal district, bordering Arey Ksat commune, Lvea Em district, while the sand depot is in Khsach Kandal district, but transported into Lvea Em district, causing damage to roads in both districts.
At the meeting, Lvea Em and Khsach Kandal district governors strongly criticized the representatives of the sand depot owners and all the car groups who did not follow the guidelines of the district authorities, who were repeatedly educated but still abusive.
After receiving orders from the upper echelons of the force, they seized all the cars, stored them, and educated the drivers and depot owners, while some of the principles were set by the authorities as follows:
* First: Suspend business temporarily * Second: Need to prepare, repair and clean the road to be ready and wait for the meeting to decide later.
It should be informed that Pov Soeng's sand depot in Svay Chrum commune, Khsach Kandal district has been criticized by the people every day and for many months due to non-compliance with the law. Tires coming out of the roof of the car smeared all over the road, causing damage to the national road, causing large potholes, and people slipping and falling into the potholes almost every day.
