During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon stressed the importance of maintaining peace and global prosperity, which all countries have worked hard to achieve, including the need for CICA member states to address the challenges posed by Kovid-19. And other challenges such as competition between superpowers, supply chain blockages, and development gaps.
The Deputy Prime Minister called on all CICA member states to strengthen cooperation to enhance CICA's international stance in promoting environmentally sound dialogue and building a spirit of trade and investment facilitation and the implementation of innovative means of communication. Promote cooperation in all areas throughout the region, such as communication through Track 1.5 and Track 2.
