To strengthen the implementation of tax revenue collection, the General Department of Taxation has introduced measures, policies and fiscal administration, including the following key measures:
1: Strengthen the implementation of the obligation to install beer and non-alcoholic beverages of domestic production enterprises, strengthen the management of the collection of taxes and duties of all kinds, especially the special tax revenue on beer and non-alcoholic beverages, which will be implemented from December 1, 2021 onwards
2. Implement effective management of tax revenue for the activities of the supply of digital goods or digital services that conduct e-commerce transactions.
3. Implement the management of revenue collection of property tax and / or unused land tax for 2021, which has been postponed until October 31, 2021.
4: Continue to strengthen the management of tax revenue collection through the information technology system that has been implemented continuously 5: Disseminate and promote the use of online tax services of the General Department of Taxation 6: Strengthen the implementation of tax debt collection, tax debt collection and Measures to tighten tax debt, especially large tax liabilities, identified as priority debt and enterprises in sectors not affected by the Kovid Outbreak 19
7: Continue to strengthen the management of the enterprise, request for temporary suspension or request for reopening, with measures to inspect the location of the enterprise directly, monitor the filing of declarations and strengthen the audit of documents 8: Continue and strive to strengthen the provision of services to those who Taxes are an important factor in improving the tax culture
9. Continuing the work of human resource reform by promoting and striving to strengthen the implementation of labor laws and regulations, and to be gentle but firm, based on the legal aspects of providing services to taxpayers and managing the collection of tax revenue.
Recent achievements in information technology and services for taxpayers of the General Department of Taxation as a precautionary measure in response to the challenges and difficulties in the context of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
