Siem Reap Provincial Administration Holds a Ceremony to Honor the 9th Anniversary of the Death of His Majesty the King
(Siem Reap): On the morning of October 15, 2021, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration held a ceremony to honor the 9th anniversary of the death of King Norodom Sihanouk.
The ceremony paid homage to Smey Smath, lit candles and incense, offered a wreath, dedicated Kosal Bochea, and paid homage to his relics with deep sorrow.
All the leaders of the Armed Forces, as children, grandchildren, great-grandchildren, great-great-grandchildren, expressed their deepest condolences and remembrance of the noble and sublime merits of His Majesty the King. Has left a lot of achievements for the motherland for the descendants of the Cambodian people throughout the country.
This ceremony is also held to pay tribute to His Majesty the King and His precious Brahma Vihara, who throughout his life sacrificed both his body and his intellect in his royal activities for the cause of the nation, territorial integrity, national reconciliation and Development in all fields.
